την εργασία τους   Τι προσφέρουμε Ικανοποιητικό πακέτο αποδοχών Εργασία σε ευχάριστο, δυναμικό και αναπτυσσόμενο επαγγελματικό περιβάλλον Διαμονή (μόνο για θέσεις σε resorts)   Έτοιμη να γίνετε μέρος της κοινότητάς μας;', 'Εποχιακός/ή');
INSERT INTO `kariera` (`id`, `title`, `url`, `location`, `posted`, `scraped`, `company`, `description`, `type`) VALUES
(641826, 'CSR & ESG MANAGER', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/301447', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 9 λεπτά', '2026-03-30 15:02:11', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'CSR & ESG MANAGER About the role Join our prestigious ZEUS Hotels & Resorts Group. We are committed to creating memorable stays for our guests while fostering a supportive and enriching work environment for our team members. As we continue to expand our portfolio, we are seeking a talented and experienced CSR / ESG Manager to join our team. What you will do Develop, execute, manage and evaluate the Group’s holistic CSR & ESG strategy, implementing sustainability KPIs, policies, procedures and initiatives in 17 hotel properties across 9 destinations in Greece & Europe. Evaluate all CSR ad hoc requests (donations, sponsorships, partnerships). Compose the Group’s annual CSR Report. Manage the Group’s annual CSR budget. Foster lasting partnerships with key stakeholders, including public authorities and NGOs. Coordinate the audit processes of sustainability awards and certifications. Provide support to hotels and deliver CSR training to employees. Manage the CSR strategic communication plan and contribute to the implementation of marketing and corporate communication initiatives. Your uniqueness is welcome We are looking for a team spirited, adaptable professional, with strong leadership, communication and organizational skills, thinking outside the box, keen interest to develop new competencies, ability to work and deliver under pressure, who: Holds Bachelor\'s degree in Sustainability, Sustainable Development, Business Administration, Communications, or a related field. A Master’s degree will be considered an asset. Has 3+ years of experience in Sustainability and CSR; experience in the hospitality and tourism industry will be considered an asset. Has in-depth knowledge of ESG (Environmental, Social, and Governance) frameworks, sustainability practices and principles, and reporting requirements. Has proven track record of developing and implementing successful sustainability & CSR projects and reporting. Displays strong project management skills, including the ability to prioritize tasks, manage budgets, and meet deadlines. Has excellent leadership, communication and interpersonal skills to engage stakeholders at all levels and collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams. Possesses strong creative thinking and excellent writing and verbal skills in English & Greek. What we offer Competitive salary Continuous training and professional development Exclusive accommodation benefits across the Zeus network A dynamic, international, and data-driven work environment The opportunity to work with a leading hospitality group Ready to join our Community?', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(641827, 'Cook A\' - Kos', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/301446', 'Ηρακλείδες', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-03-30 15:02:13', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Cook A\' About Us Join the prestigious Zeus Hotels & Resorts Group, renowned for its dedication to luxury hospitality and exceptional guest experiences.We are committed to creating memorable stays for our guests while fostering a supportive and enriching working environment for our team members.As we continue to expand our portfolio, we are seeking a talented Cook A to join our culinary team.   Position Overview We are looking for a skilled and passionate Cook A who will be responsible for preparing and delivering high-quality dishes with precision and creativity.The ideal candidate has a strong work ethic, attention to detail, and thrives in a fast-paced kitchen environment.   What You’ll Do Prepare and cook a variety of dishes (appetizers, main courses, desserts) following established recipes and presentation standards• Ensure high levels of quality, flavor, and consistency• Monitor and manage inventory of ingredients and supplies• Collaborate with the culinary team on menu development and improvements• Maintain cleanliness and organization of kitchen areas• Support the team during busy service periods• Follow all food safety and sanitation regulations• Participate in training and professional development opportunities   Your Uniqueness Is Welcome Cooking is about creativity, discipline, and teamwork.We are looking for individuals who take pride in excellence and continuous improvement. We’re looking for someone who:• Has previous experience as a Cook A or Line Cook• Holds a culinary degree or relevant certification (preferred)• Has strong knowledge of cooking techniques and food presentation• Performs well in fast-paced environments• Pays close attention to detail and quality• Is flexible to work shifts, including evenings, weekends, and holidays• Has strong knowledge of food safety and hygiene standards   What We Offer Competitive salary based on experience• Professional development and career advancement opportunities• Supportive and collaborative work environment• Meals provided during shifts• Employee discounts on hotel accommodation Ready to join our Community?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(641828, 'Cook A\' - Athens', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/301445', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν ένα λεπτό', '2026-03-30 15:02:13', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Cook A\' About Us Join the prestigious Zeus Hotels & Resorts Group, renowned for its dedication to luxury hospitality and exceptional guest experiences.We are committed to creating memorable stays for our guests while fostering a supportive and enriching working environment for our team members.As we continue to expand our portfolio, we are seeking a talented Cook A to join our culinary team.   Position Overview We are looking for a skilled and passionate Cook A who will be responsible for preparing and delivering high-quality dishes with precision and creativity.The ideal candidate has a strong work ethic, attention to detail, and thrives in a fast-paced kitchen environment.   What You’ll Do Prepare and cook a variety of dishes (appetizers, main courses, desserts) following established recipes and presentation standards• Ensure high levels of quality, flavor, and consistency• Monitor and manage inventory of ingredients and supplies• Collaborate with the culinary team on menu development and improvements• Maintain cleanliness and organization of kitchen areas• Support the team during busy service periods• Follow all food safety and sanitation regulations• Participate in training and professional development opportunities   Your Uniqueness Is Welcome Cooking is about creativity, discipline, and teamwork.We are looking for individuals who take pride in excellence and continuous improvement. We’re looking for someone who:• Has previous experience as a Cook A or Line Cook• Holds a culinary degree or relevant certification (preferred)• Has strong knowledge of cooking techniques and food presentation• Performs well in fast-paced environments• Pays close attention to detail and quality• Is flexible to work shifts, including evenings, weekends, and holidays• Has strong knowledge of food safety and hygiene standards   What We Offer• Professional development and career advancement opportunities• Supportive and collaborative work environment• Meals provided during shifts• Employee discounts on hotel accommodation Ready to join our Community?', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(641829, 'Assistant Housekeeping Manager - Eretria', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/301442', 'Ερέτρια', 'πριν μερικά δευτερόλεπτα', '2026-03-30 15:02:15', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Assistant Housekeeping Manager About the role As a Housekeeping Assistant Manager, you’ll be a key pillar in maintaining the standards, rhythm, and daily excellence of our hotel operations. Working closely with the Housekeeping Manager, you will help ensure that every space reflects comfort, cleanliness, and care — the details that shape each guest’s experience. Your role combines organization, leadership, and hands-on involvement. From supporting the team on the floor to ensuring procedures run smoothly behind the scenes, you’ll help transform daily routines into consistently high-quality service. Life Inside the Hotel Behind every spotless room and welcoming public area is a coordinated effort, teamwork, and attention to detail. Some days follow a steady flow — schedules align, inspections are completed, and operations move seamlessly. Other days require adaptability — last-minute guest requests, staffing adjustments, or operational challenges. Within this dynamic environment, you’ll be the one who brings structure, support, and calm leadership, ensuring the Housekeeping team delivers excellence every single day. What you’ll do Support the Housekeeping Manager in supervising and coordinating the housekeeping team Assign daily tasks and ensure timely completion according to operational needs Monitor cleanliness of guest rooms, public areas, and back-of-house spaces Conduct inspections and provide constructive feedback to maintain service standards Assist with onboarding and training of new team members Support inventory control of cleaning supplies, linens, and guest amenities Collaborate closely with Front Office, Maintenance, and other departments Handle guest requests or complaints related to housekeeping services with professionalism Assist with administrative duties such as reports, schedules, and performance evaluations Ensure full compliance with health, safety, and sanitation regulations Your Uniqueness is Welcome We believe great Housekeeping leaders are not defined only by checklists and procedures — but by consistency, care, and the ability to inspire teams. If you enjoy working with people, maintaining high standards, and contributing to memorable guest experiences, you’ll feel right at home with us. We’re looking for someone who: Has proven experience in a supervisory role within Housekeeping, ideally in hospitality Is highly organized, detail-oriented, and proactive Demonstrates strong leadership and team motivation skills Is comfortable using housekeeping systems and MS Office Communicates clearly and effectively (English & Greek preferred) Can adapt to shift work, weekends, and holidays What We Offer Competitive salary and benefits Opportunities for professional growth and career development A supportive and collaborative working environment Accommodation & meals provided Ready to join our community?  ', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(641830, 'Housekeeping Manager - Eretria', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/301443', 'Παλλήνη', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-03-30 15:02:15', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Housekeeping Manager About the role As a Housekeeping Manager, you will be the guardian of cleanliness, comfort, and presentation across our property. You will lead and inspire a dedicated team, ensuring that every space — from guest rooms to public areas — reflects our high standards of hospitality. Your role is essential in shaping the guest experience. Through attention to detail, strong leadership, and operational excellence, you will create an environment where guests feel cared for, relaxed, and at home.   Life Inside ZEUS Hotels & Resorts Behind every perfectly made bed, every fresh scent, and every spotless space, there is a team working in harmony. Some days follow a steady rhythm — inspections, schedules, and routine operations. Other days are more dynamic, requiring quick decisions, flexibility, and strong coordination with other departments. You will be the person who brings structure, clarity, and inspiration to the team, ensuring that excellence is not an exception — but the standard.   What you’ll do Lead, train, and motivate the housekeeping team, fostering a positive and productive work environment Supervise daily housekeeping operations across guest rooms, public areas, and back-of-house spaces Conduct regular inspections to ensure cleanliness and service standards are consistently met Address any issues or deficiencies promptly and report to the management team Create and manage staff schedules, ensuring optimal coverage during peak periods Monitor inventory of cleaning supplies, linens, and guest amenities Place orders, track usage, and control costs effectively Collaborate with Front Office, Maintenance, and other departments to resolve guest needs swiftly Respond to guest feedback, inquiries, or complaints related to housekeeping Ensure full compliance with health, safety, and sanitation regulations Support budget preparation and cost control for the department   Your uniqueness is welcome Great Housekeeping Managers are not just supervisors — they are leaders, mentors, and problem-solvers. If you enjoy organizing, motivating teams, and delivering excellence through structure and care, you will thrive in this role.   What we’re looking for Proven experience in a supervisory or managerial housekeeping role, ideally in hospitality Strong leadership and organizational skills Exceptional attention to detail and quality standards Proficiency in housekeeping management systems and Microsoft Office Excellent communication skills Fluency in English and Greek Ability to multitask and remain calm under pressure Flexibility to work shifts, weekends, and holidays   What we offer Competitive salary and benefits package Opportunities for professional growth within the Group A supportive and dynamic working environment Accommodation (for resort locations) and meals provided   Ready to lead excellence behind the scenes?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(641831, 'Assistant Housekeeping Manager - Eretria', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/301441', 'Ερέτρια', 'πριν 7 λεπτά', '2026-03-30 15:02:17', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Assistant Housekeeping Manager About the role As a Housekeeping Assistant Manager, you’ll be a key pillar in maintaining the standards, rhythm, and daily excellence of our hotel operations. Working closely with the Housekeeping Manager, you will help ensure that every space reflects comfort, cleanliness, and care — the details that shape each guest’s experience. Your role combines organization, leadership, and hands-on involvement. From supporting the team on the floor to ensuring procedures run smoothly behind the scenes, you’ll help transform daily routines into consistently high-quality service. Life Inside the Hotel Behind every spotless room and welcoming public area is a coordinated effort, teamwork, and attention to detail. Some days follow a steady flow — schedules align, inspections are completed, and operations move seamlessly. Other days require adaptability — last-minute guest requests, staffing adjustments, or operational challenges. Within this dynamic environment, you’ll be the one who brings structure, support, and calm leadership, ensuring the Housekeeping team delivers excellence every single day. What you’ll do Support the Housekeeping Manager in supervising and coordinating the housekeeping team Assign daily tasks and ensure timely completion according to operational needs Monitor cleanliness of guest rooms, public areas, and back-of-house spaces Conduct inspections and provide constructive feedback to maintain service standards Assist with onboarding and training of new team members Support inventory control of cleaning supplies, linens, and guest amenities Collaborate closely with Front Office, Maintenance, and other departments Handle guest requests or complaints related to housekeeping services with professionalism Assist with administrative duties such as reports, schedules, and performance evaluations Ensure full compliance with health, safety, and sanitation regulations Your Uniqueness is Welcome We believe great Housekeeping leaders are not defined only by checklists and procedures — but by consistency, care, and the ability to inspire teams. If you enjoy working with people, maintaining high standards, and contributing to memorable guest experiences, you’ll feel right at home with us. We’re looking for someone who: Has proven experience in a supervisory role within Housekeeping, ideally in hospitality Is highly organized, detail-oriented, and proactive Demonstrates strong leadership and team motivation skills Is comfortable using housekeeping systems and MS Office Communicates clearly and effectively (English & Greek preferred) Can adapt to shift work, weekends, and holidays What We Offer Competitive salary and benefits Opportunities for professional growth and career development A supportive and collaborative working environment Accommodation & meals provided Ready to join our community?  ', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
