(641838, 'HoReCa Brand Activator – Premium Spirits | Χαλκιδική - Seasonal', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/sales-or-business-development-or-account-management-jobs/301431', 'Θεσσαλονίκη', 'πριν 3 λεπτά', '2026-03-30 15:02:23', 'ΤΑΛΑΝΤΟΝ ΜΟΝ. ΙΚΕ', 'Η εταιρεία μας στον χώρο των premium αποσταγμάτων αναζητά έναν 🥂 HoReCa Brand Activator – Premium Spirits | Χαλκιδική - Seasonal για την ανάπτυξη του χαρτοφυλακίου στη θερινή σεζόν. Ο ρόλος επικεντρώνεται στην ενίσχυση της διανομής, την ορατότητα των brands και την εμπορική απόδοση σε κομβικές HoReCa περιοχές (bars, beach bars, εστιατόρια) και επιλεγμένα σημεία λιανικής. Είναι δυναμική εμπορική θέση πεδίου με στόχους και μετρήσιμα αποτελέσματα – όχι απλή αναπλήρωση προϊόντων. 💼 🎯 Τι θα κάνεις 🍹 Συστηματικές επισκέψεις και ανάπτυξη συνεργασιών σε HoReCa (bars, beach bars, εστιατόρια)📈 Εξασφάλιση νέων καταχωρήσεων & διεύρυνση διανομής🛍 Διασφάλιση σωστής προβολής brands (back bar, menu, υλικά προώθησης)🎉 Υλοποίηση εμπορικών & προωθητικών ενεργειών🔎 Παρακολούθηση ανταγωνισμού & feedback αγοράς📊 Τήρηση υψηλών προτύπων merchandising & εμπορικής εικόνας🎯 Επίτευξη στόχων πωλήσεων & διανομής🤝 Συνεργασία με τμήματα Πωλήσεων, Marketing & Trade Marketing 👤 Τι ζητάμε ✔ Προϋπηρεσία σε HoReCa πωλήσεις ή κλάδο ποτών✔ Ισχυρές επικοινωνιακές & διαπραγματευτικές δεξιότητες✔ Εμπορική σκέψη & προσανατολισμός σε μετρήσιμα αποτελέσματα✔ Δυναμική προσωπικότητα & επαγγελματική παρουσία✔ Προσανατολισμό σε ανάπτυξη & εκτέλεση – δεν είναι ρόλος απλής αναπλήρωσης προϊόντων 🎁 Παροχές 📅 Διάρκεια Συνεργασίας: 1 Απριλίου – 30 Σεπτεμβρίου⏰ Πλήρης απασχόληση🚗 Εταιρικό αυτοκίνητο για περιοχές ευθύνης', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(641839, 'Bartender', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/301430', 'Κως', 'πριν 10 λεπτά', '2026-03-30 15:02:25', 'Wavemaker Hospitality', 'Don’t ride the wave. Be the one who starts it. Wavemaker Hospitality, the leading hotel company in Cyprus and Greece, is expanding its operations. We are looking for experienced and talented individuals as Bartenders to join the award-winning 5* Atlantica Belvedere in Kos island for the season 2026. As a Bartender, you play a crucial role in creating a positive and enjoyable experience for our guests. Your responsibilities extend beyond simply mixing drinks; you are a hospitality professional and a customer service expert. Responsibilities Craft and serve various beverages, from classic cocktails to custom creations, ensuring precision and quality in every pour. Maintain a deep knowledge of drink recipes, garnishes, and presentation techniques. Provide exceptional customer service by engaging with patrons, taking drink orders, and making recommendations based on preferences. Create a welcoming and friendly atmosphere, fostering positive interactions with guests. Manage multiple orders simultaneously while maintaining a high level of customer satisfaction. Adhere to hygiene and safety standards, including the proper handling of glassware and bar equipment. Stay abreast of industry trends and customer preferences to keep our offerings fresh and exciting. Collaborate with other staff members to ensure a seamless and coordinated service experience. Adhere to all relevant laws and regulations related to the service of alcoholic beverages. Requirements 2 years of experience as a bartender Extensive knowledge of beverages, including industry trends and best practices Strong communication, and interpersonal skills Ability to work under pressure and handle multiple tasks simultaneously Excellent organizational and time management skills, with the ability to prioritize tasks effectively Fluent in English Benefits Competitive salary and other benefits (as per local legislation) Advanced opportunities for professional growth Accommodation (if necessary) and board Participation in educational programs Diverse and multicultural environments Professional skills development', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(641840, 'Cook A | Main Kitchen', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/301432', 'Ρόδος', 'πριν μερικά δευτερόλεπτα', '2026-03-30 15:02:25', 'Wavemaker Hospitality', 'Wavemaker Hospitality, the leading hotel company in Cyprus and Greece, is looking for experienced and talented individuals as Main Kitchen Cook A\' to join the award-winning 5* Atlantica Hotels in Rhodes island for the summer season 2026. Responsibilities Handle and portion ingredients according to recipe specifications and safety guidelines. Adjust recipes as needed to meet dietary restrictions or special requests. Monitor and maintain proper food temperatures throughout the cooking process. Ensure the culinary section adheres to all safety and health regulations Stay updated on culinary techniques and industry trends through continuous learning. Coordinate timing with other cooks and kitchen staff to ensure timely delivery of all menu items.  Requirements Minimum of 2+ years of experience in a similar position Certificate in culinary arts Strong sense of culinary creativity with attention to detail Ability to multitask in a fast-paced and dynamic environment In-depth knowledge of sanitation principles and food preparation standards Familiarity with a range of cooking and other kitchen equipment Excellent communication skills and an enthusiasm for teamwork Benefits Competitive salary and other benefits (as per local legislation) Advanced opportunities for professional growth Accommodation (if necessary) and board Participation in educational programs Diverse and multicultural environments Professional skills development  ', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(641841, 'Συσκευαστής / Συσκευάστρια Αποθήκης', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/logistics-or-warehouse-jobs/301426', 'Μεταμόρφωση', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-03-30 15:02:27', 'VICAN A.E', 'Η εταιρεία VICAN Α.Ε., η οποία δραστηριοποιείται στον ιατροφαρμακευτικό χώρο, ζητά να προσλάβει άμεσα: Συσκευαστή/Συσκευάστρια Αποθήκης Έδρα: ΑΘΗΝΑ (Κωδικός Θέσης: WH04) Αρμοδιότητες: Συσκευασία και ποιοτικός έλεγχος προϊόντων Τακτοποίηση των ειδών της αποθήκης Υποστηρικτικές εργασίες της αποθήκης Απαραίτητα Προσόντα: Απόφοιτος/η Λυκείου Επιθυμητή γνώση Αγγλικών Εξοικείωση με χρήση RF Επιθυμητή προϋπηρεσία σε αντίστοιχη θέση Ταχύτητα, αντίληψη και οξυδέρκεια Άριστες επικοινωνιακές και οργανωτικές ικανότητες Ομαδικότητα και συνεργασία Η εταιρία προσφέρει: Ικανοποιητικές αποδοχές Πενθήμερη εργασία αορίστου χρόνου Ευχάριστο εργασιακό περιβάλλον Άνετες συνθήκες εργασίας  ', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(641842, 'Engineering Storekeeper at Four Seasons Astir Palace Hotel Athens', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/logistics-or-warehouse-jobs/301415', 'Βουλιαγμένη', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-03-30 15:02:27', 'Four Seasons Astir Palace Hotel Athens', 'At Four Seasons Astir Palace Hotel Athens (ranked No. 17 in the World’s 50 Best Hotels), we are seeking a highly motivated Engineering Storekeeper to join our Purchasing Department for the Season 2026. This role plays a key part in ensuring the proper control, storage, and distribution of engineering materials and supplies, supporting the hotel’s operational excellence and compliance with Four Seasons standards. What You Will Do Check and receive all incoming engineering goods, ensuring accuracy and compliance with internal procedures. Maintain safe, clean, secure, and well-organized storage areas in accordance with hygiene and safety regulations. Monitor and maintain perpetual inventory records for engineering items. Ensure proper labeling, dating, and rotation of stock to facilitate reordering and stock control. Conduct regular inventory checks and compile orders based on par levels and operational needs. Safeguard storeroom keys and ensure restricted access to authorized personnel only. Follow internal controls, policies, and procedures related to Purchasing, Receiving, and Inventory. Work closely with Engineering, Receiving, Finance, and other departments to ensure smooth operations. Support the hotel’s Safety and Sustainability initiatives. What You Bring High School Diploma or equivalent. Minimum two years of full-time experience in the construction or engineering sector. European Passport or legal right to work in Greece. Working knowledge of inventory procedures and internal controls. Basic computer skills and ability to operate relevant systems. Good level in English & fluency in Greek (oral and written). Strong integrity, organizational skills, and attention to detail. Ability to work in a safe, structured, and professional manner.   What We Offer Competitive Salary and comprehensive Benefits Package. Complimentary Employee Meals, Bus Transportation, Uniform & Laundry Services. Ticket Restaurant monthly allowance of €100 - €120 . Complimentary Nights at Four Seasons Hotels & Resorts worldwide. Employee Recognition Program. Opportunities for Global Travel through Task Forces and Transfers. Access to Four Seasons global Training & Development programs.   Schedule & Contract Summer Seasonal Position – 5 working days per week, 2 days off. Schedule may vary according to operational needs.   If you are detail-oriented, organized, and ready to contribute to the smooth operation of one of the world’s leading luxury resorts, we look forward to receiving your application.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(641843, 'Guest Relations Agent - Crete', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/301428', 'Παλλήνη', 'πριν 3 λεπτά', '2026-03-30 15:02:29', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Guest Relations Agent About the role Join our hospitality team and become part of an environment where exceptional service and meaningful guest experiences are at the heart of everything we do. We are seeking a warm, engaging, and detail-oriented Guest Relations Agent who will act as a key point of contact for our guests, ensuring every stay is seamless, personalized, and memorable. What you will do • Welcome guests upon arrival and ensure a smooth and pleasant check-in experience• Act as a main point of communication for guests throughout their stay• Provide detailed information about the property, facilities, services, and local attractions• Handle and resolve guest concerns or complaints promptly and professionally• Anticipate guest needs and personalize services to exceed expectations• Coordinate special guest requests, including reservations, transportation, and event planning• Manage VIP guest preferences with discretion and attention to detail• Collect and analyze guest feedback to support continuous service improvement• Collaborate closely with Front Office, Housekeeping, and Food & Beverage teams• Maintain accurate guest profiles and records within the hotel system Your uniqueness is welcome We are looking for a service-driven professional who enjoys connecting with people, thrives in a fast-paced hospitality environment, and takes pride in delivering outstanding guest experiences. The ideal candidate: • Has previous experience in Guest Relations or a similar role, preferably within luxury hospitality• Possesses excellent verbal and written communication skills• Is fluent in English and Greek (additional languages will be considered a strong advantage)• Is comfortable using hotel management systems and standard office software• Demonstrates strong interpersonal skills, problem-solving abilities, and attention to detail• Is flexible to work shifts, including weekends and holidays• Shows genuine passion for guest satisfaction and service excellence What we offer • Competitive salary and benefits package• Continuous training and professional development• Opportunities for career growth within a dynamic hospitality environment• Accommodation (for resort properties) and meals provided• A supportive team culture focused on quality and guest satisfaction Ready to join our team?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(641844, 'Guest Relations Agent - Χαλκιδική', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/301429', 'Παλλήνη', 'πριν 4 λεπτά', '2026-03-30 15:02:30', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Guest Relations Agent About the role Join our hospitality team and become part of an environment where exceptional service and meaningful guest experiences are at the heart of everything we do. We are seeking a warm, engaging, and detail-oriented Guest Relations Agent who will act as a key point of contact for our guests, ensuring every stay is seamless, personalized, and memorable. What you will do • Welcome guests upon arrival and ensure a smooth and pleasant check-in experience• Act as a main point of communication for guests throughout their stay• Provide detailed information about the property, facilities, services, and local attractions• Handle and resolve guest concerns or complaints promptly and professionally• Anticipate guest needs and personalize services to exceed expectations• Coordinate special guest requests, including reservations, transportation, and event planning• Manage VIP guest preferences with discretion and attention to detail• Collect and analyze guest feedback to support continuous service improvement• Collaborate closely with Front Office, Housekeeping, and Food & Beverage teams• Maintain accurate guest profiles and records within the hotel system Your uniqueness is welcome We are looking for a service-driven professional who enjoys connecting with people, thrives in a fast-paced hospitality environment, and takes pride in delivering outstanding guest experiences. The ideal candidate: • Has previous experience in Guest Relations or a similar role, preferably within luxury hospitality• Possesses excellent verbal and written communication skills• Is fluent in English and Greek (additional languages will be considered a strong advantage)• Is comfortable using hotel management systems and standard office software• Demonstrates strong interpersonal skills, problem-solving abilities, and attention to detail• Is flexible to work shifts, including weekends and holidays• Shows genuine passion for guest satisfaction and service excellence What we offer • Competitive salary and benefits package• Continuous training and professional development• Opportunities for career growth within a dynamic hospitality environment• Accommodation (for resort properties) and meals provided• A supportive team culture focused on quality and guest satisfaction Ready to join our team?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(641845, 'Bartender - Eretria', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/301427', 'Ερέτρια', 'πριν 3 λεπτά', '2026-03-30 15:02:31', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Bartender About the role As a Barman / Barmaid, you will be at the heart of the guest experience, bringing energy, personality, and craftsmanship to every drink you serve. With each cocktail, conversation, and interaction, you help create moments of genuine hospitality that guests remember long after their stay.This role blends technical skill with creativity and human connection — balancing quality, speed, and warm service in a vibrant bar environment. Life Behind the Bar Every shift has its own rhythm. Some moments flow seamlessly — orders align, the bar runs smoothly, and teamwork is effortless. Other times are more dynamic — lively conversations, diverse guests, and spontaneous interactions shape the atmosphere.Within this rhythm, you are the one who sets the tone, keeps the bar organized, and ensures every guest feels welcome and relaxed. What you’ll do Welcome guests with a friendly, professional, and attentive approach Prepare and serve alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages according to established recipes and guest preferences Take and process orders accurately through the point-of-sale system Recommend cocktails, wines, beers, and other beverages based on guest tastes and preferences Ensure the bar area is clean, organized, and well-stocked at all times Adhere to all health, safety, sanitation, and responsible alcohol service guidelines Handle cash and credit card transactions accurately and efficiently Collaborate closely with the wider team to ensure smooth operations and exceptional guest experiences Your Uniqueness is Welcome We believe the best bartenders are defined not only by recipes and techniques, but by their ability to read the room, connect with guests, and create atmosphere.If you enjoy working with people, delivering high-quality service, and growing within a hospitality-driven environment, you’ll feel right at home with us. We’re looking for someone who: Has previous experience as a Barman / Barmaid (preferred but not required) Possesses good knowledge of cocktails, wines, beers, and non-alcoholic beverages Demonstrates excellent customer service skills and a positive, outgoing personality Is able to multitask and perform efficiently in a fast-paced environment Pays attention to detail and takes pride in quality service Is flexible to work evenings, weekends, and holidays Holds responsible alcohol service certification (preferred) What we offer Competitive salary A dynamic and supportive working environment Opportunities for career growth and professional development Meals during shifts and accommodation provided Ready to join our Hospitality Community?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(641846, 'Ηλεκτρολόγος Βάρδιας', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/technicians-or-service-jobs/301407', 'Χαλκίδα', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-03-30 15:02:31', 'HELLENIC QUALITY FOODS AET', 'Η HQF (Hellenic Quality Foods A.E.T.),είναι μία από τις σημαντικότερες βιομηχανίες τροφίμων στην ελληνική αγορά, με τα αναγνωρισμένα εμπορικά σήματα ΚΑΝΑΚΙ και MIMIKOS. Με στόχο την περαιτέρω ενίσχυση της ομάδας μας , αναζητούμε να εντάξουμε στο δυναμικό μας για τις εγκαταστάσεις μας στην Αρτάκη Ευβοίας:                                                                   Ηλεκτρολόγο Βάρδιας     Βασικές αρμοδιότητες: Έλεγχος και συντήρηση των ηλεκτρολογικών εγκαταστάσεων Επίβλεψη, διάγνωση  και αποκατάσταση βλαβών στον παραγωγικό εξοπλισμό Εκτέλεση εργασιών τακτικής και προληπτικής συντήρησης του εξοπλισμού Απαιτούμενα προσόντα Πτυχίο Ηλεκτρολόγου (ΙΕΚ/ΕΠΑΛ/ΤΕΙ) Επιθυμητή η προϋπηρεσία σε αντίστοιχη θέση Δυνατότητα εργασίας σε βάρδιες Γνώση της Αγγλικής γλώσσας Υπευθυνότητα και συνέπεια Η εταιρία παρέχει: Σταθερή και πλήρη απασχόληση Ανταγωνιστικό πακέτο αποδοχών Άριστο εργασιακό περιβάλλον', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(641847, 'Bartender - Kos', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/301425', 'Ερέτρια', 'πριν 5 λεπτά', '2026-03-30 15:02:35', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Bartender About the role As a Barman / Barmaid, you will be at the heart of the guest experience, bringing energy, personality, and craftsmanship to every drink you serve. With each cocktail, conversation, and interaction, you help create moments of genuine hospitality that guests remember long after their stay.This role blends technical skill with creativity and human connection — balancing quality, speed, and warm service in a vibrant bar environment. Life Behind the Bar Every shift has its own rhythm. Some moments flow seamlessly — orders align, the bar runs smoothly, and teamwork is effortless. Other times are more dynamic — lively conversations, diverse guests, and spontaneous interactions shape the atmosphere.Within this rhythm, you are the one who sets the tone, keeps the bar organized, and ensures every guest feels welcome and relaxed. What you’ll do Welcome guests with a friendly, professional, and attentive approach Prepare and serve alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages according to established recipes and guest preferences Take and process orders accurately through the point-of-sale system Recommend cocktails, wines, beers, and other beverages based on guest tastes and preferences Ensure the bar area is clean, organized, and well-stocked at all times Adhere to all health, safety, sanitation, and responsible alcohol service guidelines Handle cash and credit card transactions accurately and efficiently Collaborate closely with the wider team to ensure smooth operations and exceptional guest experiences Your Uniqueness is Welcome We believe the best bartenders are defined not only by recipes and techniques, but by their ability to read the room, connect with guests, and create atmosphere.If you enjoy working with people, delivering high-quality service, and growing within a hospitality-driven environment, you’ll feel right at home with us. We’re looking for someone who: Has previous experience as a Barman / Barmaid (preferred but not required) Possesses good knowledge of cocktails, wines, beers, and non-alcoholic beverages Demonstrates excellent customer service skills and a positive, outgoing personality Is able to multitask and perform efficiently in a fast-paced environment Pays attention to detail and takes pride in quality service Is flexible to work evenings, weekends, and holidays Holds responsible alcohol service certification (preferred) What we offer Competitive salary A dynamic and supportive working environment Opportunities for career growth and professional development Meals during shifts and accommodation provided Ready to join our Hospitality Community?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(641848, 'FLOCAFE ΜΑΓΕΙΡΕΣ', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/food-or-cafe-jobs/301421', 'Σπάτα Λούτσας', 'πριν 19 λεπτά', '2026-03-30 15:02:35', 'DREAM FOOD ΣΠΑΤΩΝ ΕΣΤΙΑΣΗ Α.Ε.', 'Μάγειρες ζητούνται από την καφετέρια Flocafe στο εμπορικό κέντρο Smart Park στα Σπάτα. Άμεση πρόσληψη, πλήρης και αορίστου χρόνου εργασία, ικανοποιητικός μισθός, ευχάριστο περιβάλλον εργασίας, συνεχής εκπαίδευση.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση');
