 100€ κάθε μήνα. Σταθερά 5ήμερη εργασία. Ναι, ακόμα και τον Ιούλιο και τον Αύγουστο.Πρόγραμμα εκπαίδευσης περίπου 3 εβδομάδων: πριν μπεις στα βαθιά, φροντίζουμε να μάθεις όσα χρειάζεσαι για να ξεκινήσεις δουλειά την επόμενη μέρα! Φυσικά και πληρώνεσαι παράλληλα.Μια δεμένη ομάδα: αυτό που μας ξεχωρίζει είναι η κουλτούρα της ομάδας μας, οι ευκαιρίες που βρίσκουμε για να κάνουμε πράγματα μαζί. Μαθαίνουμε online, μοιραζόμαστε δώρα, γιορτάζουμε, βραβεύουμε τα αγαπημένα μας καταστήματα, φροντίζουμε ο ένας τον άλλον.Ιδιωτική ιατρική ασφάλιση. Η υγεία σου είναι πάντα η πρώτη μας προτεραιότητα. Γι\' αυτό όλη η ομάδα μας αποκτά ιδιωτική ιατρική ασφάλιση.Μηναία κάρτα απεριορίστων διαδρομών ATH.ENA., ώστε οι διαδρομές σου από και προς την εργασία να είναι πιο εύκολες. Φυσικά, μπορείς να την χρησιμοποιείς και για τις καθημερινές σου βόλτες. Έλα στο #teamlidl Είσαι το επόμενο κεφάλαιο του success story μας; Κάνε την αίτησή σου τώρα και γίνε μέρος του #teamlidl , της πιο δυναμικής ομάδας στο #retail.', 'Μερική απασχόληση'),
(644997, 'Junior Software Developer & IT Consultant', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/303044', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 9 λεπτά', '2026-04-04 15:00:09', 'Netcompany', 'Company DescriptionAre you ready to shape the future technological landscape in Europe?We are dedicated to responsible digitalisation, building innovative, inclusive solutions that drive meaningful impact. With over 8,900 professionals across Europe, we help EU institutions, public and private organisations thrive in a rapidly evolving digital world. Are you ready to shape the future through technology? Your journey starts here. Take a look at some of our impactful projects here: https://netcompany.com/cases/Job DescriptionAre you ready for a sneak-peek in the day of a Junior Software Developer & IT Consultant in Netcompany?Joining us as a Junior Software Developer & IT Consultant at Netcompany, you won\'t just be writing code—you\'ll be shaping solutions, advising clients, and driving the digital transformation that impacts millions of people across Europe. You will become part of a highly skilled, agile team delivering large-scale IT projects for major public and private sector organizations. This is your opportunity to combine hands-on development with client-facing advisory work, growing into a trusted technology advisor on an international stage.Based in Athens, you will work on international projects, contributing to some of Denmark\'s most complex IT initiatives while building your career. Your daily responsibilities will involve software development, client collaboration, and task management, preparing you for a future in one of our specialties: backend, frontend, full-stack, or DevOps engineering.As a Junior Software Developer & IT Consultant you will:Contribute to all phases of full-cycle IT projects—from requirements analysis and solution design to development, UAT support, and user training.Collaborate directly with clients to understand business needs and translate them into technical specifications.Design, develop, and maintain enterprise-grade applications using modern technologies (e.g., Java, C#, .NET, Spring Boot, React, Angular).Work across both backend and frontend layers, as well as integration points within complex enterprise systems, including CRM/CX solutions.Develop innovative concepts and implement sophisticated consulting solutions, acting as a business advisor to clients.Create long-term relationships with clients and identify business development opportunities.Lead sub-streams of work, conduct daily stand-ups, and report progress to clients or project managers.Produce clear technical and functional documentation and participate in peer code reviews.QualificationsWhat would make you a fit for the role:A recent degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field.Strong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate business needs into technical solutions.Excellent communication skills in English (written and verbal), with the confidence to interact with clients and stakeholders.A customer-oriented mindset and genuine interest in understanding how businesses operate.Strong interpersonal and teamwork skills, with the ability to collaborate in cross-functional and international environments.A proactive attitude, ownership mentality, and commitment to delivering high-quality results.Availability to travel when required.It would also be a plus if you match some of the following:Familiarity with at least one programming language like Java or C#.Knowledge of web technologies including HTML5, CSS3, or JavaScript frameworks (e.g., Angular, React).Understanding of database concepts (SQL) and experience with source control tools (e.g., Git).Additional InformationBeing a part of the Netcompany team, you will be provided with: The opportunity to work in a modern environment & in a hybrid working modelA seamless onboarding experience and a buddy to support you on your first stepsA competitive compensation & benefits packageHealth and life insurance programMeal and commuting allowanceWell-being activities (on premises)Continuous learning opportunities using the most modern methods (unlimited access to Udemy for Business, ad-hoc trainings)A personalized development plan for targeted career growthIf you are looking forward to be part of a diverse environment, and have the opportunity to work alongside well-experienced professionals, on challenging, large-scale projects that directly impact millions of citizens around the globe, then this is the place to be!By joining Netcompany in Athens, you will be part of a vivid team of 2,300+ tech professionals. When at the office, you\'ll have the flexibility to work from our three modern, sustainable, and state-of-the-art offices!Please upload your CV in English via the Apply button. All applications will be treated as strictly confidential.We ensure equal opportunities, treatment, and consideration to all candidates. Discrimination based on sex, racial or ethnic origin, religion or belief, disability, age, sexual orientation or marital status, physical or mental disability, or any other factor protected by applicable laws and regulations is prohibited. As part of the Netcompany culture, we respect human rights and focus on creating a positive workplace, where all employees are valued, and where diversity and inclusion are a vital part of our everyday working experience.In the following link you may find our CV Submission privacy notice: https://netcompany.com/cv-submission-privacy-notice/Please upload your CV in English via the Apply button. All applications will be treated as strictly confidential.We ensure equal opportunities, treatment, and consideration to all candidates. Discrimination based on sex, racial or ethnic origin, religion or belief, disability, age, sexual orientation or marital status, physical or mental disability, or any other factor protected by applicable laws and regulations is prohibited. As part of the Netcompany culture, we respect human rights and focus on creating a positive workplace, where all employees are valued, and where diversity and inclusion are a vital part of our everyday working experience.In the following link you may find our CV Submission privacy notice: https://netcompany.com/cv-submission-privacy-notice/', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(644998, 'SEO / GEO Specialist', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/retail-jobs/303045?origin=pjp', 'Ηράκλειο', 'πριν 13 λεπτά', '2026-04-04 15:00:09', 'Κωτσόβολος', 'At Kotsovolos, we believe in your uniqueness and everything you have to offer!Here, you create your own current!📈 Our achievements in numbers3,000+ People | 100+ Stores | 2 Logistics Centers - 77.000 sqm | 2 Call Centers | 2 Modern Training Centers | Kapaskill - our live, personalized learning ecosystem | 75,000+ hours of training per year | 400+ different roles & 49 Business Units🎯 Our purposeBetter Living. Everywhere. for Everyone!💼 Your everyday work-life Conduct technical SEO audits and manage key elements (site architecture, Core Web Vitals, structured data, XML sitemaps) to ensure crawlability and indexation health Act as the internal SEO point of contact, coordinating priorities and delivery across Marketing, E-commerce, and Content teams Develop and execute keyword strategy aligned with commercial and E-commerce goals Optimize on-page SEO across category, product, and landing pages, including internal linking Manage Local SEO strategy across store locations, including Google Business Profile optimization, local citations, and location-based search visibility Support E-commerce growth through SEO roadmaps, product launch strategies, and ongoing performance tracking Lead Generative Engine Optimization (GEO) initiatives for AI search (e.g. Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Perplexity) and monitor brand visibility Drive off-site organic authority initiatives, including social SEO, Digital PR coordination, and brand presence across external platforms 🚀 As an ideal fit, you should have BA in Marketing, Computer Science, or related field 2-4 years in SEO, with proven track record of organic traffic growth E-commerce SEO experience required Proficiency in SEO tools (Ahrefs, SEMrush, Screaming Frog) Google Analytics and Search Console expertise Solid stakeholder management and communication skills, with ability to coordinate across multiple teams Experience with AI search optimization - a strong plus 💎 What we offer Continuous training in new technologies and tools Career development and growth opportunities Competitive bonus scheme, performance-based Group health/medical insurance package Hybrid working model Internal wellbeing actions ⭐ Join #teamKotsovolos and be part of a team that promotes new technologies, loves to evolve, embraces diversity and is next to society.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(645000, 'Οδηγός για το κατάστημά μας στο Μαρούσι', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/transport-or-driving-jobs/303041?origin=pjp', 'Μαρούσι', 'πριν 17 λεπτά', '2026-04-04 15:00:11', 'ΑΒ Βασιλόπουλος', 'Ο Όμιλος ΑΛΦΑ ΒΗΤΑ ΒΑΣΙΛΟΠΟΥΛΟΣ είναι μία από τις μεγαλύτερες αλυσίδες στο χώρο εμπορίας τροφίμων με περισσότερα από 500 καταστήματα, λιανεμπορίου, χονδρικής και franchise καταστήματα, και πάνω από 12.500 εργαζόμενους.Είναι μέλος του Ομίλου Ahold Delhaize που αποτελείται από 21 εταιρίες σε 3 ηπείρους (11 χώρες), πάνω από 375.000 εργαζόμενους και απολαμβάνει την εμπιστοσύνη περισσότερων από 50 εκατομμύρια πελατών κάθε εβδομάδα.Για το κατάστημά μας στο ΜαρούσιΗ Εταιρεία μας ενδιαφέρεται να προσλάβει προσωπικό για το κάτωθι τμήμα:ΟδηγόςΠροσφέρονται ικανοποιητικές αποδοχές, δυναμικό περιβάλλον εργασίας και προοπτικέςΑποστολή βιογραφικώνΟι υποψήφιοι που ενδιαφέρονται παρακαλούνται να υποβάλλουν βιογραφικό σημείωμα online.Όλα τα βιογραφικά θα θεωρηθούν εμπιστευτικά.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
