(645002, 'Πωλητές/ Πωλήτριες για τα καταστήματά μας στο Μαρούσι', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/retail-jobs/303040?origin=pjp', 'Μαρούσι', 'πριν 8 λεπτά', '2026-04-04 15:00:13', 'ΑΒ Βασιλόπουλος', 'Ο Όμιλος ΑΛΦΑ ΒΗΤΑ ΒΑΣΙΛΟΠΟΥΛΟΣ είναι μία από τις μεγαλύτερες αλυσίδες στο χώρο εμπορίας τροφίμων με περισσότερα από 500 καταστήματα, λιανεμπορίου, χονδρικής και franchise καταστήματα, και πάνω από 12.000 εργαζόμενους. Είναι μέλος του Ομίλου Ahold Delhaize που αποτελείται από 21 εταιρίες σε 3 ηπείρους (11 χώρες), πάνω από 375.000 εργαζόμενους και απολαμβάνει την εμπιστοσύνη περισσότερων από 50 εκατομμύρια πελατών κάθε εβδομάδα.Για τα καταστήματά μας στοΜαρούσιΗ Εταιρεία μας ενδιαφέρεται να προσλάβει προσωπικό για τα κάτωθι τμήματα:ΑλλοιώσιμαΤυποποιημέναΠροσφέρονται ικανοποιητικές αποδοχές, δυναμικό περιβάλλον εργασίας και προοπτικές εξέλιξης.Αποστολή βιογραφικώνΟι υποψήφιοι που ενδιαφέρονται παρακαλούνται να υποβάλλουν βιογραφικό σημείωμα online.Όλα τα βιογραφικά θα θεωρηθούν εμπιστευτικά.', 'Μερική απασχόληση'),
(645003, 'Προσωπικός βοηθός / Συντηρητής / Προσωπικός Οδηγός', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/303039', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-04 15:00:15', 'Red Center', 'Αναζητούμε Συντηρητή - Προσωπικό Βοηθό στελέχους με καθήκοντα συντήρησης κτηρίου, μετακινήσεων και διεκπεραίωσης εργασιών. Απαραίτητα: δίπλωμα Β’ κατηγορίας, ιδιόκτητη μηχανή, εμπειρία σε γενικές εργασίες συντήρησης, ευελιξία & υπευθυνότητα. Δίπλωμα ταχυπλόου θα εκτιμηθεί. Αποστολή βιογραφικού με φωτογραφία Παροχές: ανάλγα με την προϋπηρεσία, άμεση έναρξη.  ', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση / Μερική απασχόληση'),
(645004, 'Promo Marketing Specialist', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/marketing-or-advertising-jobs/303043?origin=pjp', 'Γέρακας', 'πριν ένα λεπτό', '2026-04-04 15:00:15', 'ΑΒ Βασιλόπουλος', 'AB Vassilopoulos: A world of opportunities awaits you At AB Vassilopoulos, we are more than 12,000 people sharing the same purpose: to give our best every day and make a difference in people\'s lives. With a presence across Greece - from stores and offices to distribution centers and our Home Shop Center with more than 500 Job roles - we offer countless opportunities for growth, in an environment that respects and supports every team member. As part of the global Ahold Delhaize group and one of the most dynamic brands in Greece, we are proud to consistently be recognized as a Top Employer.Become part of the #proudABers team!The opportunity As a Promo & Price Marketing Specialist, you will play an important role in contributing to the success of our promotional & pricing campaigns through effective use of 360 communication. You will be responsible for creating and overseeing compelling promotional content, ensuring it aligns with our overall pricing and promotional strategies.This role requires a strong understanding of both consumer behavior and media dynamics, with a focus on delivering impactful promo marketing material that drive sales and customer engagement.What you will focus on Participate in all stages of planning, creation of the corporate promotional materials for all AB stores coordinating the process of leaflet (digital & print) working closely with Commercial teams.Develop and oversee TV promotional content and campaigns, ensuring they align with AB\'s pricing strategies and promotional calendar.Collaborate with internal teams & external partners, including marketing, commerce, agencies to create impactful promotional messaging for TV broadcasts and digital platforms.Ensure the accurate execution of promotional campaigns, coordinating with the media and production teams to guarantee that TV ads and digital content are delivered on time and within budget.Work closely with the trade team to ensure that promotions are accurately communicated and that pricing reflects the overall promotional strategy across all channels.Monitor competition marketing promo communication & assets.Stay up to date on the latest trends in TV advertising, and promotional strategies within the supermarket and retail sector.Support budget management, tracking costs and ensuring efficient allocation of resources.Who we are looking for BSc in Marketing, Communication, Business Administration, or any relevant field. MSc would be considered an asset.3 to 4 years working experience, in relevant industry or agency, especially in Μarketing/Trade Marketing in FMCG or agencies. Retail knowledge would be considered an assetFluency in English language, both written & verbalMS Office literacyThe value you bring Passion for the Customer | Focus on in depth customer needs\' understanding & excel at retail Results orientation |Accountability - attention to detailAuthentic Communication | Deliver messages in a clear, compelling and concise manner, create wow effect to audiencesTogetherness |Value team\'s ideas, uniqueness and safeguard belongingMomentum | Make a difference, secure end results and be on topWe care for you A buddy to support you during onboardingFree lunch meals in our restaurantUnlimited access to LinkedIn Learning programsHealth insuranceAvailable parkingHybrid way of workingWellbeing ProgramA place where everyone belongs All our candidates and employees are treated with respect and equality, regardless of race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic protected by law.As part of our commitment to inclusion and equality, we have signed the Diversity Charter Greece , we are certified with the SHARE Equality Label and we are members of LEAD Network, recognizing our tangible actions toward a truly inclusive work environment.*All applications are treated with utmost confidentiality', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(645005, 'Sales & Marketing', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/marketing-or-advertising-jobs/303025', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-04 15:00:17', '', 'Η εταιρεία μας, αναζητά 5 νέους συνεργάτες με όρεξη και θετική διάθεση, να στελεχώσουν το αντίστοιχο τμήμα Marketing & Πωλήσεων. Προφίλ υποψηφίου: Ευχέρεια στην επικοινωνία και το λόγο Διαθέτει ομαδικό πνεύμα και συνεργατική διάθεση  Άμεση διαθεσιμότητα  Διάθεση για προσωπική εξέλιξη και μάθηση Θετική προσωπικότητα & επαγγελματισμό Δεν απαιτείται προϋπηρεσία - παρέχεται δομημένη εκπαίδευση και πιστοποιήση απο την εταιρία, καθώς γνώση και υποστήριξη για όποιον επιθυμεί να εξελιχθεί στα επόμενα στάδια της εταιρίας. Αν σε ενδιαφέρει η καριέρα σου, η εξελιξή σου και θέλεις να εισαι μέλος μιας ομάδας που σε στηρίζει, στείλε μας το βιογραφικο σου σήμερα!', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση / Μερική απασχόληση'),
(645006, 'Front Office Manager - Chalkidiki', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/303038', 'Παλλήνη', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-04 15:00:17', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Front Office Manager About the role As a Front Office Manager, you’ll be at the heart of the guest experience — leading the teams that shape first impressions and lasting memories across our hotel. You’ll oversee the full Front Office operation, ensuring that every arrival, interaction, and departure reflects the standards of a luxury hospitality environment. Your role blends operational excellence with people leadership, creating a front office culture where service feels effortless, personal, and genuine. Working closely with Hotel Operations and all key departments, you’ll ensure smooth daily performance while continuously elevating guest satisfaction and team engagement.   Life Inside the Hotel The front office is where the hotel truly comes alive. Some days follow a steady rhythm — arrivals flow smoothly, guests are delighted, and teams work in sync. Other days are more dynamic — high occupancy, special requests, last-minute changes, or opportunities to turn a challenge into a memorable guest moment. Within this fast-paced environment, you’ll be the visible leader — guiding your team with confidence, setting the tone for service excellence, and ensuring that every guest feels welcomed, understood, and cared for.   What you’ll do Oversee all Front Office operations, including Reception, Concierge, and Guest Services Lead, train, and inspire the Front Office team to deliver exceptional and personalized service Ensure a seamless check-in and check-out experience, room assignments, and reservation coordination Maintain a strong presence in the lobby, engaging with guests and proactively addressing their needs Monitor guest feedback, handle concerns professionally, and implement service improvements Collaborate closely with Housekeeping, F&B, Sales, and other departments to ensure a unified guest journey Prepare and manage departmental budgets, ensuring cost control and operational efficiency Ensure full compliance with hotel policies, procedures, and health & safety standards   Your Uniqueness is Welcome We believe great Front Office Managers are more than operational experts — they are hosts, mentors, and problem solvers. If you thrive in guest interaction, enjoy leading diverse teams, and take pride in creating memorable experiences, you’ll feel right at home with us. We’re looking for someone who: Has proven experience as a Front Office Manager or in a similar leadership role within luxury hospitality Demonstrates strong leadership, multitasking, and problem-solving skills Is proficient in PMS systems (preferably Protel) Possesses excellent organizational and communication abilities Is fluent in English Has a genuine passion for service excellence and guest satisfaction   Why Join Us? A supportive and collaborative work environment Opportunities for career growth within a world-class resort and hotel group Competitive compensation and benefits Accommodation (for resorts) and meals provided Ready to join our community?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(645007, 'Front Office Manager - Kos Island', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/303036', 'Ηρακλείδες', 'πριν 8 λεπτά', '2026-04-04 15:00:19', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Front Office Manager About the role As a Front Office Manager, you’ll be at the heart of the guest experience — leading the teams that shape first impressions and lasting memories across our hotel. You’ll oversee the full Front Office operation, ensuring that every arrival, interaction, and departure reflects the standards of a luxury hospitality environment. Your role blends operational excellence with people leadership, creating a front office culture where service feels effortless, personal, and genuine. Working closely with Hotel Operations and all key departments, you’ll ensure smooth daily performance while continuously elevating guest satisfaction and team engagement.   Life Inside the Hotel The front office is where the hotel truly comes alive. Some days follow a steady rhythm — arrivals flow smoothly, guests are delighted, and teams work in sync. Other days are more dynamic — high occupancy, special requests, last-minute changes, or opportunities to turn a challenge into a memorable guest moment. Within this fast-paced environment, you’ll be the visible leader — guiding your team with confidence, setting the tone for service excellence, and ensuring that every guest feels welcomed, understood, and cared for.   What you’ll do Oversee all Front Office operations, including Reception, Concierge, and Guest Services Lead, train, and inspire the Front Office team to deliver exceptional and personalized service Ensure a seamless check-in and check-out experience, room assignments, and reservation coordination Maintain a strong presence in the lobby, engaging with guests and proactively addressing their needs Monitor guest feedback, handle concerns professionally, and implement service improvements Collaborate closely with Housekeeping, F&B, Sales, and other departments to ensure a unified guest journey Prepare and manage departmental budgets, ensuring cost control and operational efficiency Ensure full compliance with hotel policies, procedures, and health & safety standards   Your Uniqueness is Welcome We believe great Front Office Managers are more than operational experts — they are hosts, mentors, and problem solvers. If you thrive in guest interaction, enjoy leading diverse teams, and take pride in creating memorable experiences, you’ll feel right at home with us. We’re looking for someone who: Has proven experience as a Front Office Manager or in a similar leadership role within luxury hospitality Demonstrates strong leadership, multitasking, and problem-solving skills Is proficient in PMS systems (preferably Protel) Possesses excellent organizational and communication abilities Is fluent in English Has a genuine passion for service excellence and guest satisfaction   Why Join Us? A supportive and collaborative work environment Opportunities for career growth within a world-class resort and hotel group Competitive compensation and benefits Accommodation (for resorts) and meals provided Ready to join our community?', 'Εποχιακός/ή');
