nd beverages, maintain stock levels, and contribute to minimizing waste.Promote and upsell food, beverages, and specialty drinks to enhance guest satisfaction and increase revenue.Ensure compliance with all health, safety, and hygiene procedures, maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment.Assist with service across other hotel outlets, events, and in-room dining operations as required.RequirementsMinimum of 2 years of experience in a similar role within five-star hotels or high-volume fine dining venues.Degree or diploma in Tourism, Hospitality, or a related field.Knowledge of wines; experience in wine tasting is considered an advantage.Experience using MICROS or other POS systems is an advantage.Excellent command of English; additional languages are considered an asset. Candidate’s ProfileFlexibility and adaptability to respond effectively to a variety of work situations.Genuine passion for delivering consistently high levels of guest service.Strong negotiation, communication and interpersonal skills.Pleasant, professional, and guest-oriented personality with a positive attitude.BenefitsAt Empiria Group, our hotels are more than workplaces — they are environments where people grow, evolve, and find purpose.Staff accommodation with Wi-Fi and air conditioning.Half-board meal plan (Breakfast & Lunch).Continuous training and development opportunities.Career growth opportunities within Empiria Group and across Marriott International properties worldwide. At Empiria Group we are proud to foster Equal Employment Opportunities regardless of race, color, ethnicity, religion, gender, age, disability, or sexual orientation. All applications are considered strictly confidential. After careful consideration of all the resumes received, we will only contact the candidates who meet the requirements of the job to arrange an interview. ​You provide the Talent!We provide the Space for Opportunity and Growth!', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
