(647683, 'Java Developer-Lottery Solutions (2)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/304095', 'Παιανία', 'πριν 27 λεπτά', '2026-04-08 15:01:10', 'ΙΝΤΡΑΛΟΤ Α.Ε.', 'Join Bally\'s Intralot as a Software Engineer (Java)!Are you a Java Developer looking for an opportunity to work with modern technologies and microservices? Do you thrive in a dynamic environment that fosters innovation and technical excellence? If so, we invite you to join our team!What you\'ll be doing:Contributing to the development and evolution of critical backend systems that support our applications and services.Developing and maintaining web applications in a microservices environment.Writing clean, efficient, and well-documented code.Collaborating with the team to analyze requirements and design solutions.Supporting internal and external customers when needed.Keeping up with the latest technologies and best practices. What we\'re looking for:Degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field.3+ years of experience in Java development.We work with Java 17 and are migrating to Java 21 - so you\'ll have the opportunity to work with the latest technologies!Experience with Spring Boot (currently using 2.6).Understanding of RESTful APIs and microservices architecture.Knowledge of multithreading programming and testing frameworks (JUnit).Experience with databases (MySQL) and ORM frameworks (Hibernate).Familiarity with Source Control (GIT, SVN) and Build Tools (Maven).Knowledge or experience with Kubernetes, Docker, and Kafka.Team player with strong problem-solving skills!About UsBally\'s Intralot is a newly formed company created through the combination of Intralot and Bally\'s International Interactive, positioning the group as a top iGaming operator and a leading global provider of lottery solutions.Operating at the intersection of technology, regulation, and entertainment, Bally\'s Intralot has a strong presence across digital gaming markets, including lottery, iLottery, and sports betting. The company is uniquely positioned to capitalize on global growth trends driven by digital adoption and the expansion of regulated gaming markets worldwide.At Bally\'s Intralot, we Win as One, are Powered by Curiosity, bring Fun with Purpose, Embrace the Possibility, and always Guard the Game.Why Join Us: A competitive compensation package combined with additional benefits. Hybrid working model. Private Insurance for you and your family. Modern facilities, parking inside, enticing restaurant and corporate bus. An extensive training program upon induction and throughout employment. Exceptional opportunities to learn and develop in a multinational environment. Prospects for professional growth both locally and globally.Equal Opportunity Employer: We celebrate diversity and are proud to be an Equal Opportunity Employer. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds and do not discriminate based on race, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, national origin, age, marital status, medical condition, disability, or any other protected status. Our premises in Paiania, Attica, are accessible to individuals with disabilities. Join us in shaping the future of gaming and lottery solutions!', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(647684, 'Program Management, Principal', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/304096?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 10 λεπτά', '2026-04-08 15:01:12', 'Metlen Energy & Metals', 'At METLEN Energy & Metals, we are catalysts for a sustainable future, positioned at the forefront of the energy transition while being a reference point for competitive green metallurgy at both the European and global levels. We are a global industrial and energy company operating across two highly interconnected and complementary sectors: Energy and Metals. With a consolidated turnover of €5,683 million and an EBITDA of €1,080 million, along with a workforce of over 7,627 dedicated individuals, we drive success through cutting-edge technology and diverse talent.We are committed to embracing new state-of-the-art technologies and advancements, propelling us towards a cleaner, brighter tomorrow. Our positive footprint extends across five continents, creating a lasting impact. At METLEN, we foster a culture of resilience, challenge, respect, excellence, and change, empowering our diverse workforce to achieve remarkable outcomes.Job Description Program Management, Principal 08/04/2026 Job Description: We are looking for a Program Management Principal to join our team and play a key role in the design, execution, and monitoring of strategic transformation programs. Reporting to the Transformation Office Director, you will drive cross-functional initiatives, ensure governance and delivery excellence, and contribute to the continuous improvement of transformation processes across the organization.Your role will encompass:Support the design and structuring of transformation programs, including initiative portfolios and governance modelsDevelop and maintain program roadmaps, tracking progress through KPIs and performance dashboardsMonitor execution and ensure alignment with strategic objectives and timelinesEstablish and manage program governance cadence (e.g. weekly meetings, SteerCos), including preparation of materialsLead end-to-end execution of projects and initiatives driven by the Transformation OfficeCoordinate cross-functional teams and ensure effective resource allocationCollect, analyze, and interpret data to support decision-making and project deliveryDevelop detailed action plans and track implementation progressManage external partners and third parties where applicableDrive stakeholder communication, including senior leadership and C-level executivesContribute to continuous improvement initiatives, including process optimization and use of technology/ AI toolsWhat You Bring to the Role:Bachelor\'s degree in Engineering, Business, or Economics; Master\'s degree is a plus4+ years in transformation office, strategy or PMO roles in multinational companies (ideally within the energy and industrial goods space)2+ years of experience in management consulting; experience in transformation programs and large-scale PMOProficiency in MS Office tools (Excel, PowerPoint, Word)Familiarity with AI tools (e.g. Microsoft Copilot) is considered an assetFluency in English; additional languages (e.g. French, Spanish, Italian) are a plusStrong analytical and problem-solving skills with a structured and strategic mindsetAbility to manage multiple priorities and work effectively in dynamic, fast-paced environmentsProven stakeholder management skills, with the ability to interact confidently with senior leadershipTeam player with the ability to lead and collaborate across cross-functional teamsShare the same Value Based Behaviors: People & Personal growth Results orientation & Safety excellence Collaboration & Trust Empathy & Effective communication Flexibility & Adaptability Your Benefits: Competitive remuneration package Ticket Restaurant Card Group Health Insurance Plan Preferential household electricity plan Pension PlanFollow us on LinkedIn and stay updated on our latest newsWe respect your personal data. All personal information in your application and CV will remain strictly confidential. At Metlen Energy & Metals we are proud to have Diversity and Inclusion at the centre of everything we do. We are committed to Equal Employment Opportunity regardless of race, colour, national origin, ethnicity, gender, age, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or religion.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(647685, 'Senior IT Billing Engineer', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/304093?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-08 15:01:12', 'Metlen Energy & Metals', 'At METLEN Energy & Metals, we are catalysts for a sustainable future, positioned at the forefront of the energy transition while being a reference point for competitive green metallurgy at both the European and global levels. We are a global industrial and energy company operating across two highly interconnected and complementary sectors: Energy and Metals. With a consolidated turnover of €5,683 million and an EBITDA of €1,080 million, along with a workforce of over 7,627 dedicated individuals, we drive success through cutting-edge technology and diverse talent.We are committed to embracing new state-of-the-art technologies and advancements, propelling us towards a cleaner, brighter tomorrow. Our positive footprint extends across five continents, creating a lasting impact. At METLEN, we foster a culture of resilience, challenge, respect, excellence, and change, empowering our diverse workforce to achieve remarkable outcomes.Job Description Senior IT Billing Engineer 07/04/2026 Job Description: We are currently looking for an IT Billing Engineer to join our Information Technology & Digital Strategy team, based in Athens, Greece.As part of the team, you will support the development, maintenance, and optimization of billing systems, ensuring accuracy, performance, and continuous improvement of billing-related processes.Your role will encompass:Develop well-designed, efficient, and testable code to support billing system functionalities.Manage billing operations, performing validations, checks, and corrections where necessary.Participate in UAT and QAT processes for billing system enhancements and changes.Translate business requirements into functional specifications and collaborate with third-party developers for implementation.Integrate software components into fully functional systems and ensure smooth operation.Develop and execute software testing and quality assurance procedures.Maintain and update system documentation and ensure software is aligned with latest features and standards.Troubleshoot, debug, and upgrade existing billing systems.Identify opportunities to optimize and enhance billing processes and systems.Provide 3rd level support for billing-related issues and customer care escalations.Participate in ad hoc IT and business projects.What you bring to the role:Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related field.Master\'s degree in Finance or Banking will be considered an asset.5+ years of experience in IT Billing or a similar role, ideally within the retail or utilities sector.Strong knowledge of relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL); familiarity with non-relational databases is a plus.Experience in JavaScript development and solid understanding of software development principles.Good understanding of software design patterns and system architecture.Familiarity with software engineering tools and practices.Strong analytical and problem-solving skills.Proficiency in English (written and spoken). Your Benefits:Competitive remuneration packageTicket Restaurant CardGroup Health Insurance PlanPreferential household electricity planPension Plan Follow us on LinkedIn and stay updated on our latest newsWe respect your personal data. All personal information in your application and CV will remain strictly confidential. At Metlen Energy & Metals we are proud to have Diversity and Inclusion at the centre of everything we do. We are committed to Equal Employment Opportunity regardless of race, colour, national origin, ethnicity, gender, age, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or religion.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(647686, 'Senior AC Technician', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/retail-jobs/304099?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-08 15:01:14', 'Κωτσόβολος', 'At Kotsovolos, we believe in your uniqueness and everything you have to offer!Here, you create your own current!📈 Our achievements in numbers3,000+ People | 100+ Stores | 2 Logistics Centers - 77.000 sqm | 2 Call Centers | 2 Modern Training Centers | Kapaskill - our live, personalized learning ecosystem | 75,000+ hours of training per year | 400+ different roles & 49 Business Units🎯 Our purposeBetter Living. Everywhere. for Everyone!💼 Your everyday work-life Installing, maintaining and repairing AC and HVAC units, especially Heat Pumps Troubleshooting and determining of causes of operating errors Conducting tests and inspections of products, services or processes to evaluate quality or performance Determining the relative costs of repair procedures Refurbishing MDA products Checking of DOA products to justify the return cause Evaluating installation defects on HVAC/Heat Pumps projects 🚀 As an ideal fit, you should have 3+ years of relevant work experience as an Electrician, A/C repairer or Heat Pump installer/repairer Technical degree from a relative technical institute Proficiency with electrical testing equipment Experience with ERP/SAP/Dynamic systems (work order system experience will be ideal) Excellent communication skills Strong troubleshooting and problem solving skills Advanced computer literacy (MS Office) 💎 What we offer Continuous training in new technologies and tools Career development and growth opportunities Competitive bonus scheme, performance-based Group health/medical insurance package Internal wellbeing actions ⭐ Join #teamKotsovolos and be part of a team that promotes new technologies, loves to evolve, embraces diversity and is next to society!', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
