es. Managing raw materials and organizing the production station. Supporting kitchen organization and daily replenishment. Complying with hygiene, safety, and HACCP standards. Supervising and guiding junior staff when required. Collaborating with the team to optimize production processes and ensure smooth kitchen operations.   Qualifications Previous experience (minimum 2 years) in a similar role within a 5* hotel environment. Degree from a Culinary School, Tourism or Gastronomy Studies, or a related field. Excellent knowledge of food preparation and presentation techniques. Attention to detail, creativity, and passion for high-quality gastronomy.   Benefits Double accommodation. 2 meals daily. Continuous training and professional development opportunities. Stable and structured working environment within a growing hotel group. All applications will be treated with absolute confidentiality. After careful evaluation of the CVs, we will contact only the candidates who meet the requirements of the position. #bettertogether #workforall', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
