(648327, 'Security & Connectivity Presales Engineer', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/security-jobs/304508?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 31 λεπτά', '2026-04-09 15:00:55', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doThe job holder will be responsible for designing Security and Connectivity solutions such as Next Generation Firewall, SASE, SD-WAN, and SD-LAN, aligning them with customers\' requirements. Additionally, they will describe and present these solutions\' design and deployment plans. Will work closely with a wide network of partners, manage key accounts and vendors, and propose solutions. Design and propose state-of-the-art solutions for Security, SASE, SD-WAN, and SD-LAN that best address customer needs. Perform customer visits, lead the technical discussion, prepare the solution design and technical presentations, in collaboration with other technical teams, and direct feedback from the customer. Manage and coordinate Vodafone\'s sub-contractors to bring the appropriate technical solution on time. Participation and ownership of Customer\'s RFPs. It is important to keep up with the latest Security and Connectivity technology trends to be able to introduce and train internally about new products or solutions accordingly. Who you areThe candidate for this position must have at least 3 years of relevant experience in business customer engineering, Security, or Connectivity Presales. Additionally, should have a university degree in IT or Telecom and more than one certification on the following Vendors Cisco or Huawei (CCNP level preferred), Fortinet (Professional or higher), Vmware (VMware SD-WAN Foundations), Checkpoint (CCSA or higher), HPE Aruba certifications or any other relevant certification. A Master\'s degree will be considered as a plus.Inspired to effectively communicate in technical and commercial terms and explain the benefits of technology proposals with excellent command of written and spoken Greek and English language.Proficient in effectively managing large-scale projects utilizing cutting-edge technology.Passion for continuous learning of new Security and Connectivity technologies and staying up to date with technological trends.Ability to understand the customer\'s IT operation model and in collaboration with Security and Connectivity products to propose transformation and security solutions. Not a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youAward-winning work environment -certified #1 Top Employer in GreeceCompetitive pay, bonus & remuneration packagePrivate Health & Medical InsuranceHybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroadUnlimited access to learning resources and trainingsVodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of serviceSpirit of Vodafone Day: one day each quarter dedicated to your personal developmentExtra days off: Vodafone Day, Family Day, Volunteering DayOffice amenities (subject to the office location): such as restaurant, beauty corner, gym and parkingSpecial employee offers and discountsWho we areWe are a leading international Telco, serving millions of customers. At Vodafone, we believe that connectivity is a force for good. If we use it for the things that really matter, it can improve people\'s lives and the world around us. Through our technology we empower people, connecting everyone regardless of who they are or where they live and we protect the planet, whilst helping our customers do the same.Belonging at Vodafone isn\'t a concept; it\'s lived, breathed, and cultivated through everything we do. You\'ll be part of a global and diverse community, with many different minds, abilities, backgrounds and cultures. ;We\'re committed to increase diversity, ensure equal representation, and make Vodafone a place everyone feels safe, valued and included.If you require any reasonable adjustments or have an accessibility request as part of your recruitment journey, for example, extended time or breaks in between online assessments, please refer to https://careers.vodafone.com/application-adjustments/ for guidance.Together we can.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(648328, 'Senior Campaign Specialist', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/304506?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 5 λεπτά', '2026-04-09 15:00:55', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doThe Senior Campaign Specialist plays a pivotal role in delivering Vodafone\'s always-on marketing vision by owning and shaping the decisioning and contact strategy that transforms briefs into automated customer journeys and maximizes customer value across the lifecycle, supporting the implementation of household value management within the PEGA platform. The role ensures scalable, relevant customer engagement by combining customer insights, segmentation and advanced decisioning and channel orchestration rules. Key AccountabilitiesOwn the design and evolution of automated, always-on customer journeys by translating campaign briefs and strategic commercial priorities into scalable decisioning logic within the PEGA platform.Act as a strategic bridge between business needs and platform, working closely with the PEGA Product Owner, CVM, Base Growth, Digital, and Product teams to critically assess and refine briefs, converting commercial priorities into robust campaign strategies, segmentation frameworks, and decision rules. Lead collaboration with Technology for Delivery Excellence by engaging the PEGA Technology team to clarify requirements, support testing, and ensure timely acceptance and rollout of new features and platform enhancements. Own execution, monitoring & optimization of always-on campaigns by delivering campaigns based on CVM principles that cover hypothesis-driven logic, A/B testing, incrementality measurement, control groups definition and successful campaign roll-out across digital & offline touchpoints with clear accountability for performance and business impact. Own Day-to-Day Configuration that includes Data, Product, Offers and Channel Catalog configurations and alterations in PEGA, while ensuring cross-channel consistency in collaboration with CBU key stakeholders and PEGA Technology team Who you areMSc or BSc in Statistics, Information Systems, Engineering, or Business Studies, with a strong analytical mindset and passion for data-driven decision-making.3+ years of experience in customer behavior analysis, CVM or decisioning roles, with proven ownership of complex always-on use cases across Physical & Digital channels and hands-on experience with marketing automation platforms/Hands-on experience with marketing automation platforms is required, with expertise or prior experience in PEGA, Unica, Salesforce, Adobe, or similar tools strongly preferred. Proven ability to work with multiple data sources, advanced SQL knowledge and strong technical fluency in marketing automation, resulting in scalable, personalized, trigger-based customer journeys.Experience working in agile teams, with adaptability and a proactive mindset to contribute to iterative delivery.Strong communication and stakeholder engagement, analytical thinking, creative problem-solving, and effective time management with attention to detail. Not a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youAward-winning work environment -certified #1 Top Employer in GreeceCompetitive pay, bonus & remuneration packagePrivate Health & Medical InsuranceHybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroadUnlimited access to learning resources and trainingsVodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of serviceSpirit of Vodafone Day: one day each quarter dedicated to your personal developmentExtra days off: Vodafone Day, Family Day, Volunteering DayOffice amenities (subject to the office location): such as restaurant, beauty corner, gym and parkingSpecial employee offers and discountsWho we areWe are a leading international Telco, serving millions of customers. At Vodafone, we believe that connectivity is a force for good. If we use it for the things that really matter, it can improve people\'s lives and the world around us. Through our technology we empower people, connecting everyone regardless of who they are or where they live and we protect the planet, whilst helping our customers do the same.Belonging at Vodafone isn\'t a concept; it\'s lived, breathed, and cultivated through everything we do. You\'ll be part of a global and diverse community, with many different minds, abilities, backgrounds and cultures. ;We\'re committed to increase diversity, ensure equal representation, and make Vodafone a place everyone feels safe, valued and included.If you require any reasonable adjustments or have an accessibility request as part of your recruitment journey, for example, extended time or breaks in between online assessments, please refer to https://careers.vodafone.com/application-adjustments/ for guidance.Together we can.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(648329, 'Join us | General Job Application', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/304499?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 19 λεπτά', '2026-04-09 15:00:57', 'Vodafone', 'About Vodafone:At Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.Thanks for your interest in Vodafone Greece! Here, we are all about new opportunities, continuous growth and making an impact for a better future.Submit your CV to join our talent pool. This allows us to match your profile with future opportunities. We are always on the lookout for new talent.What\'s in it for you at Vodafone:Award-winning work environment -certified #1 Top Employer in GreeceCompetitive pay, bonus & remuneration packagePrivate Health & Medical InsuranceHybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroadUnlimited connectivity with our mobile, landline and Vodafone TV services - Experience first what our customers loveUnlimited access to learning resources and trainingsVodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of serviceRemote work equipment to help you create a comfortable, ergonomic workspace at homeSpirit of Vodafone days: dedicated time to pause, develop new skills and connect with our teams, values and servicesExtra days off: Vodafone Day, Family Day, Volunteering DayOffice amenities (subject to the office location): such as restaurant, beauty corner, gym and parkingSpecial employee offers and discountsYou can always find all our open vacancies here.Come as you are! At Vodafone, we pride ourselves on having built an open and inclusive environment which enables you to thrive. A place where you can grow and develop alongside the best minds in the business, where you can harness the power of technology to make a real, tangible difference to communities big and small.Follow us on social media: Facebook, Instagram, LinkedIn.#LI-Hybrid #Vodafonespirit #Togetherwecan #TogetherIsGreat', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(648330, 'Quality Assurance Chapter Lead', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/quality-assurance-jobs/304496?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 7 λεπτά', '2026-04-09 15:00:57', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doThe QA Chapter Lead is the Product Owner of Skills Development, who builds expertise in the chapter and develops chapter members. Enthusiastic about transferring knowledge to others, coaching and oversee personal development. Responsible to create the Strategy of Testing & maintain the backlog of the chapter, thus will contribute in designing and implementing Vodafone\'s high volume and high impact digital and core it channels/platforms. Ensures knowledge transfer within chapter and boost innovation in testing practices. More specifically you will: Guide a community of Experts that are working within squads Allocating resources based on seniority and priority across organization. Work with the Tribe and Tech Lead to provide workforce plans for recruitment and development Organises interactions between the members of the chapter to nurture best practice and encourage knowledge & tool sharing Act as a supporting leader, rather than a line manager, aiming at maturing the organisation readiness, vs. controlling the work Provides guidance and harmonization of chapter best-practices (Chapter principles) Acts as a mentor for Expert members of the chapter, helping them grow in expertise and experience new areas Play a pivotal role in inspiring and motivating everyone in the chapter to be the best they can be Ensure technical integrity and quality control consistency throughout the development life cycle Own test architecture, review test code, and ensure compliance to industry best practices Understand functional requirements and help creating user stories with testability in mind Responsible to identify and improve Processes for Testing across OrganizationsWho you areAt least 5 years of experience in QA Engineering role (3 of which in Automation) Have a passion for personal and functional development, supporting members to be the best they can be Agility and willingness to track, assess, and incorporate practice and technology developments into day-to-day working Looks externally /brings in best practices, experiments, tests, pushes innovation Able to foster learning around agile ways of working and the overall agile mind-set Strong relationship building, persuasion, and collaboration skills, acting as enabler for coordination of activities between technical teams and building of cross-functional relationships quickly and confidently Solid understanding of both object-oriented programming and scripting languages Experience with version control systems (GitHub, GitLab, etc.),performance, load, and test testing Expert: a) in Continuous Integration / Deployment design, b) with testing tools and practices on every level in the test pyramid (unit, component, integration) Can apply a range of techniques to support facilitation, training, coaching and mentoring to guide and manage a group event to ensure that objectives are met effectively Clear and effective communication skills in English (written and verbal) Opensource contributing will be considered a plus Not a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youCompetitive pay, bonus & remuneration package Private Health & Medical Insurance Hybrid way of working: a blend of 60% remote and 40% office-based working, including the option to work up to 20 days from abroad Unlimited connectivity with our mobile, landline and Vodafone TV services - Experience first what our customers love Unlimited access to learning resources and trainings Vodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of service Remote work equipment to help you create a comfortable, ergonomic workspace at home Spirit of Vodafone days: dedicated time to pause, develop new skills and connect with our teams, values and services Extra days off: Vodafone Day, Family Day, Volunteering Day Office amenities (subject to the office location): such as restaurant, beauty corner, gym and parking Special employee offers and discounts Who we areWe are a leading international Telco, serving millions of customers. At Vodafone, we believe that connectivity is a force for good. If we use it for the things that really matter, it can improve people\'s lives and the world around us. Through our technology we empower people, connecting everyone regardless of who they are or where they live and we protect the planet, whilst helping our customers do the same.Belonging at Vodafone isn\'t a concept; it\'s lived, breathed, and cultivated through everything we do. You\'ll be part of a global and diverse community, with many different minds, abilities, backgrounds and cultures. ;We\'re committed to increase diversity, ensure equal representation, and make Vodafone a place everyone feels safe, valued and included.If you require any reasonable adjustments or have an accessibility request as part of your recruitment journey, for example, extended time or breaks in between online assessments, please refer to https://careers.vodafone.com/application-adjustments/ for guidance.Together we can.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(648331, 'Senior Data Analyst', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/bi-or-business-analysis-jobs/304514?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 9 λεπτά', '2026-04-09 15:00:59', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doAs a Senior Data & Analytics Analyst you will be member of the Data & Analytics (ie D&A) Business Performance Agile squad, a cross-functional team handling end 2 end the Data needs of Vodafone Greece. You will be responsible for the design, build and maintenance of Data and Analytics products.Key Accountabilities:Deliver timely and accurately company performance reports and ensure local D&A environment is fit for purposeAnalyse and prioritize stakeholder needs; support team during the product roll outLead the design and build reporting, serviced in a Digital and Visualized mannerPerform reconciliations on various data sources to assure data integritySupport and guide junior team members, promoting best practises in analytics and reporting developmentExecute ad-hoc and scheduled analysis - data mining - to produce actionable resultsContribute to continuous improvements of data products, analytical methodologies and reporting standardsLead discussions related to analyses, insights, and recommendations with technical and business audiencesWho you areYou have strong understanding of Data Warehousing Analytics and Visualization concepts and best practicesYou are proficient with SQL, Data Modelling (priority on LookML), Business Intelligence (priority on SAP BO), Visualization (priority on Looker), Data Mining (priority on Python), as well as collaboration tools (Jira, Confluence)You demonstrate strong analytical thinking and can independently solve complex business problemsYou have professional experience of interacting with stakeholders and translating business needs into analytical solutionsYou are familiar with Agile practicesYou have experience supervising and providing directions to junior data analystsYou have fluency in EnglishYou have a background in Data Analytics and, ideally, you have four or more years of experience in relative areasNot a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youAward-winning work environment -certified #1 Top Employer in GreeceCompetitive pay, bonus & remuneration packagePrivate Health & Medical InsuranceHybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroadUnlimited access to learning resources and trainingsVodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of serviceSpirit of Vodafone Day: one day each quarter dedicated to your personal developmentExtra days off: Vodafone Day, Family Day, Volunteering DayOffice amenities (subject to the office location): such as restaurant, beauty corner, gym and parkingSpecial employee offers and discountsWho we areWe are a leading international Telco, serving millions of customers. At Vodafone, we believe that connectivity is a force for good. If we use it for the things that really matter, it can improve people\'s lives and the world around us. Through our technology we empower people, connecting everyone regardless of who they are or where they live and we protect the planet, whilst helping our customers do the same.Belonging at Vodafone isn\'t a concept; it\'s lived, breathed, and cultivated through everything we do. You\'ll be part of a global and diverse community, with many different minds, abilities, backgrounds and cultures. ;We\'re committed to increase diversity, ensure equal representation, and make Vodafone a place everyone feels safe, valued and included.If you require any reasonable adjustments or have an accessibility request as part of your recruitment journey, for example, extended time or breaks in between online assessments, please refer to https://careers.vodafone.com/application-adjustments/ for guidance.Together we can.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(648332, 'ICT Presales Solutions Engineer', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/sales-or-business-development-or-account-management-jobs/304493?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 4 λεπτά', '2026-04-09 15:00:59', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doThe job holder will perform Presales solutions design and operation of Vodafone ICT Services for private sector customers. The job holder will be able to develop expertise in new technologies & services and work closely with a wide network of key accounts and vendors.Design, operate, and propose the appropriate IaaS (Public - Private Cloud) & SaaS solutions that best address customer needs.Perform customer visits lead the technical discussion, prepare the sales offers and technical presentations, and follow up on any open points with customers, to get the sales orders executed.Market monitoring and investigation for potential new solutions that can be developed, based on strong market, customer, and Solution Sales insights.Liaise thoroughly with internal and external business partners, combining technical advice to design and fulfil the best possible ROI for the customer\'s IT estate.It is important to keep up with the latest technology trends to be able to introduce and train internal about new products or solutions accordinglyWho you areThe candidate for this position must have a minimum of 3 years of relevant experience in ICT business customer engineering or ICT Presales. Additionally, should have a university degree in IT or Telecom and certifications in Microsoft Azure (such as AZ-104, AZ-305, SC-100, MS-102), or any other relevant field.Ability to understand the customer\'s IT operation model and propose, in technical terms, the migration to dedicated computing, colocation, Private Cloud, Public Cloud services & solutions.Inspired to effectively communicate technical and commercial terms and explain the benefits of cloud economics with excellent command of the written and spoken Greek and English language.Passion for continuous learning of new technologies and stay current with the latest Cloud services & solutions.Self-drive and commitment to create awareness, consideration, and adoption of innovative services and solutions.Not a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youAward-winning work environment -certified #1 Top Employer in GreeceCompetitive pay, bonus & remuneration packagePrivate Health & Medical InsuranceHybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroadUnlimited connectivity with our mobile, landline and Vodafone TV services - Experience first what our customers loveUnlimited access to learning resources and trainingsVodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of serviceWho we areWe are a leading international Telco, serving millions of customers. At Vodafone, we believe that connectivity is a force for good. If we use it for the things that really matter, it can improve people\'s lives and the world around us. Through our technology we empower people, connecting everyone regardless of who they are or where they live and we protect the planet, whilst helping our customers do the same.Belonging at Vodafone isn\'t a concept; it\'s lived, breathed, and cultivated through everything we do. You\'ll be part of a global and diverse community, with many different minds, abilities, backgrounds and cultures. ;We\'re committed to increase diversity, ensure equal representation, and make Vodafone a place everyone feels safe, valued and included.If you require any reasonable adjustments or have an accessibility request as part of your recruitment journey, for example, extended time or breaks in between online assessments, please refer to https://careers.vodafone.com/application-adjustments/ for guidance.Together we can.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(648333, 'Telecom Presales Engineer', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/sales-or-business-development-or-account-management-jobs/304483?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-09 15:01:01', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doThe job holder will be responsible for designing Security and Connectivity solutions such as Next Generation Firewall, SASE, SD-WAN, and SD-LAN, aligning them with customers\' requirements. Additionally, they will describe and present these solutions\' design and deployment plans. Will work closely with a wide network of partners, manage key accounts and vendors, and propose solutions.• Design and propose state-of-the-art solutions for Security, SASE, SD-WAN, and SD-LAN that best address customer needs.• Perform customer visits, lead the technical discussion, prepare the solution design and technical presentations, in collaboration with other technical teams, and direct feedback from the customer.• Manage and coordinate Vodafone\'s sub-contractors to bring the appropriate technical solution on time.• Participation and ownership of Customer\'s RFPs.• It is important to keep up with the latest Security and Connectivity technology trends to be able to introduce and train internally about new products or solutions accordingly.Who you are• The candidate for this position must have at least 3 years of relevant experience in business customer engineering, Security, or Connectivity Presales. Additionally, should have a university degree in IT or Telecom and more than one certification on the following Vendors Cisco or Huawei (CCNP level preferred), Fortinet (Professional or higher), Vmware (VMware SD-WAN Foundations), Checkpoint (CCSA or higher), HPE Aruba certifications or any other relevant certification. A Master\'s degree will be considered as a plus.• Inspired to effectively communicate in technical and commercial terms and explain the benefits of technology proposals with excellent command of written and spoken Greek and English language.• Proficient in effectively managing large-scale projects utilizing cutting-edge technology.• Passion for continuous learning of new Security and Connectivity technologies and staying up to date with technological trends.• Ability to understand the customer\'s IT operation model and in collaboration with Security and Connectivity products to propose transformation and security solutions.Not a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youAward-winning work environment -certified #1 Top Employer in Greece Competitive pay, bonus & remuneration package Private Health & Medical Insurance Hybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroad Unlimited connectivity with our mobile, landline and Vodafone TV services - Experience first what our customers love Unlimited access to learning resources and trainings Vodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of service Remote work equipment to help you create a comfortable, ergonomic workspace at home Spirit of Vodafone days: dedicated time to pause, develop new skills and connect with our teams, values and services Extra days off: Vodafone Day, Family Day, Volunteering Day Office amenities (subject to the office location): such as restaurant, beauty corner, gym and parking Special employee offers and discounts #LI-Hybrid #Vodafonespirit #Togetherwecan Who we areWe are a leading international Telco, serving millions of customers. At Vodafone, we believe that connectivity is a force for good. If we use it for the things that really matter, it can improve people\'s lives and the world around us. Through our technology we empower people, connecting everyone regardless of who they are or where they live and we protect the planet, whilst helping our customers do the same.Belonging at Vodafone isn\'t a concept; it\'s lived, breathed, and cultivated through everything we do. You\'ll be part of a global and diverse community, with many different minds, abilities, backgrounds and cultures. ;We\'re committed to increase diversity, ensure equal representation, and make Vodafone a place everyone feels safe, valued and included.If you require any reasonable adjustments or have an accessibility request as part of your recruitment journey, for example, extended time or breaks in between online assessments, please refer to https://careers.vodafone.com/application-adjustments/ for guidance.Together we can.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
