(648336, 'Field Services Technician (Crete)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/call-center-or-customer-support-jobs/304511?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 7 λεπτά', '2026-04-09 15:01:03', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doThe role is responsible for taking care of all Field Services requests for Corporate Customer in various facilities. Managing on-site installation, repair, maintenance, system improvement and testing. Providing service and customer support during visits or dispatches. Key accountabilities and decision ownership: Evaluate customer infrastructure, confirm that the correct solution is offered to the Business CustomersPerform customer support and troubleshooting tasks for Business Services. Perform all on-site activities related to installation, repair, management and maintenance. Operate field automation systems and databases. Write logs and add notes to customer records of every Field Service managed and / or call to customers performed. Demonstrate equipment capabilities to customers and demonstrate how to perform various tasks, including simple maintenance.Manage and maintain the inventory in their service trucks, ordering new items when stock runs low. Adhere to company\'s given rules and regulations. Keep service vehicles clean and organized and replenish fuel as needed. Team up with colleagues and other team members. Build relationships and trust with customers and clientsKey performance indicators: Average Handling of Field Service request per FS type Average Handling FS Time per Service/FS type NPS and TNPS Who you areAt least 2-year experience in a Technical Field Service support department.At least Technical Institution degree.Experience with managing and preserving technical equipmentCritical thinker and problem-solving skillsExcellent communication skills.Strong customer orientation attitude.Take initiative, being alerted, have a sense of urgency.Good knowledge of fixed products & ICT services.Responsible for providing technical support (L1/L2/L3) for SD-WAN and Firewall-as-a-Service environments Accustomed to using mobile tools and applicationsStrong experience in SD-WAN design, deployment, and optimization across multi-site and hybrid cloud environments Must have technical/professional qualifications: Very good knowledge of Greek and English language (oral and written).CCNA Certification similar technical trainingHands-on expertise with leading SD-WAN platforms Good knowledge of MS Office Suite (MS Excel, MS Word etc.).Not a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youAward-winning work environment -certified #1 Top Employer in Greece Competitive pay, bonus & remuneration package Private Health & Medical Insurance Hybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroad Unlimited connectivity with our mobile, landline and Vodafone TV services - Experience first what our customers love Unlimited access to learning resources and trainings Vodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of service Spir