to develop new skills, rotate in different roles based on your career path, work on business-critical and experimentation projects and have a personalised learning journey for you, in a fully inclusive working environment.Here at Vodafone, we do amazing things to keep our people, customers and society connected: from providing superfast network speed to smartphones, to making our Business clients and their businesses smart with cloud services, fleet & cooler controls, or streaming music into a car through the internet of things. Benefit your career growth from a global and diverse network of leaders and shape innovative solutions that impact customers and society. Our global scale and strategy provide countless challenges and experiences that will stretch your skills and keep you excited.Stay connected: Vodafone Greece Career page, Facebook , LinkedIn#LI-Hybrid #VodafoneGreece #Togetherwecan', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(648351, 'Landlord Operations Specialist (m/f/d) for Vantage Towers', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/operations-jobs/304519?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-09 15:01:19', 'Vodafone', 'At Vantage Towers, we\'re on a mission to power Europe\'s sustainable digital transformation. As a leading tower company, we\'re ushering in an era of technology-driven advances to help connect people, businesses, and internet-enabled devices like never before. We combine the scale, stability, and quality of our tower network with the agility, optimism, and energy of a start-up.As a young TowerCo, we have already achieved strong results with a continued focus on accelerating growth and a special emphasis put on sustainability. As part of our team, you\'ll work in a dynamic and multicultural environment that embraces open communication, collaboration, and teamwork. If you\'re ready to take responsibility and shape the future of telco infrastructure with us, then let\'s level up in your career and reach the top - together.Your contribution:You build and maintain long-term relationships with property owners who host telecommunications infrastructure, contractors, customers, and public service entitiesYou ensure 24/7 site accessibility, including key management and access procedures, to support timely execution of field projects and maintenance activitiesYou negotiate lease contract renewals and manage all lease-related matters, including handling requests, inquiries, renewals, documentation and updates to commercial and technical termsYou collaborate with legal and technical departments to resolve issues related to usage rights, access, and technical interventionsYou provide timely and comprehensive documentation to support legal proceedings involving property owners, neighbors, or public authoritiesYou monitor and report on key performance indicators (KPIs) to support strategic planning and decision-makingYou ensure data security and confidentiality across all activities and communicationsWhat makes you stand out:Bachelor\'s degree in Economics, Business Administration, or a related fieldProven experience in client relationship management, ideally within the telecommunications and/or real estate sectorsStrong negotiation and conflict resolution skills, with a professional, diplomatic, and collaborative approachHands-on experience with ERP/SAP systems and proficiency in Microsoft Office SuiteExcellent written and verbal communication skills in both Greek and EnglishWhat we offer:A diverse, multicultural setup based on our values - accountability, respect, teamwork, and trust - and the opportunity to shape the organizationAttractive salary and bonus planPrivate medical insurance, including dependentsMobile plan with unlimited talk time and dataFood allowanceParking slotFlexible working arrangements, actively supporting caring for family members', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(648352, '2026 Discover Graduate Program Greece | Corporate Business', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/304503?origin=pjp', 'Φουρνάς', 'πριν 29 λεπτά', '2026-04-09 15:01:21', 'Vodafone', 'Discover Graduate Program Greece | Corporate BusinessJoin our Discover Graduate Program and shape your career in a global technology and communications company committed to creating a better future for everyone.When & Where:Duration of Program: 2 years, aiming at a permanent renewal upon completionLocation: Athens (Hybrid)Areas you could be working in include:• Human Resources Management • Finance• Legal• Corporate AffairsThe teams you could join per area:The area of Human Resources includes: Learning and Development, Talent Management, Reward, Organisational Development, Resourcing, Business Partnering, Internal Communication, Employer Branding TeamsThe area of Finance includes: Corporate Finance, Financial Planning, Mergers & Acquisitions, Finance Operations/Accounting TeamsThe area of Legal & Corporate Affairs includes: Legal, Regulatory, External Communications, Corporate Security, Foundation and Sustainability TeamsWhat we\'re looking for:• Recently graduated - BSc or MSc degree preferably in Finance/Accounting, HR or Legal/Law studies • Strong academic performance • 0-2 years of experience • English & Greek proficient • Curiosity and learning agility • Passion for technology and digital experiencesWhat\'s in it for you:• Hybrid Way of Working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work up to 20 days from abroad • Investment in your personal development• Having business exposure and accountability from day one• Being part of a global community of graduates• Competitive pay & benefits• Working with a global community to deliver world-leading technology to empower customers around the world connect and build our digital futureWhat to expect:• Gain critical experiences, stretch your skills and thrive • Opportunities to rotate in different roles based on your career path• Personalised learning journey and skills development to ensure you\'ll always be future-ready • Continuous feedback and support on how to meet your career goals• A diverse and inclusive working environment where you can be yourself, share inspiration and belong• An agile environment where you can work with flexibility and the freedom to experiment and innovate• A rewarding workplace with practices, initiatives and policies to support your health, safety and wellbeing.If you think this sounds like you, we would love to hear from you.Application ProcessWe are continuing virtual hiring and onboarding processes to ensure a smooth and efficient experience.Step 1: Application form. When you apply for the Vodafone Discover Program you will be asked to fill out an application form. This allows us to get to know you and your background of experience. As part of your application, you will also be required to answer additional pre-screening questions to fully complete your application. Make sure you attach your CV in English.Step 2: Online assessment. If your background and experience match the requirements, you will be invited to participate in our online assessment. This allows us to assess if you are the right fit for the Vodafone culture. Online assessment stage is in English and includes a recorded video interview and gamified cognitive ability tests.Step 3: Virtual assessment center. The most successful candidates will be invited to participate in our virtual assessment center which includes group activities and interviews.Need help? Vodafone is committed to making reasonable adjustments for all candidates considered to have a disability during the recruitment process. In case you have any kind of question, please let us know at the following address: [email protected].About the programThrough the Discover Graduate Program, we are looking for Vodafone\'s future leaders. Those who dream big, innovate with heart and embrace new technologies, and who are continuously learning and exploring the world of opportunity on offer.If you are a young recent graduate with bright ideas, then we\'re brimming with excitement to meet you. From day one, you will join a global community of graduates and you\'ll get the chance to make a real impact in many ways.Kick-start your career by gaining hands-on experience and accelerating your personal development. During the program, you have the opportunity to develop new skills, rotate in different roles based on your career path, work on business-critical and experimentation projects and have a personalised learning journey for you, in a fully inclusive working environment.Here at Vodafone, we do amazing things to keep our people, customers and society connected: from providing superfast network speed to smartphones, to making our Business clients and their businesses smart with cloud services, fleet & cooler controls, or streaming music into a car through the internet of things. Benefit your career growth from a global and diverse network of leaders and shape innovative solutions that impact customers and society. Our global scale and strategy provide countless challenges and experiences that will stretch your skills and keep you excited.Stay connected: Vodafone Greece Career page, Facebook , LinkedIn#LI-Hybrid #VodafoneGreece #Togetherwecan', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(648353, 'Monetization & Charging Senior Engineer', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/304510?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 21 λεπτά', '2026-04-09 15:01:21', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doThe Charging Service implements all the Tariff Plan, Promotions and Regulatory services (such as spending limits, etc) as per Commercial demand and it is therefore made up of a mission critical application, continuously evolved for supporting the stream of Commercial needs for facing the day-by-day competition. From Technology standpoint, a journey towards 5G enablement is in progress moving the legacy service to a complete new, cloud-based application able to support the monetization of the incoming 5G network and services.Role purpose: • Deliver harmonized convergent rating and charging solutions cross markets and cross vendors in line with the architectural and strategic guidelines• Coordinate cross European programs, both for the design phase and for the delivery phase ensuring compliance with deliverables, costs and quality• Research and develop new products and services leveraging the leading technologies of convergent rating and charging, in line with Vodafone Digitalization strategy• Design, Drive and Deliver the Convergent Charging Service (CCS) on Cloud Transformation program in the Market(s), leading CCS to a Cloud, 5G ready system. • Design and Engineer the solution based on Cloud technologies, such as Containers, Open-Source components (Graphana, Kibana), CI/CD (Jenkins, JMeter). • Design and Engineer the software for complying with state-of-the-art Cyber Security guidelines and requirements • Design and Develop backend applications using technologies like JAVA, Python, etc. Designing PoC as well as designing and developing integrations based on opensource components and APIs using CI/CD process (e.g., developing interfaces or protocol for automatic testing tools, developing automatic test scripts, etc)• Owns solution HLD and LLD including IP design. Chooses technologies and standards used for the underlying capabilities. Determines dimensioning and configuration data per node. Ensures security requirements are imbedded in the design.• Design and integrate the new 5G Core with CCS for developing innovative monetization streams. • Drive as Technical Project Manager the delivery projects ensuring a proper coordination of all involved domains (e.g., Infrastructure, Core Network, Operating Support Systems, Provisioning) • Analyse, together with the business demand areas, the needs, requirements and expectations for the definition and implementation of the different functionalities of the CCS projects and commercial productsKey accountabilities and decision ownership • Design, Drive and Deliver the Convergent Charging Service (CCS) cross markets and cross Vendors • Decide and influence the best software architecture for legacy / 5G charging applications.• Design and Implement Capacity Planning for CCS • Lead assigned projects coordinating the involved Technology Providers (aka Vendors) and the relevant VF teams cross markets• Vendors Selection & ManagementWho you areCore competencies, knowledge and experience:• Deep knowledge on IT and network protocols, including 5G SA architecture • Cloud (AWS/Azure/GCP) deployment, Kubernetes, Red Hat• Charging and Rating Services and Digital Services experience• DevOps process and tools (Harbor, Helm, Jenkins, GitLab, JMeter) and Programming skills and experience • Strong experience in managing complex and inter-functional projectsMust have technical / professional qualifications: • MSc/BSc in Computer Science or similar (mandatory)• Fluent in English (mandatory)• Analytical ability, creativity and problem-solving (mandatory)• Knowledge in charging applications• Experience in SOAP, Diameter, Restful API appreciatedNot a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youAward-winning work environment -certified #1 Top Employer in GreeceCompetitive pay, bonus & remuneration packagePrivate Health & Medical InsuranceHybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroadUnlimited access to learning resources and trainingsVodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of serviceSpirit of Vodafone Day: one day each quarter dedicated to your personal developmentExtra days off: Vodafone Day, Family Day, Volunteering DayOffice amenities (subject to the office location): such as restaurant, beauty corner, gym and parkingSpecial employee offers and discountsWho we areWe are a leading international Telco, serving millions of customers. At Vodafone, we believe that connectivity is a force for good. If we use it for the things that really matter, it can improve people\'s lives and the world around us. Through our technology we empower people, connecting everyone regardless of who they are or where they live and we protect the planet, whilst helping our customers do the same.Belonging at Vodafone isn\'t a concept; it\'s lived, breathed, and cultivated through everything we do. You\'ll be part of a global and diverse community, with many different minds, abilities, backgrounds and cultures. ;We\'re committed to increase diversity, ensure equal representation, and make Vodafone a place everyone feels safe, valued and included.If you require any reasonable adjustments or have an accessibility request as part of your recruitment journey, for example, extended time or breaks in between online assessments, please refer to https://careers.vodafone.com/application-adjustments/ for guidance.Together we can.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(648354, 'Release Manager', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/304497?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-09 15:01:23', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doThe Release Manager is responsible for ensuring structured, predictable, and high-quality software releases across multiple systems and teams. The role focuses on release governance, environment coordination, and delivery alignment, while promoting the adoption of modern DevOps and CI/CD practices across the organization. The Release Manager acts as a trusted partner to engineering, QA, and DevOps teams, ensuring that releases are well-planned, risks are managed, and deployments are executed smoothly. More specifically you will: Own end-to-end release management across applications; define policies, standards, and Go/No-Go governance Lead release planning, manage dependencies, risks, and cross-team coordination Develop and maintain release calendars; align business priorities with technical delivery Provide clear visibility into release status, timelines, and risks Govern environment usage (Dev, Test, UAT, Prod) and ensure consistency and stability Coordinate environment synchronization and reduce environment-related release issues Drive CI/CD and DevOps best practices with engineering and DevOps teams Ensure release quality and readiness (test results, rollback plans, deployment procedures) Monitor release performance, incidents, and improve key delivery metrics through post-release reviews Act as central coordination point across Engineering, QA, DevOps, Product, and Operations, building strong stakeholder alignment Who you areComputer Science, Engineering, or relevant background 5+ years of experience in Release Management, DevOps, or Software Delivery Strong understanding of release management processes, governance, and lifecycle Hands-on experience with CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices Experience coordinating complex, cross-team and multi-application releases Solid understanding of environments (Dev, Test, UAT, Production) and deployment flows Strong knowledge of risk, issue, and change management practices Experience with monitoring, reporting, and release performance metrics Excellent communication, stakeholder management, and leadership skills Experience in agile environments; strong English communication (written & verbal); self-motivated and well-organized Fulfilled military services (for male candidates) Not a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youAward-winning work environment - certified #1 Top Employer in GreeceCompetitive pay, bonus & remuneration packagePrivate Health & Medical InsuranceHybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroadUnlimited access to learning resources and trainingsVodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of serviceSpirit of Vodafone Day: one day each quarter dedicated to your personal developmentExtra days off: Vodafone Day, Family Day, Volunteering DayOffice amenities (subject to the office location): such as restaurant, beauty corner, gym and parkingSpecial employee offers and discountsWho we areWe are a leading international Telco, serving millions of customers. At Vodafone, we believe that connectivity is a force for good. If we use it for the things that really matter, it can improve people\'s lives and the world around us. Through our technology we empower people, connecting everyone regardless of who they are or where they live and we protect the planet, whilst helping our customers do the same.Belonging at Vodafone isn\'t a concept; it\'s lived, breathed, and cultivated through everything we do. You\'ll be part of a global and diverse community, with many different minds, abilities, backgrounds and cultures. ;We\'re committed to increase diversity, ensure equal representation, and make Vodafone a place everyone feels safe, valued and included.If you require any reasonable adjustments or have an accessibility request as part of your recruitment journey, for example, extended time or breaks in between online assessments, please refer to https://careers.vodafone.com/application-adjustments/ for guidance.Together we can.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση');
