(648732, '.NET Developer (Senior-Lead)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/295780', 'Πάτρα', 'πριν ένα μήνα', '2026-04-10 07:00:20', 'Netcompany', 'Company DescriptionAre you ready to shape the future technological landscape in Europe?We are dedicated to responsible digitalisation, building innovative, inclusive solutions that drive meaningful impact. With over 8,900 professionals across Europe, we help EU institutions, public and private organisations thrive in a rapidly evolving digital world. Are you ready to shape the future through technology? Your journey starts here. Take a look at some of our impactful projects here: https://netcompany.com/cases/Job DescriptionEver wondered what it feels like to be a .NET Developer (Senior-Lead) in Netcompany? As a .NET Developer (Senior-Lead), you become part of a high-performing team driving enterprise-level digital transformation. This isn\'t just about writing code — it\'s about shaping scalable architectures, influencing technical direction, and delivering solutions that make a real impact.You\'ll work on complex, mission-critical systems where performance, maintainability, and architectural quality are non-negotiable. As a senior team member, you\'ll lead by example, mentor others, and ensure technical excellence across the board.As a .NET Developer (Senior-Lead) you will:Lead the design and development of scalable, secure, high-performance enterprise applicationsTranslate complex business requirements into robust, future-proof technical architecturesWrite clean, reusable, well-documented code aligned with best practicesContribute to and review architectural decisions and technical designsMentor and support mid-level and junior developersConduct code reviews and promote high coding standardsCollaborate closely with architects, product owners, and key stakeholdersActively participate in Agile/Scrum ceremonies, estimations, and planningEnsure delivery quality through testing strategies, CI/CD pipelines, and performance optimizationQualificationsWhat would make you a fit for the role:5+ years of hands-on experience in .NET / C# backend development, with a strong track record of delivering scalable, secure, and maintainable enterprise-grade solutionsProven expertise in designing, developing, and maintaining RESTful APIs, with a focus on performance, reliability, and security best practicesStrong understanding and practical application of software architecture principles (SOLID, Clean Architecture, design patterns) in complex, large-scale systemsExperience or exposure to modern frontend frameworks such as Angular or React is considered an advantageFamiliarity with Docker, cloud environments (e.g., Azure), and CI/CD pipelines within enterprise development ecosystemsDemonstrated ability to lead technical discussions, contribute to architectural decisions, and mentor junior and mid-level developersExcellent English communication skills, both written and verbal, with the ability to collaborate effectively in cross-functional teamsAdditional InformationBeing a part of the Netcompany team, you will be provided with: The opportunity to work in a modern environment & in a hybrid working modelA seamless onboarding experience and a buddy to support you on your first stepsA competitive compensation & benefits packageHealth and life insurance programMeal and commuting allowanceWell-being activities (on premises)Continuous learning opportunities using the most modern methods (unlimited access to Udemy for Business, ad-hoc trainings)A personalized development plan for targeted career growthIf you are looking forward to be part of a diverse environment, and have the opportunity to work alongside well-experienced professionals, on challenging, large-scale projects that directly impact millions of citizens around the globe, then this is the place to be!Our branch in Patras employs 180+ talented professionals, working on a variety of EU mission-critical projects!Please upload your CV in English via the Apply button. All applications will be treated as strictly confidential.We ensure equal opportunities, treatment, and consideration to all candidates. Discrimination based on sex, racial or ethnic origin, religion or belief, disability, age, sexual orientation or marital status, physical or mental disability, or any other factor protected by applicable laws and regulations is prohibited. As part of the Netcompany culture, we respect human rights and focus on creating a positive workplace, where all employees are valued, and where diversity and inclusion are a vital part of our everyday working experience.In the following link you may find our CV Submission privacy notice: https://netcompany.com/cv-submission-privacy-notice/', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(648734, '.NET Developer (Mid-Senior)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/295783', 'Θεσσαλονίκη', 'πριν 25 μέρες', '2026-04-10 07:00:22', 'Netcompany', 'Company DescriptionAre you ready to shape the future technological landscape in Europe?We are dedicated to responsible digitalisation, building innovative, inclusive solutions that drive meaningful impact. With over 8,900 professionals across Europe, we help EU institutions, public and private organisations thrive in a rapidly evolving digital world. Are you ready to shape the future through technology? Your journey starts here. Take a look at some of our impactful projects here: https://netcompany.com/cases/Job DescriptionEver wondered what it feels like to be a .NET Developer (Mid-Senior) at Netcompany?As a .NET Developer (Mid-Senior), you will be part of a high-performing engineering team delivering enterprise-level digital solutions. In this role, you will contribute to the design and development of scalable applications while collaborating closely with senior engineers, architects, and product stakeholders.This position is ideal for developers who already have strong backend development experience and want to further grow their technical expertise while contributing to impactful, large-scale systems.You will work on complex enterprise platforms where quality, maintainability, and performance are key. You will take ownership of technical tasks, contribute to architectural discussions, and help maintain high engineering standards across the team.As a .NET Developer (Mid-Senior) you will:Design, develop, and maintain scalable and secure enterprise applications using .NET / C#Implement and maintain RESTful APIs ensuring performance, reliability, and securityTranslate business requirements into well-structured and maintainable technical solutionsWrite clean, testable, and reusable code following best practices and coding standardsParticipate in architectural discussions and technical design reviewsCollaborate with senior developers and architects on system design and improvementsPerform code reviews and contribute to improving team coding standardsWork closely with product owners, QA engineers, and other stakeholdersParticipate in Agile/Scrum ceremonies, sprint planning, and estimationsContribute to testing strategies, CI/CD processes, and application performance improvementsQualificationsWhat would make you a fit for the role:3+ years of hands-on experience in .NET / C# backend developmentSolid experience designing and developing RESTful APIsGood understanding of software engineering principles such as SOLID and common design patternsExperience building scalable, maintainable backend services in production environmentsExposure to frontend frameworks such as Angular or React is considered a plusFamiliarity with Docker, cloud platforms (e.g., Azure), and CI/CD pipelinesAbility to collaborate effectively within cross-functional Agile teamsStrong problem-solving mindset and willingness to continuously improve technical skillsGood English communication skills, both written and spokenAdditional InformationBeing a part of the Netcompany team, you will be provided with: The opportunity to work in a modern environment & in a hybrid working modelA seamless onboarding experience and a buddy to support you on your first stepsA competitive compensation & benefits packageHealth and life insurance programMeal and commuting allowanceWell-being activities (on premises)Continuous learning opportunities using the most modern methods (unlimited access to Udemy for Business, ad-hoc trainings)A personalized development plan for targeted career growthIf you are looking forward to be part of a diverse environment, and have the opportunity to work alongside well-experienced professionals, on challenging, large-scale projects that directly impact millions of citizens around the globe, then this is the place to be!Our branch in Thessaloniki employs 300+ talented professionals, working on a variety of EU mission-critical projects!Please upload your CV in English via the Apply button. All applications will be treated as strictly confidential.We ensure equal opportunities, treatment, and consideration to all candidates. Discrimination based on sex, racial or ethnic origin, religion or belief, disability, age, sexual orientation or marital status, physical or mental disability, or any other factor protected by applicable laws and regulations is prohibited. As part of the Netcompany culture, we respect human rights and focus on creating a positive workplace, where all employees are valued, and where diversity and inclusion are a vital part of our everyday working experience.In the following link you may find our CV Submission privacy notice: https://netcompany.com/cv-submission-privacy-notice/', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση');
