equence diagramsEnsure integrations meet non-functional requirements: performance, scalability, security, and complianceContribute to automation, logging, monitoring, and operational readiness of integration solutionsProduce clear and maintainable technical documentation for development and operations teamsQualificationsWhat would make you a fit for the role:Hands-on experience with Oracle SOA Suite 12c and/or Oracle Service Bus (OSB)Experience or strong interest in Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC)Solid understanding of REST and SOAP services and API designExperience with XML, JSON, XSD, XSLT, and message transformationsFamiliarity with error handling, fault policies, and retry patterns in enterprise integrationsScripting experience (e.g. Unix shell, WLST)Experience working with Git and structured version-control workflowsExposure to unit and integration testing in integration projectsExperience with logging and monitoring tools (e.g. Kibana, Grafana, or similar)Understanding of integration security: OAuth2, mTLS, API keys, and secrets managementStrong written communication skills and comfort working in structured, regulated environmentsA proactive, curious mindset and a collaborative way of workingIt would also be a plus if you match some of the following:SQL for monitoring and troubleshooting; PL/SQL is an advantageExperience working in Telecommunications or Utilities domainsExperience supporting integrations in production and enterprise-scale environmentsPrior consulting experience or customer-facing rolesDeeper hands-on experience with Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC)Additional InformationBeing a part of the Netcompany team, you will be provided with: The opportunity to work in a modern environment & in a hybrid working modelA seamless onboarding experience and a buddy to support you on your first stepsA competitive compensation & benefits packageHealth and life insurance programMeal and commuting allowanceWell-being activities (on premises)Continuous learning oppor