(649392, 'Integration Engineer / Consultant', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/engineering-jobs/286790', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-11 07:00:21', 'Netcompany', 'Company DescriptionAre you ready to shape the future technological landscape in Europe?We are dedicated to responsible digitalisation, building innovative, inclusive solutions that drive meaningful impact. With over 8,900 professionals across Europe, we help EU institutions, public and private organisations thrive in a rapidly evolving digital world. Are you ready to shape the future through technology? Your journey starts here. Take a look at some of our impactful projects here: https://netcompany.com/cases/Job DescriptionEver wondered what it feels like to work as an Integration Engineer / Consultant on large-scale enterprise platforms at Netcompany?Joining us, you\'ll be part of teams delivering mission-critical integrations for enterprise clients, using Oracle integration technologies at the core. You\'ll work with experienced architects and engineers, apply proven integration patterns, and help shape solutions that are secure, scalable, and built for long-term operation.This role is ideal for engineers or consultants who enjoy working close to the platform, understand enterprise integration challenges, and want to deepen their expertise in Oracle SOA Suite, OSB, and Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC).As an Integration Engineer / Consultant you will:Design, implement, and test integrations using Oracle SOA Suite 12c, Oracle Service Bus (OSB), and/or Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC)Develop and expose REST and SOAP services, including schema design, mappings, transformations, and fault handlingApply established enterprise integration patterns (synchronous, asynchronous, pub/sub, batch, event-driven, file-based)Build and troubleshoot BPEL processes, OSB pipelines, adapters, and integrationsCollaborate with business analysts and architects to translate requirements into interface contracts, message flows, and sequence diagramsEnsure integrations meet non-functional requirements: performance, scalability, security, and complianceContribute to automation, logging, monitoring, and operational readiness of integration solutionsProduce clear and maintainable technical documentation for development and operations teamsQualificationsWhat would make you a fit for the role:Hands-on experience with Oracle SOA Suite 12c and/or Oracle Service Bus (OSB)Experience or strong interest in Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC)Solid understanding of REST and SOAP services and API designExperience with XML, JSON, XSD, XSLT, and message transformationsFamiliarity with error handling, fault policies, and retry patterns in enterprise integrationsScripting experience (e.g. Unix shell, WLST)Experience working with Git and structured version-control workflowsExposure to unit and integration testing in integration projectsExperience with logging and monitoring tools (e.g. Kibana, Grafana, or similar)Understanding of integration security: OAuth2, mTLS, API keys, and secrets managementStrong written communication skills and comfort working in structured, regulated environmentsA proactive, curious mindset and a collaborative way of workingIt would also be a plus if you match some of the following:SQL for monitoring and troubleshooting; PL/SQL is an advantageExperience working in Telecommunications or Utilities domainsExperience supporting integrations in production and enterprise-scale environmentsPrior consulting experience or customer-facing rolesDeeper hands-on experience with Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC)Additional InformationBeing a part of the Netcompany team, you will be provided with: The opportunity to work in a modern environment & in a hybrid working modelA seamless onboarding experience and a buddy to support you on your first stepsA competitive compensation & benefits packageHealth and life insurance programMeal and commuting allowanceWell-being activities (on premises)Continuous learning opportunities using the most modern methods (unlimited access to Udemy for Business, ad-hoc trainings)A personalized development plan for targeted career growthIf you are looking forward to be part of a diverse environment, and have the opportunity to work alongside well-experienced professionals, on challenging, large-scale projects that directly impact millions of citizens around the globe, then this is the place to be!By joining Netcompany in Athens, you will be part of a vivid team of 2,300+ tech professionals. When at the office, you\'ll have the flexibility to work from our three modern, sustainable, and state-of-the-art offices!Please upload your CV in English via the Apply button. All applications will be treated as strictly confidential.We ensure equal opportunities, treatment, and consideration to all candidates. Discrimination based on sex, racial or ethnic origin, religion or belief, disability, age, sexual orientation or marital status, physical or mental disability, or any other factor protected by applicable laws and regulations is prohibited. As part of the Netcompany culture, we respect human rights and focus on creating a positive workplace, where all employees are valued, and where diversity and inclusion are a vital part of our everyday working experience.In the following link you may find our CV Submission privacy notice: https://netcompany.com/cv-submission-privacy-notice/', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(649393, 'Senior Integration Engineer / Consultant', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/engineering-jobs/286791', 'Θεσσαλονίκη', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-11 07:00:25', 'Netcompany', 'Company DescriptionAre you ready to shape the future technological landscape in Europe?We are dedicated to responsible digitalisation, building innovative, inclusive solutions that drive meaningful impact. With over 8,900 professionals across Europe, we help EU institutions, public and private organisations thrive in a rapidly evolving digital world. Are you ready to shape the future through technology? Your journey starts here. Take a look at some of our impactful projects here: https://netcompany.com/cases/Job DescriptionEver wondered what it feels like to work as a Senior Integration Engineer / Consultant at Netcompany, shaping integration solutions at enterprise scale?Joining us in this role, you\'ll take technical ownership of business-critical integrations for large enterprise clients. You\'ll lead the design and delivery of complex integration landscapes built on Oracle SOA Suite, Oracle Service Bus (OSB), and Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC), while guiding teams, influencing architecture, and ensuring solutions are robust, secure, and future-proof.This role is well suited to experienced integration engineers or consultants who enjoy combining hands-on development, technical leadership, and client-facing responsibility.As a Senior Integration Engineer / Consultant you will:Design, implement, and optimize Oracle-based integration solutions, including orchestration, mediation, messaging, retries, idempotency, and correlationTake ownership of REST and SOAP API design, governance, and lifecycle management, ensuring performance, resiliency, and compliance with non-functional requirementsTranslate business and architectural requirements into integration designs, interface specifications, and SLAs, balancing scope, risk, and technical trade-offsBuild, troubleshoot, and support BPEL processes, OSB pipelines, adapters, and OIC integrationsLead the integration of enterprise platforms such as CRM, ERP, Billing, Collections, Portals, and Chatbots, working with internal and vendor APIsDrive automation and CI/CD for integration components and contribute to operational excellence through logging, monitoring, and alerting (e.g. Grafana, Kibana, ELK)Act as a technical mentor: review designs and code, support junior engineers, and promote best practices across teamsEnsure integrations meet security, compliance, and audit requirements, including OAuth2/OIDC/SAML, mTLS, secure secrets handling, and audit loggingQualificationsWhat would make you a fit for the role:Extensive hands-on experience with enterprise integration patterns (synchronous/asynchronous, pub/sub, batch, file-based, event-driven)Strong expertise in XML, JSON, XSD, XSLT, and complex message transformationsProven ability to design, build, test, and optimize resilient APIs and services, including fault handling and recovery strategiesSolid scripting skills (e.g. Unix shell, WLST) for automation and operational supportStrong hands-on experience with Oracle SOA Suite 12c and/or Oracle Service Bus (OSB); experience with Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC) is highly valuedExperience working with CI/CD pipelines, Git, and structured release processes in enterprise environmentsGood understanding of unit, integration, and regression testing for integration solutionsStrong experience with logging, monitoring, and observability in production environments (Grafana, Kibana, ELK, or similar)Deep understanding of integration security: OAuth2/OIDC/SAML, mTLS, API keys, and secrets managementExcellent communication skills and the ability to explain technical concepts to both technical and non-technical stakeholdersA leadership mindset with a collaborative, pragmatic, and quality-driven approachIt would also be a plus if you match some of the following:Advanced SQL for monitoring and troubleshooting; PL/SQL is a strong advantageExperience working in Telecommunications or Utilities domainsHands-on experience with Oracle Integration Cloud (OIC) in productionExperience working in large, distributed enterprise ecosystems and managing external vendor integrationsPrior experience in a consulting or client-facing roleAdditional InformationBeing a part of the Netcompany team, you will be provided with: The opportunity to work in a modern environment & in a hybrid working modelA seamless onboarding experience and a buddy to support you on your first stepsA competitive compensation & benefits packageHealth and life insurance programMeal and commuting allowanceWell-being activities (on premises)Continuous learning opportunities using the most modern methods (unlimited access to Udemy for Business, ad-hoc trainings)A personalized development plan for targeted career growthIf you are looking forward to be part of a diverse environment, and have the opportunity to work alongside well-experienced professionals, on challenging, large-scale projects that directly impact millions of citizens around the globe, then this is the place to be!Our branch in Thessaloniki employs 300+ talented professionals, working on a variety of EU mission-critical projects!Please upload your CV in English via the Apply button. All applications will be treated as strictly confidential.We ensure equal opportunities, treatment, and consideration to all candidates. Discrimination based on sex, racial or ethnic origin, religion or belief, disability, age, sexual orientation or marital status, physical or mental disability, or any other factor protected by applicable laws and regulations is prohibited. As part of the Netcompany culture, we respect human rights and focus on creating a positive workplace, where all employees are valued, and where diversity and inclusion are a vital part of our everyday working experience.In the following link you may find our CV Submission privacy notice: https://netcompany.com/cv-submission-privacy-notice/', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
