(651632, 'ΧΕΙΡΙΣΤΗΣ ΕΡΓΑΛΕΙΟΜΗΧΑΝΩΝ', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/workers-jobs/305029', 'Πειραιάς', 'πριν 17 λεπτά', '2026-04-14 15:01:15', 'A.MAKARIAN Co', 'Εταιρεία με 60 χρόνια προσφορά στο χώρο της ναυτιλίας και έδρα στον Πειραιά, ζητά να προσλάβει Χειριστή ή Βοηθό Χειριστή Εργαλειομηχανών, ρεκτιφιέ, honing & τόρνου.Παρακαλούνται οι ενδιαφερόμενοι, όπως αποστείλουν Βιογραφικό Σημείωμα. Βασικές Γνώσεις εργαλειομηχανώνΣταθερός Μισθός Πλήρης πενθήμερη απασχόληση & ΑσφάλισηΕυχάριστο περιβάλλονΕκμάθηση χειρισμού εργαλειομηχανώνΣτρατιωτικές υποχρεώσεις εκπληρωμένεςΟμαδικό πνεύμα εργασίας Θετική διάθεση εργασίας για συνεχή εκμάθηση πολλών τύπων εργαλειομηχανών', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(651633, 'Ηλεκτρολόγος ή Μηχανολόγος Μηχανικός', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/engineering-jobs/305022', 'Άρτα', 'πριν 4 λεπτά', '2026-04-14 15:01:16', 'NEW ALERT', 'Η NewALERT, τεχνική εταιρεία με εξειδίκευση στα ηλεκτρομηχανολογικά έργα και τις τεχνικές εγκαταστάσεις, ενδιαφέρεται να προσλάβει Ηλεκτρολόγο ή Μηχανολόγο Μηχανικό για το Γενικό Νοσοκομείο Άρτας.  Αρμοδιότητες Επίβλεψη και συντονισμός εργασιών συντήρησης Παρακολούθηση λειτουργίας Η/Μ εγκαταστάσεων Διαχείριση και καθοδήγηση τεχνικού προσωπικού Εντοπισμός και επίλυση τεχνικών προβλημάτων Συνεργασία με προμηθευτές και εξωτερικά συνεργεία Τήρηση διαδικασιών ασφάλειας και τεχνικών προδιαγραφών  Απαραίτητα Προσόντα Πτυχίο Ηλεκτρολόγου ή Μηχανολόγου Μηχανικού (ΠΕ) Επιθυμητή εμπειρία σε συντήρηση κτιριακών εγκαταστάσεων Καλή γνώση Η/Μ συστημάτων Υπευθυνότητα και οργανωτικές ικανότητες  Η εταιρεία προσφέρει Μόνιμη απασχόληση Σταθερό και οργανωμένο περιβάλλον εργασίας Προοπτικές εξέλιξης   Τηλέφωνα: 22950 54206, 22950 23957 email: [email protected] & [email protected]  ', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(651634, 'Director of Engineering', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/305028?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν 2 λεπτά', '2026-04-14 15:01:17', 'Kariera Group Recruitment Services | Hospitality Talent Solutions', 'We are Hiring a Director of Engineering on behalf of Mandarin Oriental Purpose of Position It is the mission and intent of this position that the incumbent will take full responsibility in the maintenance, repairs and safe operation of all technical services in accordance with Mandarin Oriental Hotel Group standards, policies and procedures to always achieve optimum operating efficiency and guest comfort. Furthermore, this position provides continuous leadership and guidance on all FLHSS&E matters as well as Security of the property by developing and implementing risk management evaluations which will follow MOHG FLHSS&E guidelines, as well as, ensures compliance with all country and local regulations. Organisational Structure The position report to the hotel’s General Manager. Additionally, the position reports to the MOHG Corporate Director of Engineering on a functional basis. Position Objectives The Director of Engineering ‘s role is to coordinate and control all Engineering, FLHSS&E, Landscaping with a clear focus in providing a balanced service to meet the needs of the physical property, our customers and colleagues. The incumbent is expected to actively participate in the general day to day operation of the department leading, mentoring, training and educating the engineering team. The Director of Engineering is responsible for the financial management of the property operation and maintenance expenses and for utilities consumption. Duties and Supporting Responsibilities · Maintain in a proper and safe condition all buildings, plant, plant rooms, equipment, landscaping, front and back of house areas. · Establish and implement “Safe and Sound” procedures such as the Fire, Life, Health, Safety and Security, Emergency and Standard Operating Procedures in compliance with Mandarin Oriental Hotel Group standards. · Ensure all work carried out for the hotel is in compliance with the relevant statutory requirements, regulations and codes. · To be fully conversant with The Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino Emergency Procedures. · Perform “Emergency Response Team” duties as required. · Chairperson for the Risk Management meeting · Be appointed as the Fire & Safety manager for the property. · Actively initiate and support all training programs and initiatives. · Directly oversee and control the activities of the Engineering team. · Oversee the selection of engineering outsourced companies and services. · Participate in the formulation of strategic business plans for the hotel. · Formulate and implement strategic development for the hotel’s involvement in the local community. · Develop and implement the preventative maintenance programs in accordance with Mandarin Oriental Hotel Group guidelines. · Participate in Executive Committee and other meetings as required. · Establish and manage the annual CapEX plan and budget for all aspects of engineering. · Oversee the strategic direction of general projects related to the enhancement of the hotel. Project management covers the areas of planning, administration, implementation and evaluation of financial results of projects. · Support the Director of Fiance in the hotel’s overall financial performance; the annual hotel budget process; the energy and cost consumption; and the engineering contractor’s selection and documentation. · Support the Director of P&C in their strategy for the recruitment and selection of employees; career development programs for employees; labor cost management; community programs; and the evaluation and recognition of employees. · Support the IT&T Director in telecommunications upgrades and enhancements; annual maintenance of the contingency systems that support IT&T equipment and systems; and the annual testing and conformance of emergency power systems based on Mandarin Oriental Hotel Group guidelines. · Support the Operations team on the training and demonstration of various systems such as the key system for guest rooms, audio visual equipment, lighting and temperature and control systems, etc. · Regularly meet with Department Heads to ensure we are meeting their needs. · Ensure strict record keeping is well always maintained. · Liaise with builders, consultants and contractors. · Participate in the Repairs and Maintenance, Project and Risk Management Committee meetings as required. · Conduct regular inspections of all front and back of house areas to ensure the quality and standards are maintained at the highest level. · Ensure all drawings, manuals and documentation is updated as and when changes are made. · Ensure all certifications, test reports, inspections and maintenance reports are properly stored and updated. · Prepare tender documents. · Be fully conversant with all technical details of all plant and services relating to the hotel. · Assist engineering personnel with technical advice and ensure standards are maintained. · Prepare budgets, forecasts and costings. · Actively assist with energy conservation and control. · Oversee the activities of service and project contractors. · Maintain contact with local authorities and Government Departments such as the Fire Service Department, Electrical and Mechanical Service Department, Water Supply Department, Building Ordinance Office, Drainage Department, Labour Department, Environmental Protection Department, to ensure that all requirements are being complied with and that assistance or advice will be readily available whenever required. · Evaluates individual employee performance, determines areas in need of improvement or requirements for advancement, establishes goals, objectives and training needs required to achieve them. · Evaluates changes in guest needs, the hotels guest mix and industry competitive set, to recommend appropriate product/service and operational changes necessary to ensure guest and employee satisfaction, while maintaining market dominance and exceptional financial prospects. · To ensure all company financial standards and audit requirements are adhered to at all times. · To carry out any other reasonable request as directed by your General Manager. Health and Safety · To be aware of, and comply with, safe working practices as laid down under Company H & S Manual, as applicable to your place of work. This will include your awareness of any specific hazards at your work place. · To be aware of and comply with Food Hygiene Standards. · To wear any appropriate protective clothing provided by or recommended by the Hotel. · To report any defects in the building, plant or equipment according to the Hotel procedures. · To ensure any accidents to colleagues, guests or visitors are reported in accordance with Hotel procedures. · To attend statutory fire training and to be fully conversant with and abide by all rules concerning, fire, health & safety. · To attend any training deemed appropriate by your Head of Department. · To elect a departmental health & safety representative. · To ensure H&S representative attends all meetings · To undertake responsibility for supervising, training and instructing colleagues in terms of H & S.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(651635, 'Συντηρητής - Ερέτρια', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/305027', 'Ερέτρια', 'πριν 2 λεπτά', '2026-04-14 15:01:17', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Συντηρητής Σχετικά με τον ρόλο Ως Τεχνικός Συντήρησης, θα αποτελέσετε βασικό μέλος της λειτουργικής ομάδας του ξενοδοχείου, διασφαλίζοντας την άρτια κατάσταση του εξοπλισμού και των εγκαταστάσεων. Ο ρόλος σας συμβάλλει άμεσα στην ασφάλεια, τη λειτουργικότητα και τη συνολική εμπειρία φιλοξενίας των επισκεπτών μας. Με τεχνική γνώση, υπευθυνότητα και πνεύμα συνεργασίας, θα διασφαλίζετε ότι όλοι οι χώροι του ξενοδοχείου λειτουργούν απρόσκοπτα και σύμφωνα με τα υψηλά μας πρότυπα.   Ζωή στο Ξενοδοχείο Κάθε ημέρα φέρνει διαφορετικές τεχνικές προκλήσεις — από προληπτική συντήρηση έως άμεση αντιμετώπιση αιτημάτων επισκεπτών και λειτουργικών ζητημάτων. Σε αυτό το περιβάλλον, η ομαδικότητα, η ευελιξία και η σωστή επικοινωνία με τα υπόλοιπα τμήματα είναι καθοριστικής σημασίας. Ως μέλος της ομάδας μας, θα εργάζεστε σε ένα οργανωμένο και σύγχρονο περιβάλλον, όπου η τεχνική αρτιότητα υποστηρίζει τη συνολική εμπειρία φιλοξενίας.   Τι θα κάνετε Συντηρείτε και επισκευάζετε εξοπλισμό σε δωμάτια και κοινόχρηστους χώρους Εκτελείτε προληπτική συντήρηση σε όλα τα ξενοδοχειακά συστήματα και εγκαταστάσεις, σύμφωνα με τα προβλεπόμενα πρότυπα Αντιμετωπίζετε άμεσα τεχνικά ζητήματα και αιτήματα επισκεπτών Διατηρείτε καθαρό και οργανωμένο τον χώρο εργασίας και τις αποθήκες Τηρείτε αυστηρά όλους τους κανόνες υγείας και ασφάλειας Επικοινωνείτε αποτελεσματικά και ευγενικά με τη ρεσεψιόν και τη διοίκηση Διαχειρίζεστε παράπονα ή αιτήματα επισκεπτών με επαγγελματισμό, φιλική διάθεση και υπομονή Συνεργάζεστε στενά με τους συναδέλφους όλων των τμημάτων   Αυτό που σας κάνει ξεχωριστούς Πιστεύουμε ότι ένας επιτυχημένος τεχνικός δεν ξεχωρίζει μόνο για τις τεχνικές του γνώσεις, αλλά και για τη συνέπεια, τη διάθεση προσφοράς και την ικανότητά του να εργάζεται αποτελεσματικά υπό πίεση.   Αναζητούμε άτομα που: Διαθέτουν καλή γνώση ηλεκτρολογικών, μηχανολογικών, υδραυλικών και αυτοματισμών Έχουν τουλάχιστον 1 έτος εμπειρίας σε αντίστοιχη θέση Διαθέτουν εμπειρία στην επισκευή μηχανολογικού, ηλεκτρολογικού, εξοπλισμού κουζίνας και πλυντηρίων Έχουν καλή γνώση Αγγλικών (επιθυμητή) Διαθέτουν ομαδικό πνεύμα και διάθεση συνεργασίας Είναι οργανωτικοί, υπεύθυνοι και προσανατολισμένοι στη λύση προβλημάτων   Τι προσφέρουμε Ευκαιρίες επαγγελματικής εξέλιξης και ανάπτυξης καριέρας εντός του ξενοδοχειακού ομίλου Εργασία σε σύγχρονο και οργανωμένο περιβάλλον με ποικιλία καθηκόντων Ανταγωνιστικό πακέτο αποδοχών και παροχών Διαμονή και διατροφή (για θέσεις σε resorts)   Έτοιμοι να γίνετε μέρος της κοινότητάς μας;', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(651636, 'F&B Manager', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/305025?origin=pjp', 'Πάτρα', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-14 15:01:19', 'Kariera Group Recruitment Services | Hospitality Talent Solutions', 'Ο Όμιλος Airotel έχει παρουσία σε Αθήνα, Πάτρα, Καβάλα και δραστηριοποιείται σε πολλούς τομείς της τουριστικής βιομηχανίας. Στόχος μας υπήρξε πάντα η παροχή εξαιρετικών υπηρεσιών φιλοξενίας, επισιτισμού και διοργάνωσης επαγγελματικών συναντήσεων.Για τo ξενοδοχείο Astir Hotel στην Πάτρα αναζητούμε F&B ManagerΑρμοδιότητες:- Οργάνωση, συντονισμός και επίβλεψη όλων των λειτουργιών F&B (εστιατόρια, bars,room service, banquet).- Διαχείριση και υποστήριξη εκδηλώσεων υψηλού όγκου, από τον σχεδιασμό έως την εκτέλεση.- Επίτευξη στόχων ποιότητας, κόστους και κερδοφορίας.- Εκπαίδευση, καθοδήγηση και αξιολόγηση προσωπικού.- Συνεργασία με τμήματα πωλήσεων και events για βέλτιστη εμπειρία πελάτη.- Έλεγχος διαδικασιών HACCP και των Υγειονομικών πρωτοκόλλων.- Συνεργάζεται με την ομάδα Κουζίνας και τον Chef για να διασφαλίσει την ομαλή λειτουργία των τμημάτων F&B.- Συμβολή στην κάλυψη και μεγιστοποίηση του μηνιαίου προϋπολογισμού εσόδων για τοαντίστοιχο κατάστημα.- Φροντίζει με ασφαλή και φιλικό προς το περιβάλλον τρόπο για την προστασία της υγείαςκαι της ασφάλειας των επισκεπτών και των συναδέλφων, καθώς και για την προστασίακαι διατήρηση του περιβάλλοντος- Φροντίζει για την άριστη υποδοχή και εξυπηρέτηση των επισκεπτών και χτίζει σχέσειςεμπιστοσύνης μαζί τους Απαραίτητα Προσόντα:- Προϋπηρεσία τουλάχιστον 3-5 ετών σε αντίστοιχη θέση σε ξενοδοχείο 4* ή 5*.- Εμπειρία στη διαχείριση εκδηλώσεων μεγάλης κλίμακας.- Άριστη γνώση ελληνικών και αγγλικών (προφορικά & γραπτά).- Ικανότητα ηγεσίας, επικοινωνίας και επίλυσης προβλημάτων.- Γνώση συστημάτων POS και βασικών αρχών κοστολόγησης.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(651637, 'Αποθηκάριος - Βραυρώνα', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/305026', 'Αρτέμιδα', 'πριν μερικά δευτερόλεπτα', '2026-04-14 15:01:19', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Αποθηκάριος Σχετικά με το ρόλο Γίνε μέλος του ZEUS Hotels & Resorts Group, ενός ταχέως αναπτυσσόμενου ομίλου πολυτελούς φιλοξενίας. Στόχος μας είναι η παροχή υψηλής ποιότητας υπηρεσιών, μέσα από άρτια οργανωμένες λειτουργίες και δυνατές ομάδες.Στο πλαίσιο αυτό, αναζητούμε έναν/μία έμπειρο/η Υπεύθυνο/η Τμήματος Προμηθειών για τον συντονισμό, την επίβλεψη και τη βελτιστοποίηση των διαδικασιών προμηθειών του Ομίλου. Η καθημερινότητα στον Όμιλο • Εποπτεία και συντονισμός της καθημερινής λειτουργίας του Τμήματος Προμηθειών• Διαχείριση και έγκριση παραγγελιών προμηθειών• Ανάπτυξη και διατήρηση συνεργασιών με προμηθευτές• Διαπραγμάτευση όρων συνεργασίας και τιμολογιακής πολιτικής• Παρακολούθηση αποθεμάτων και έλεγχος μέσω ERP συστημάτων• Διασφάλιση της ορθότητας δεδομένων, παραστατικών και διαδικασιών• Εξασφάλιση συμμόρφωσης με τις εταιρικές πολιτικές και διαδικασίες• Συνεργασία με τα τμήματα λειτουργίας των ξενοδοχείων για κάλυψη αναγκών• Εντοπισμός ευκαιριών βελτίωσης αποδοτικότητας και μείωσης κόστους Αυτό που σε κάνει μοναδικό/ή Αναζητούμε έναν δυναμικό και οργανωτικό επαγγελματία που: • Διαθέτει άριστες γνώσεις χρήσης Η/Υ και εφαρμογών γραφείου (Microsoft Office)• Έχει αποδεδειγμένη εμπειρία στη χρήση ERP συστημάτων• Έχει πολύ καλή γνώση της Αγγλικής γλώσσας (γραπτά και προφορικά)• Διαθέτει ηγετικές, οργανωτικές και διαπραγματευτικές δεξιότητες• Μπορεί να συντονίζει ομάδες και να εργάζεται αποτελεσματικά υπό πίεση• Προϋπηρεσία σε αντίστοιχη θέση (ιδανικά στον ξενοδοχειακό κλάδο) θα θεωρηθεί σημαντικό προσόν Τι προσφέρουμε • Ανταγωνιστικό πακέτο αποδοχών• Συνεχή εκπαίδευση και ευκαιρίες επαγγελματικής εξέλιξης• Σύγχρονο και υποστηρικτικό εργασιακό περιβάλλον• Σταθερότητα και προοπτικές καριέρας σε έναν κορυφαίο ξενοδοχειακό όμιλο Έτοιμοι να γίνετε μέρος της κοινότητάς μας;', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(651638, 'Director of Engineering', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/305023?origin=pjp', 'Μύκονος', 'πριν 3 ώρες', '2026-04-14 15:01:21', 'Kariera Group Recruitment Services | Hospitality Talent Solutions', 'About UsWith years of industry experience, the Hospitality Recruitment Services team of Kariera.gr is your compass for navigating a rewarding career in the dynamic world of hospitality and tourism. We specialize in connecting passionate individuals with diverse opportunities spanning from entry-level to senior management roles within the hospitality sector. We believe in fostering an environment where career journeys align seamlessly with the growth and success of hospitality businesses. Join a new movement in luxury, built by people with creativity, curiosity, and heart. ORA Hospitality is introducing a new ultra-luxury hotel brand that’s redefining what modern hospitality feels like. With resorts opening soon in Egypt’s North Coast, Abu Dhabi, and Tunisia, alongside award-winning hotels Silversands Grenada and The Beach House in the Caribbean. We\'re creating a global collection built on style, substance, service and soul. Our culture is shaped by imagination and insight, by a deep respect for people and place, and by the courage to do things differently. Our first new property will open in Mykonos, designed by the world-renowned Rockwell Group. Nestled in the bay of Kalo Livadi, it features 88 sea-view rooms and suites, five private villas, two signature restaurants, a world-class spa and wellness centre, and experiences designed for every generation, from sunrise yoga to golden-hour gatherings overlooking the Aegean Sea. What you will Do The Director of Engineering will be responsible for the overall management, operation, and maintenanceof the hotel’s physical assets and engineering systems. This includes ensuring that all building systems—such as HVAC, electrical, plumbing, fire and life-safety systems, elevators, and energy management—operate safely, efficiently, and in full compliance with local regulations and brand standards. The role encompasses preventive and corrective maintenance planning, capital project oversight, andenergy conservation initiatives aimed at cost control and asset longevity. The Director of Engineering willlead and develop the engineering team, manage contractors and suppliers, control departmental budgets,and ensure continuous operational readiness to support guest satisfaction and uninterrupted hoteloperations. In addition, the position plays a key role in health, safety, and environmental compliance, emergencypreparedness, and sustainability initiatives, while working closely with the hotel’s executive team to alignengineering operations with business objectives and guest experience standards. The Director of Engineering will active participate in the handover of the new hotel. What you need to bring Minimum 5 years of experience in hotel engineering management, preferably within a luxury 5-star or resort environment. University degree in Mechanical, Electrical, Civil Engineering, or a related field. Excellent command of the English language Proven leadership and team management abilities. Strong knowledge of building systems, electrical, mechanical, HVAC, plumbing, and preventive maintenance practices. Excellent problem-solving, decision-making, and organizational skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities, high-pressure situations, and emergency responses. Familiarity with engineering management software and energy optimization systems. Strong commitment to safety, quality, and sustainability standards What we offer Competitive Compensation: Attractive salary package aligned with industry standards. Career Experience: Opportunity to work with a newly established global hospitality brand. Professional Growth: Ongoing training and development programs to support career advancement. If you’re ready to grow with a brand that values creativity, collaboration, and curiosity, join our pre-opening team and be part of building something extraordinary, together. All applications will be handled with the utmost confidentiality and evaluated solely on professional qualifications and merit. Our company is an Equal Opportunity Employer, committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace where every team member can thrive. Eligibility to work in Greece is a prerequisite for all applicants.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(651639, 'Night Shift Receptionist - Kos Island', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/305024', 'Ηρακλείδες', 'πριν μερικά δευτερόλεπτα', '2026-04-14 15:01:21', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Night Receptionist About the role As a Night Receptionist, you will be the face of our hotel during the overnight hours, ensuring smooth front desk operations and exceptional guest service. You will welcome late arrivals, assist guests with their needs, and handle administrative and operational tasks with professionalism and care. This role requires responsibility, attention to detail, and a calm, service-oriented mindset. If you thrive in independent work environments and enjoy supporting guests during quieter but critical hours, this role is for you.   Life Inside ZEUS Hotels & Resorts While most of the hotel rests, your shift begins. The night hours bring a unique rhythm — peaceful at times, unpredictable at others. You’ll manage late check-ins, guest requests, safety procedures, and essential reporting that sets the tone for the next day. You will be the steady presence that ensures everything runs smoothly until morning — providing reassurance, structure, and high-quality service at every moment.   What you’ll do Welcome and assist guests with late arrivals, departures, and requests Manage front desk operations during the night shift Answer phone calls, emails, and handle reservations Monitor hotel premises to ensure safety and report any suspicious activity Handle payments, invoices, and prepare shift reports Coordinate with other departments to fulfill guest requests Maintain accurate guest records and update the system accordingly Handle emergency situations calmly and efficiently   Your uniqueness is welcome We believe great night receptionists are calm, reliable, and naturally caring. You are someone who stays focused under pressure, notices details others might miss, and enjoys helping guests feel safe and welcome at any hour.   What we’re looking for Previous experience in a similar role, preferably in hospitality or front office Knowledge of hotel management systems and basic computer skills (e.g., MS Office, Protel) Strong organizational and multitasking abilities Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Fluency in Greek and English Ability to work independently and remain calm under pressure   What we offer Competitive salary and benefits package Opportunities for professional development and training A supportive and collaborative work environment Accommodation (for resort locations) and meals provided   Ready to join our team?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(651640, 'Night Shift Receptionist - Agios Nikolaos', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/305021', 'Άγιος Νικόλαος', 'πριν 29 λεπτά', '2026-04-14 15:01:23', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Night Receptionist About the role As a Night Receptionist, you will be the face of our hotel during the overnight hours, ensuring smooth front desk operations and exceptional guest service. You will welcome late arrivals, assist guests with their needs, and handle administrative and operational tasks with professionalism and care. This role requires responsibility, attention to detail, and a calm, service-oriented mindset. If you thrive in independent work environments and enjoy supporting guests during quieter but critical hours, this role is for you.   Life Inside ZEUS Hotels & Resorts While most of the hotel rests, your shift begins. The night hours bring a unique rhythm — peaceful at times, unpredictable at others. You’ll manage late check-ins, guest requests, safety procedures, and essential reporting that sets the tone for the next day. You will be the steady presence that ensures everything runs smoothly until morning — providing reassurance, structure, and high-quality service at every moment.   What you’ll do Welcome and assist guests with late arrivals, departures, and requests Manage front desk operations during the night shift Answer phone calls, emails, and handle reservations Monitor hotel premises to ensure safety and report any suspicious activity Handle payments, invoices, and prepare shift reports Coordinate with other departments to fulfill guest requests Maintain accurate guest records and update the system accordingly Handle emergency situations calmly and efficiently   Your uniqueness is welcome We believe great night receptionists are calm, reliable, and naturally caring. You are someone who stays focused under pressure, notices details others might miss, and enjoys helping guests feel safe and welcome at any hour.   What we’re looking for Previous experience in a similar role, preferably in hospitality or front office Knowledge of hotel management systems and basic computer skills (e.g., MS Office, Protel) Strong organizational and multitasking abilities Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Fluency in Greek and English Ability to work independently and remain calm under pressure   What we offer Competitive salary and benefits package Opportunities for professional development and training A supportive and collaborative work environment Accommodation (for resort locations) and meals provided   Ready to join our team?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(651641, 'Chef De Partie', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/305020?origin=pjp', 'Θήρα', 'πριν 4 λεπτά', '2026-04-14 15:01:23', 'Kariera Group Recruitment Services | Hospitality Talent Solutions', 'About Us With years of industry experience, our Workathlon | Recruitment team is your compass to navigating a rewarding career in the dynamic world of tourism. We specialize in connecting passionate individuals with diverse opportunities spanning entry-level to senior management roles. We believe in fostering an environment where your career journey aligns seamlessly with the growth and success of our tourism initiatives. At Workathlon | Recruitment, an integral part of Kariera.gr, every career move is a step towards excellence. Choose us as your catalyst for success, and let\'s shape your future together. Key Responsibilities Prepare, cook, and present dishes according to the menu and the Executive Chef’s instructions. Maintains consistency regarding the preparation and presentation of all menu items. Ensures that all ingredients received by stores and suppliers are up to standards. Effectively allocates work to subordinates. Follows all necessary policies and procedures relating to HACCP guidelines. Must be able to follow and implement all company’s policies and procedures. Performs related duties and special projects as assigned by the Kitchen department. Requirements Proven, continuous experience in a similar role, in a luxury hotel or upscale restaurant. Very good knowledge of A La Carte. Culinary degree or equivalent qualification from a recognized culinary institute. Excellent organizational and time management skills. Prepare, cook, and present dishes according to the menu and the Knowledge of current culinary trends and techniques.Very good knowledge of the Greek and the English language. Available to work nights and weekends. Company offers Fixed Term Contract (season 2026) Career development opportunities. Excellent working environment. Accommodation and meals on all working days. Transportation from/to staff houses', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(651642, 'Operations Manager', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/305018?origin=pjp', 'Πάτρα', 'πριν 3 ώρες', '2026-04-14 15:01:25', 'Kariera Group Recruitment Services | Hospitality Talent Solutions', '  PATRAS AREA OPERATIONS MANAGER About UsWith years of industry experience, our Workathlon | Recruitment team is your compass to navigating a rewarding career in the dynamic world of tourism. We specialize in connecting passionate individuals with diverse opportunities spanning entry-level to senior management roles. We believe in fostering an environment where your career journey aligns seamlessly with the growth and success of our tourism initiatives. At Workathlon | Recruitment, an integral part of Kariera.gr, every career move is a step towards excellence. Choose us as your catalyst for success, and let\'s shape your futuretogether. Among the various industries we recruit for, we are exclusively retained to find an experienced Operations Manager. Department: Hotel Operations Refers to: Managing Director Subordinates: HODs (directly) – FnB Manager, FO Manager, Housekeeping Manager Working Location: Patras Position Objectives: Responsible for designing, overseeing and implementing actions that ensure a smooth and effective hotels’ operation, including but not limited to guest satisfaction, people management, revenue generation and cost efficiency matters. Responsibilities: Always demonstrating a pleasant and positive professional image to both guests and the rest of the team. Always following the company’s internal policies as well as behavioral, grooming and personal hygiene Standards. Monitoring the attire and behavior of the department\'s staff as well as their compliance with all internal policies. Ensuring that all Standard Operating Procedures (SOP’s) are constantly followed and in the right way by all team members, aiming to achieve the highest guest satisfaction. Providing leadership, motivation and guidance to the hotel management team, setting expectations, managing performance, and communicating goals and objectives. Developing in coordination with the Managing Director and the HR Manager the annual staff budgets for the hotels under his/her responsibility. Developing in coordination with the Managing Director and the Director of Procurement the annual supplies budget for the hotels under his/her responsibility. Developing in coordination with the Managing Director, the annual internal revenue budgets. Developing, overseeing and implementing in coordination with the HODs, an annual action plan, in order to achieve the internal revenue budgets and the highest guest satisfaction for the hotels under his/her responsibility. Ensuring all agreed KPIs are met including guest satisfaction and financial targets. Overseeing the good relationships with key local stakeholders, including suppliers, and regulatory bodies; Enhancing brand awareness of the company through various partnerships and actions. Successful handling of any operational challenges that may occur, including but not limited to guest satisfaction, resources management, maintenance, authority audits. Participating in recruitment, training, retention, performance evaluation and other HR related actions, based on hotels’ needs and always in coordination with the company’s HR team and policies. Ensuring compliance with health, safety and labor law and regulations. Identifying areas for improvement and implementing changes to enhance operational and cost efficiency, revenue generation and guest experience enhancement. Providing reporting and advice to the Managing Director, concerning opportunities and threats identified locally or internally in his/her area of responsibility. Participating actively in all departmental and interdepartmental meetings whenever necessary, in order to support an effective communication flow and enhance collaboration and decision making. Initiating effective meetings with his/her team in order to ensure alignment with goals and provide guidance. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Tourism Management, Business Administration or related field At least 3 years’ experience as a General Manager in a multi property environment Excellent written and verbal communication skills both in Greek and English language Proficient use of MS Office and Hotel Management System (preferably Protel) Strong leadership and interpersonal skills', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(651643, 'Night Shift Receptionist - Nea Makri', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/305019', 'Νέα Μάκρη', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-14 15:01:25', 'ZEUS INTERNATIONAL A.E.', 'Night Shift Receptionist About the role Join our team and play a key role in delivering an excellent guest experience during the night. We are seeking a reliable and service-oriented Night Front Office Agent who will act as the main point of contact for our guests during night hours, ensuring smooth front desk operations and high standards of hospitality. This role requires responsibility, professionalism, and the ability to multitask calmly and efficiently. What you will do • Handle guest arrivals, departures, and requests during the night shift• Ensure smooth front desk operations, including phone and email communication• Monitor and update reservations in the system• Manage payments, invoicing, and prepare night shift reports• Maintain accurate guest records and system updates• Coordinate with other hotel departments to fulfill guest needs• Monitor hotel premises and report any suspicious activity• Handle emergency situations with professionalism and composure Your uniqueness is welcome We are looking for a responsible, well-organized professional with strong communication skills and the ability to work independently, who: • Has previous experience in a similar role, preferably within hospitality• Is familiar with hotel management systems (e.g. Protel) and basic computer skills (MS Office)• Demonstrates strong attention to detail and organizational skills• Can remain calm and effective under pressure• Has excellent command of Greek and English What we offer • Competitive salary and benefits package• Continuous training and professional development• A supportive and collaborative working environment• Accommodation (for resort positions) and meals provided• A stable role within a professional hospitality environment Ready to join our Community?', 'Εποχιακός/ή');
