(652999, 'Communications Specialist, Costa Navarino (2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/296602', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 3 ώρες', '2026-04-16 15:02:20', 'Costa Navarino', 'Costa Navarino is a sustainably driven destination in the Mediterranean, located in Messinia in the southwest Peloponnese. Graced with a breath-taking seaside landscape, this is a region shaped by 4,500 years of history. The Costa Navarino philosophy is driven by a genuine desire to preserve the natural beauty and heritage of Messinia. It is currently home to four 5-star hotels, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort Costa Navarino at Navarino Dunes, W Costa Navarino and Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino at Navarino Bay.The destination comprises several distinct sites featuring five-star hotels, luxury private residences, a world-class golf experience, and many year-round activities. Navarino Dunes is home to The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort, The Westin Resort Costa Navarino and Costa Navarino Residences. Navarino Bay is the setting for Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino, W Costa Navarino and Navarino Agora, a curated marketplace. Both sites have signature golf courses, while at Navarino Hills there are two further signature golf courses.Costa Navarino, is seeking a Communications Specialist to contribute to the execution of integrated communication campaigns that enhance brand visibility and engage key audiences. This newly created position is based at our headquarters in Athens and reports to the Communication Manager. The role will primarily focus on supporting media relations and internal communication events, while collaborating closely with cross-functional teams.ResponsibilitiesAssist in the implementation of communication strategies and campaigns.Facilitate media relations by maintaining relationships with press contacts, developing media kits, tracking coverage, and organizing hosted visits.Collaborate with internal teams (e.g., Guest Services, Operations) to ensure uniform messaging and provide seamless experiences.Contribute to the Internal Communications function.Track and report on communication metrics and the performance of campaigns.Assist with communication efforts for events, including product launches and press gatherings.RequirementsBachelor’s degree in Tourism, Marketing, Communications, or related field.Minimum 3 years of relevant experience in Tourism & Travel, Luxury Goods, or Agency environments.Excellent written and verbal communication skills in Greek and English; additional languages are a plus. Strong attention to detail, creativity, and organizational skills. Familiarity with social and digital performance platforms. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment and manage multiple projects simultaneously.Driving license holder and ability to travel to Costa Navarino. Effective communication, guest centric, multi-tasker, organized, analytical thinking, team player.BenefitsWhat We Offer:Competitive Compensation PackagePrivate Medical PlanPension PlanPersonal & Professional Growth:Ongoing Training & Development OpportunitiesExposure to an International Work EnvironmentWellbeing & Perks:Access to the Support Room – Online Wellness PlatformDiscounts at Marriott Hotels Worldwide', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653000, 'Construction Mechanical or Electrical Engineer, Costa Navarino (2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/305886', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-16 15:02:20', 'Costa Navarino', 'Costa Navarino is a sustainably driven destination in the Mediterranean, located in Messinia in the southwest Peloponnese. Graced with a breath-taking seaside landscape, this is a region shaped by 4,500 years of history. The Costa Navarino philosophy is driven by a genuine desire to preserve the natural beauty and heritage of Messinia. It is currently home to four 5-star hotels, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort Costa Navarino at Navarino Dunes, W Costa Navarino and Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino at Navarino Bay.The destination comprises several distinct sites featuring five-star hotels, luxury private residences, a world-class golf experience, and many year-round activities. Navarino Dunes is home to The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort, The Westin Resort Costa Navarino and Costa Navarino Residences. Navarino Bay is the setting for Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino, W Costa Navarino and Navarino Agora, a curated marketplace. Both sites have signature golf courses, while at Navarino Hills there are two further signature golf courses.We are seeking an experienced Construction MEP Engineer to join our team, with a strong background in the construction of building projects.Responsibilities :Supervise and manage building construction works on siteEnsure projects are executed according to plans, specifications, and safety regulationsCoordinate with contractors, subcontractors, and other engineersMonitor project progress, quality, and timelinesProvide technical support as requiredRequirementsMinimum Degree in mechanical or electrical engineeringProven minimum of 5 years of professional experience in the construction of building projectsSolid knowledge of construction methods, materials, and on-site processesAbility to supervise and coordinate construction activities on siteStrong problem-solving and organizational skillsExcellent communication and teamwork abilitiesAbility to work under deadlines and manage multiple tasksFluent in GreekBenefitsCompetitive compensation package based on experienceOpportunities for professional growth and developmentPrivate Medical PlanUse of Costa Navarino Facilities, according to the relevant policies', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση / Μερική απασχόληση'),
(653001, 'Cluster Revenue Manager, Costa Navarino (2025)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/305885', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν ένα λεπτό', '2026-04-16 15:02:22', 'Costa Navarino', 'Costa Navarino is a sustainably driven destination in the Mediterranean, located in Messinia in the southwest Peloponnese. Graced with a breath-taking seaside landscape, this is a region shaped by 4,500 years of history. The Costa Navarino philosophy is driven by a genuine desire to preserve the natural beauty and heritage of Messinia. It is currently home to four 5-star hotels, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort Costa Navarino at Navarino Dunes, W Costa Navarino and Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino at Navarino Bay.The destination comprises several distinct sites featuring five-star hotels, luxury private residences, a world-class golf experience, and many year-round activities. Navarino Dunes is home to The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort, The Westin Resort Costa Navarino and Costa Navarino Residences. Navarino Bay is the setting for Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino, W Costa Navarino and Navarino Agora, a curated marketplace. Both sites have signature golf courses, while at Navarino Hills there are two further signature golf courses.Costa Navarino is looking for its next Revenue Management Manager. The selected candidate will be responsible for driving hotel revenue and profitability by developing and implementing effective pricing and inventory strategies across all segments and channels. Aligned with brand guidelines, this role analyzes market trends, monitors competitor performance, and collaborates with cross-functional teams to optimize business mix, forecast demand, and support strategic decision-making.ResponsibilitiesDeveloping overall pricing strategy, in alignment with Marriott Divisional Pricing Guidelines including all market segments (retail, group, wholesale) and distribution channels and executing hotel’s strategic plan.Effectively managing inventory and pricing strategy in all distribution channels including branded web, 3rd party sites, and the GDS. Checks distribution channels for hotel positioning, information accuracy and competitor positioning.Collaborate with the Account Manager and Director of Sales & Marketing (DOSM) in the decision-making process of marketing promotions/campaigns participation, and rates.Communicate market direction & revenue management strategies to sales team, hotel leaders, and internal key stakeholders.Closely monitoring competitive pricing and set selective sell guidelines for groups and coordinate management of group business closely with the sales and event teams.Pro-actively identifying Soft Spot periods and prepare a Soft Spot Revenue Management Plan, in cooperation with Sales, Marketing, with the engagement of Corporate and Regional resources.Explore opportunities that drive profit, drive Market Share and Revenue Performance through proper pricing and mix management.Analyse competitive reports and formulate appropriate strategies through use of Market share tools, STR. Analysing information, identifying current and potential problems and propose solutions.Responsible for effective implementation and compliance with all Marriott Revenue Management Standards, Policies & Procedures. (Rate Plan Configuration, Market Segmentation, PMS-Opera related RM functionalities).Utilize brand’s revenue management systems and tools to ensure that revenue and profit are maximized.Demonstrate knowledge of job-relevant issues, products, systems, and processes.Responsible for administration and use of the One Yield tool and the accuracy of all rooms’ data as input into the system.All Rate Solicitations acted upon in a timely manner and rate plans maintenance and extended as appropriate. Maintain accurate reservation system information.Ensures that sales strategies and rate restrictions are communicated, implemented, and modified as market conditions fluctuate.Actively looking at trends for mid/long term, along with historical data and develop an action plan as a team (Rev Mgt, S&M, GM, Finance) to take advantage of opportunities or minimize risks.Generate and provides accurate and timely results in the form of reports, presentations, etc. Submit reports in a timely manner, ensuring delivery deadlines.Responsible for the preparation of 30-60-90 day fully updated Forecasts monthly.Responsible for preparation and presentation of Rooms Revenue Management elements as part of the Annual Budget Process and Budget Presentations.Leading the property’s weekly Revenue Management/Strategy Meeting.Utilize interpersonal and communication skills to lead, influence, and encourage others; advocates sound financial/business decision-making; demonstrates honesty/integrity; leads by example.Complete understanding and effective execution of current and new Revenue Management systems and Tools. Includes Opera PMS/One Yield/HPP/MARSHA/ MarRFP, EMPOWER etc.Requirements 4-year bachelor’s degree from an accredited university in Business Administration, Finance and Accounting, Economics, Hotel Management, or related major 3+ years direct experience in Revenue Management in 5* Branded Hotels Fluent English Analytical and advance Excel skills. Strong preference for analysing and organizing numerical, statistical, and financial data Strong preference for setting up and using systems to monitor and evaluate information from a wide variety of sources Develop constructive and cooperative working relationships with others and maintains them over time. Develop and manages internal key stakeholder relationships. Problem solver and attention to detail Action oriented with a drive for results Effective communication, presentational and influencing skills Marriott brand and system knowledge will a bonus Benefits Competitive compensation package On going training opportunities Private Medical Plan', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση / Μερική απασχόληση'),
(653002, 'Chef de Partie, W Costa Navarino (2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/304191', 'Πύλος', 'πριν ένα λεπτό', '2026-04-16 15:02:22', 'Costa Navarino', 'Costa Navarino is in Messinia in the southwest Peloponnese, in one of the most unspoiled and breathtaking landscapes in the Mediterranean. It is currently home to four 5-star deluxe hotels, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort at Navarino Dunes, W-Costa Navarino and Mandarin Oriental at Navarino Bay. In the coming years, more upscale branded hotels will be added to our portfolio, both in Messinia and Athens.Navarino Dunes Costa Navarino facilities include 766 bedroom units award winning Anazoe Spa, a 4,000m2 spa & thalassotherapy center, four multi-awarded, signature golf courses, over 20 fine dining venues, 5,000 m2 House of Events and a wide range of sports, such as the “Mouratoglou Tennis Center”, Bayern Munich football academy, Navarino Outdoor and many more.W Costa Navarino, exclusively for adults and young adults over 12 years old, offers 226 stylish rooms, 2 bedroom suites and 3 bedroom villas with infinity private pools, staged in the Bay of Navarino with stunning Ionian Sea views, The Watersports Center, The Away Spa and gym with a heated 25m-long lap pool, including the new Navarino Agora, an open marketplace with retail, street food, open-air cinema and exciting programming throughout the day and night.W Costa Navarino is seeking for a Chef De Partie to make an impact on this job. The successful candidate will strongly support the Sous Chef, will be responsible for food preparation, maintaining consistency, will be an expert in kitchen and will be passionate about creating recipes guest will remember.Responsibilities Estimate and communicate daily production needs Demonstrate proper and safe usage of all kitchen equipment Have knowledge of all standard procedures and policies pertaining to food preparation, receiving, storage and sanitation Respond appropriately to guests’ needs during the hours of operation Have the ability to support the control of food cost Be able to clearly define productivity standards with quality requirements and methods required to obtain them Check that all food and beverage outlets’ orders are at the correct level and do not surpass the stocks which are required Requirements Minimum of 5 years’ experience in the sector, including a minimum of 2 years as a Chef De Partie in an international 5*hotel chain A culinary degree Ability to speak, write and converse freely in English. Ability to speak, write and converse freely in Greek is desirable. Strong computer skills Good hygiene knowledge and HACCP Standards High energy, ability to work under pressure, good organizational skills and interpersonal skills BenefitsWhat We Offer: Competitive Compensation Package Private Medical Plan Accommodation in the vicinity of Costa Navarino (for non-Messinian associates) Meals Provided On-site Personal & Professional Growth: Ongoing Training & Development Opportunities Potential for Task Force Assignments Abroad in Marriott Hotels Exposure to an International Work Environment Wellbeing & Perks: Use of Costa Navarino Facilities (subject to internal policies) Access to the Support Room – Online Wellness Platform Discounts at Marriott Hotels Worldwide', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653003, 'Butler, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort Costa Navarino (2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/298653', 'Πύλος', 'πριν 3 ώρες', '2026-04-16 15:02:24', 'Costa Navarino', 'Costa Navarino is in Messinia in the southwest Peloponnese, in one of the most unspoiled and breathtaking landscapes in the Mediterranean. It is currently home to four 5-star deluxe hotels, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort at Navarino Dunes, W-Costa Navarino and Mandarin Oriental at Navarino Bay. In the coming years, more upscale branded hotels will be added to our portfolio, both in Messinia and Athens.Navarino Dunes Costa Navarino facilities include 766 bedroom units award winning Anazoe Spa, a 4,000m2 spa & thalassotherapy center, four multi-awarded, signature golf courses, over 20 fine dining venues, 5,000 m2 House of Events and a wide range of sports, such as the “Mouratoglou Tennis Center”, Bayern Munich football academy, Navarino Outdoor and many more.W Costa Navarino, exclusively for adults and young adults over 12 years old, offers 226 stylish rooms, 2 bedroom suites and 3 bedroom villas with infinity private pools, staged in the Bay of Navarino with stunning Ionian Sea views, The Watersports Center, The Away Spa and gym with a heated 25m-long lap pool, including the new Navarino Agora, an open marketplace with retail, street food, open-air cinema and exciting programming throughout the day and night.The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort, is seeking a Butler to make an impact on this job. The successful candidate will create memorable stays for our Ionian Exclusive guests by being actively engaged in the onsite guest experience. Impeccably mannered and discreet, butlers are available to satisfy our Ionian Exclusive guests’ needs throughout their stay. Responsibilities Prepare the suites/villas and make sure that all guest requests / preferences/ requested items as noted in the prearrival contact are fulfilled. Greet and interact with suite/villas guests upon arrival. Escort guests to rooms. Offer and explain butler service. Deliver to each suite/villa refreshing amenities, on a daily basis. Provide F&B services to guests in suites/villas. Assist with departure plans the day prior to departure and assist guests accordingly. In charge of packing and unpacking of guest’s belongings. Assist with maintaining and updating current guest files, specifically targeting guest preferences, stay patterns and personal profiles. Use data to create tailor made experiences. Direct, coach, support and supervise runners/trainees. Ensure that each person under supervision reports to their assignment on time and according to job description manual. Anticipate and attend courteously, timely and with discretion to guest needs. Resolve any complaints or issues. Act as a concierge regarding guests’ daily arrangements. Knowledge of menus, facilities, activities etc. Arrange and perform transfers in the resort. Adhere and maintain all etiquette protocol, always offering safe and courteous service. Communicate all guest requests to relevant departments or operators, timely and accurately. Follow all H&S rules, hotel policies, SOPs and Brand Standards at all times. Guide and encourage team to do the same. Attend all trainings and seminars provided by the company and continuously remain updated for all trends and market news. Requirements High school Diploma Ability to speak, write and converse fluently in Greek and English. Additional languages are a plus. Excellent communication and customer service skills Thorough knowledge of food products, standard recipes, and proper preparation. Must possess a strong desire to provide extraordinary guest service. Ability to operate hotel systems & other software programs (computer skills) Ability to handle difficult and stressful situations / work under pressure and under supervision Negotiation / Upselling skills / Telephone skills BenefitsWhat We Offer: Competitive Compensation Package Private Medical Plan Accommodation in the vicinity of Costa Navarino (for non-Messinian associates) Meals Provided On-site Personal & Professional Growth: Ongoing Training & Development Opportunities Potential for Task Force Assignments Abroad in Marriott Hotels Exposure to an International Work Environment Wellbeing & Perks: Use of Costa Navarino Facilities (subject to internal policies) Access to the Support Room – Online Wellness Platform Discounts at Marriott Hotels Worldwide', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653004, 'Chef de Partie, Costa Navarino (2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/304190', 'Πύλος', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-16 15:02:24', 'Costa Navarino', 'Costa Navarino is in Messinia in the southwest Peloponnese, in one of the most unspoiled and breathtaking landscapes in the Mediterranean. It is currently home to four 5-star deluxe hotels, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort at Navarino Dunes, W-Costa Navarino and Mandarin Oriental at Navarino Bay. In the coming years, more upscale branded hotels will be added to our portfolio, both in Messinia and Athens.Navarino Dunes Costa Navarino facilities include 766 bedroom units award winning Anazoe Spa, a 4,000m2 spa & thalassotherapy center, four multi-awarded, signature golf courses, over 20 fine dining venues, 5,000 m2 House of Events and a wide range of sports, such as the “Mouratoglou Tennis Center”, Bayern Munich football academy, Navarino Outdoor and many more.W Costa Navarino, exclusively for adults and young adults over 12 years old, offers 226 stylish rooms, 2 bedroom suites and 3 bedroom villas with infinity private pools, staged in the Bay of Navarino with stunning Ionian Sea views, The Watersports Center, The Away Spa and gym with a heated 25m-long lap pool, including the new Navarino Agora, an open marketplace with retail, street food, open-air cinema and exciting programming throughout the day and night.Costa Navarino is looking for a Chef de Partie. The selected candidate will be responsible for mentoring and supervising their team, ensuring tasks are effectively allocated and monitoring inventory and costs. They will oversee the production and quality control of dishes in line with brand standards and the guidance of their superiors. The role requires excellent collaboration with other departments and the ability to resolve issues and address special customer requests promptly.Responsibilities Follows all company policy procedures related to food preparation, receipt, storage and handling Full knowledge of the menu, its recipes, its production methods and the presentation of the dishes according to the company\'s brand standards Quality control of raw materials and specifications To organize, guide and distribute responsibilities to the team according to daily needs Operation: Presentation and listing of recipes according to brand standards Attendance of all trainings and seminars provided by the company and up-to-date knowledge on materials and procedures Ability to complete responsibilities correctly and consistently within the time frames we have set for completing departmental goals Solving problems and satisfying special customer requests Knowledge and adherence to meal preparation procedures for allergies and dietary habits Requirements At least four years of progressive culinary experience, with a minimum of two years as a Demi Chef de Partie, preferably in a five-star hotel. Degree from IEK or Culinary School (2 years). Fluent in Greek and English, both written and spoken. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Comprehensive knowledge of raw materials, recipes, and presentation techniques. Skilled in creating and standardizing recipes. Able to identify allergens in raw materials and recipes with attention to safety and compliance. Proficient in computer skills, including Microsoft Office (Word, Excel), and internet navigation. Experienced in the proper operation and management of kitchen equipment and machinery. Familiar with HACCP protocols and ISO 22000 standards, including accurate completion of required forms. Capable of giving clear instructions and leading a team effectively. Able to understand and analyze P&L reports, with a focus on managing food costs. Skilled in managing inventory, warehouse stock, and refrigerators within assigned areas of responsibility. Proficient in all fundamental hot and cold kitchen techniques. BenefitsWhat We Offer: Competitive Compensation Package Private Medical Plan Accommodation in the vicinity of Costa Navarino (for non-Messinian associates) Meals Provided On-site Personal & Professional Growth: Ongoing Training & Development Opportunities Potential for Task Force Assignments Abroad in Marriott Hotels Exposure to an International Work Environment Wellbeing & Perks: Use of Costa Navarino Facilities (subject to internal policies) Access to the Support Room – Online Wellness Platform Discounts at Marriott Hotels Worldwide', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653005, 'Bell Attendant, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort Costa Navarino (2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/305884', 'Πύλος', 'πριν μερικά δευτερόλεπτα', '2026-04-16 15:02:26', 'Costa Navarino', 'Costa Navarino is a sustainably driven destination in the Mediterranean, located in Messinia in the southwest Peloponnese. Graced with a breath-taking seaside landscape, this is a region shaped by 4,500 years of history. The Costa Navarino philosophy is driven by a genuine desire to preserve the natural beauty and heritage of Messinia. It is currently home to four 5-star hotels, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort Costa Navarino at Navarino Dunes, W Costa Navarino and Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino at Navarino Bay.The destination comprises several distinct sites featuring five-star hotels, luxury private residences, a world-class golf experience, and many year-round activities. Navarino Dunes is home to The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort, The Westin Resort Costa Navarino and Costa Navarino Residences. Navarino Bay is the setting for Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino, W Costa Navarino and Navarino Agora, a curated marketplace. Both sites have signature golf courses, while at Navarino Hills there are two further signature golf courses.The The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort, is seeking a Bell Attendant to make an impact on this job. The successful candidate is primarily responsible for welcoming all guests to the hotel as well as bidding them farewell. The Bell Attendant escorts guests to and from their accommodations, orienting them with the features of the property and their accommodations, assisting the guest in any way to make them feel more comfortable and welcome to the hotel.ResponsibilitiesWelcome guests as per brand standards and direct them to Reception area.Load and unload luggage from vehicles and deliver it to rooms. Offer valet services. Ensure guests’ luggage security in his care and safely store them and provide guest with a receipt.Answer guest questions; escalate guest issues to a supervisor.Be aware of daily functions, events, VIP and group arrivals.Escort guests to rooms; provide all necessary room information.Report any issues from guests, groups, as well as technical issues spotted around the resort.Ensure that all equipment is well maintained & in good operational condition.Actively promote the online reputation of the hotel by encouraging guests to post reviews on social media.Transfer guests with golf buggy within the resort upon request.Follow all H&S rules, hotel policies, SOPs, and Brand Standards at all times. Attend all trainings and seminars provided by the company and continuously remain updated for all trends and market newsRequirements High school Diploma 1 year of experience preferred Excellent knowledge of Opera PMS / MS Office is preferred Excellent knowledge of Marriott platforms is considered an asset Excellent knowledge of English & local language. Additional language is considered an asset Excellent knowledge of Marriott Bonvoy loyalty program is considered is considered an asset BenefitsWhat We Offer: Competitive Compensation Package Private Medical Plan Accommodation in the vicinity of Costa Navarino (for non-Messinian associates) Meals Provided On-site Personal & Professional Growth: Ongoing Training & Development Opportunities Potential for Task Force Assignments Abroad in Marriott Hotels Exposure to an International Work Environment Wellbeing & Perks: Use of Costa Navarino Facilities (subject to internal policies) Access to the Support Room – Online Wellness Platform Discounts at Marriott Hotels Worldwide', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653006, 'ΥΠΑΛΛΗΛΟΣ ΕΛΕΓΧΟΥ ΠΟΙΟΤΗΤΑΣ', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/production-jobs/305878', 'Σχηματάρι', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-16 15:02:26', 'DUNAPACK PACKAGING ΕΛΛΑΣ ΜΟΝ. ΑΕΒΕ', 'Η DUNAPACK PACKAGING HELLAS AEBE, μέλος του πολυεθνικού Αυστριακού Ομίλου Prinzhorn Group, με ηγετική θέση στον χώρο της συσκευασίας, αναζητά ταλαντούχους ανθρώπους, που θα ενδυναμώσουν την ομάδα της και θα εξελιχθούν μαζί της και συγκεκριμένα:  ΥΠΑΛΛΗΛΟΣ ΕΛΕΓΧΟΥ ΠΟΙΟΤΗΤΑΣ ΠΕΡΙΓΡΑΦΗ ΘΕΣΗΣ Να κάνει μετρήσεις σύμφωνα με τις τεχνικές προδιαγραφές. Να παρακολουθεί και να τηρεί την Διαδικασία Ποιοτικού Ελέγχου. Διαχείριση ενοτήτων του Σχεδίου Διασφάλισης Ποιότητας & Περιβάλλοντος με την επίβλεψη του Υπεύθυνου Διασφάλισης Ποιότητας. Εποπτεία και συντονισμός υλοποίησης διορθωτικών και προληπτικών ενεργειών, Να επαληθεύει με εργαστηριακές μετρήσεις τις τεχνικές προδιαγραφές των Α υλών (χαρτιά) αλλά και τελικών προϊόντων. Να επιμελείται του εργαστηριακού χώρου και να επικοινωνεί με τους προμηθευτές των εργαστηριακών οργάνων. ΠΡΟΦΙΛ ΥΠΟΨΗΦΙΟΥ 3 έτη σε τμήμα Ποιοτικού Ελέγχου Πτυχίο Τεχνολογικής ή Μηχανολογικής κατεύθυνσης  Εμπειρία στον κλάδο της κυτιοποιίας επιθυμητή Πολύ καλή γνώση Αγγλικών Γνώση Η/Υ (OFFICE) Επιθυμητή γνώση συστημάτων ERP Ευελιξία και ικανότητα διαχείρισης προβλημάτων  Ικανότητα επικοινωνίας, προγραμματισμού και οργάνωσης Αίσθημα ευθύνης, συνέπεια και ακεραιότητα Δυνατότητα εργασίας σε 3 βάρδιες ΠΑΚΕΤΟ ΠΑΡΟΧΩΝ Αποδοχές αναλόγως προσόντων Ιδιωτική ασφάλεια Μεταφορά προσωπικού Δυνατότητες εκπαίδευσης και ανάπτυξης Ευκαιρίες εξέλιξης Θα προτιμηθούν βιογραφικά από την ευρύτερη περιοχή Σχηματαρίου. Στείλτε το βιογραφικό σας σημείωμα στο [email protected].  Όλες οι αιτήσεις θεωρούνται απόλυτα εμπιστευτικές. Θα επικοινωνήσουμε μόνο με τους υποψήφιους που ανταποκρίνονται στις απαιτήσεις της θέσης. Για οποιαδήποτε πληροφορία μπορείτε να απευθυνθείτε στο Τμήμα Ανθρώπινου Δυναμικού (HR) στο τηλέφωνο 2262057906 (εσωτ.*208 Ηλιάνα Μπίτου, Υπεύθυνη Προσλήψεων).', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653007, 'Barista/Bartender, Costa Navarino (2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/305883', 'Πύλος', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-16 15:02:28', 'Costa Navarino', 'Costa Navarino is a sustainably driven destination in the Mediterranean, located in Messinia in the southwest Peloponnese. Graced with a breath-taking seaside landscape, this is a region shaped by 4,500 years of history. The Costa Navarino philosophy is driven by a genuine desire to preserve the natural beauty and heritage of Messinia. It is currently home to four 5-star hotels, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort Costa Navarino at Navarino Dunes, W Costa Navarino and Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino at Navarino Bay.The destination comprises several distinct sites featuring five-star hotels, luxury private residences, a world-class golf experience, and many year-round activities. Navarino Dunes is home to The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort, The Westin Resort Costa Navarino and Costa Navarino Residences. Navarino Bay is the setting for Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino, W Costa Navarino and Navarino Agora, a curated marketplace. Both sites have signature golf courses, while at Navarino Hills there are two further signature golf courses.The award-winning The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort Costa Navarino are seeking for a Barista/Bartender dedicated in ensuring the perfectness in every detail and customer service, creating memorable experiences, in an excellent working environment. A Barista must organize and oversee the daily operation of the bar by ensuring daily preparation for operational needs, excellent knowledge of all coffee recipes and coffee machine functions. Must demonstrate creativity and commitment to the team and collaborate smoothly. Required to have guest-oriented attitude and must always offer high quality services through every interaction to offer a memorable stay.ResponsibilitiesGreet and welcome guests in a courteous manner, take orders and serve with accuracy, while demonstrating upselling techniques. Prepare and serve hot and cold beverages and have basic knowledge of classic and signature cocktail recipes.Organize and prepare the mise en place at all bar sections, in a timely manner and according to brand standards. Check daily the stock retail products and refill stations according to operational needs. Must be able to work under pressure and high volume operation effectively and seamlessly Ensure all equipment is clean and properly functioning, as well as ensure the cleanliness of the BOH.Follow all SOPs to ensure operational excellence and ensure brand standards are followed at all times. Follow all H&S rules, hotel policies, SOPs and Brand Standards at all times. Attend all trainings and seminars provided by the company and continuously remain updated for all trends and market news.RequirementsTo be successful in this role you will: Have 2 years’ experience in the Food and Beverage industry - Service experience at a 5* hotel preferred Excellent knowledge of drink recipes and mixology techniques, along with selling and upselling skills. Speak, write and converse freely in English. Knowledge of Greek, German and/or Russian language is an advantage. Have good computer skills. Good knowledge of MICROS and POS systems. H&S, Brand Standards and Company procedures knowledge is highly preferred. Be a great communicator who allures guests from all over the world, with enviable customer service skills. Set the example with your proper communication etiquette (both written and spoken) towards internal and external guests Have unflappable temperament and professional integrity. Be an inspiring team player. Attention to detail and a passion for delivering high-quality beverages BenefitsWhat We Offer: Competitive Compensation Package Private Medical Plan Accommodation in the vicinity of Costa Navarino (for non-Messinian associates) Meals Provided On-site Personal & Professional Growth: Ongoing Training & Development Opportunities Potential for Task Force Assignments Abroad in Marriott Hotels Exposure to an International Work Environment Wellbeing & Perks: Use of Costa Navarino Facilities (subject to internal policies) Access to the Support Room – Online Wellness Platform Discounts at Marriott Hotels Worldwide', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653008, 'Barista, Kafeneio Deli', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/298011', 'Πύλος', 'πριν ένα λεπτό', '2026-04-16 15:02:28', 'Costa Navarino', 'At Costa Navarino, in collaboration with Chef Alexandros Tsiotinis, our restaurant portfolio offers different expressions of Greek and Mediterranean hospitality. From the refined yet relaxed dining experience of Parafrasi by CTC — where contemporary culinary creativity meets thoughtful service — to the warm, traditional and flavour-driven character of Kafeneio Deli and Souvlakeri, each concept carries its own identity and rhythm. What connects them all is a shared commitment to quality ingredients, genuine human interaction and a service culture built on teamwork and consistency. As we prepare for the season, we are looking to grow our teams with individuals who take pride in their work, thrive in a dynamic environment and understand that hospitality is, above all, about people.We are recruiting a Barista for Kafeneio Deli who can deliver high-quality coffee while creating a friendly and welcoming environment for our guests. The role requires attention to detail, consistency and speed, combined with a warm and professional attitude. A genuine interest in coffee culture and guest interaction will be highly valued. ResponsibilitiesGreet and welcome guests in a courteous manner, take orders and serve with accuracy, while demonstrating upselling techniques. Prepare and serve hot and cold beverages.Organize and prepare the mise en place at all bar sections, in a timely manner and according to brand standards. Check daily the stock retail products and refill stations according to operational needs. Must be able to work under pressure and high volume operation effectively and seamlessly Ensure all equipment is clean and properly functioning, as well as ensure the cleanliness of the BOH.Follow all SOPs to ensure operational excellence and ensure brand standards are followed at all times. Follow all H&S rules, SOPs and Brand Standards at all times. Attend all trainings and seminars provided by the company and continuously remain updated for all trends and market news.RequirementsTo be successful in this role you will:Have 2 years’ experience in the Food and Beverage industry.Excellent knowledge of drink recipes and mixology techniques, along with selling and upselling skills.Speak, write and converse freely in English. Knowledge of Greek, German and/or Russian language is an advantage.Have good computer skills. Good knowledge of MICROS and POS systems.H&S, Brand Standards and Company procedures knowledge is highly preferred.Be a great communicator who allures guests from all over the world, with enviable customer service skills. Set the example with your proper communication etiquette (both written and spoken) towards internal and external guestsHave unflappable temperament and professional integrity. Be an inspiring team player.Attention to detail and a passion for delivering high-quality beveragesBenefitsCompetitive Compensation Package.Ongoing Training & Development Opportunities.Exposure to an International Work Environment.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653009, 'Bar Waiter/Waitress, Costa Navarino (2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/305882', 'Πύλος', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-16 15:02:30', 'Costa Navarino', 'Costa Navarino is a sustainably driven destination in the Mediterranean, located in Messinia in the southwest Peloponnese. Graced with a breath-taking seaside landscape, this is a region shaped by 4,500 years of history. The Costa Navarino philosophy is driven by a genuine desire to preserve the natural beauty and heritage of Messinia. It is currently home to four 5-star hotels, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort Costa Navarino at Navarino Dunes, W Costa Navarino and Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino at Navarino Bay.The destination comprises several distinct sites featuring five-star hotels, luxury private residences, a world-class golf experience, and many year-round activities. Navarino Dunes is home to The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort, The Westin Resort Costa Navarino and Costa Navarino Residences. Navarino Bay is the setting for Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino, W Costa Navarino and Navarino Agora, a curated marketplace. Both sites have signature golf courses, while at Navarino Hills there are two further signature golf courses.Costa Navarino is looking for a Bar Waiter / Waitress. The selected candidate will ensure that the level of service provided is always impeccable, has excellent knowledge of recipes and products, ensuring the proper recommendations to uplift the guest experience. Apart from delivering beverages and snacks, a guest-oriented attitude is required and offering at all times high quality services by taking the extra step.ResponsibilitiesPrepare and organize mise en place based on daily outlet needs, to ensure smooth operations as per brand standards. Excellent knowledge of all products and recipes, while demonstrating selling and upselling skills.Greet and welcome guests in a courteous manner. Take orders and serve with accuracy, following brand standards.Follow all SOP procedures to ensure operational excellence.Handle cash transactions accurately, process payments, and provide change as needed.Follow all H&S rules, hotel policies, SOPs and Brand Standards at all times. Guide and encourage team to do the same.Attend all trainings and seminars provided by the company and continuously remain updated for all trends and market newsRequirements Fluent in English and Greek Good communication skills, both verbal and written Multitasking abilities / Flexibility / Positivity Good knowledge of MICROS and POS systems Basic Wine knowledge Customer service skills, including selling and upselling skills Ability to train and lead others BenefitsWhat We Offer: Competitive Compensation Package Private Medical Plan Accommodation in the vicinity of Costa Navarino (for non-Messinian associates) Meals Provided On-site Personal & Professional Growth: Ongoing Training & Development Opportunities Potential for Task Force Assignments Abroad in Marriott Hotels Exposure to an International Work Environment Wellbeing & Perks: Use of Costa Navarino Facilities (subject to internal policies) Access to the Support Room – Online Wellness Platform Discounts at Marriott Hotels Worldwide', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653010, 'Bar Team Leader, Costa Navarino (2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/299635', 'Πύλος', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-16 15:02:30', 'Costa Navarino', 'Costa Navarino is in Messinia in the southwest Peloponnese, in one of the most unspoiled and breathtaking landscapes in the Mediterranean. It is currently home to four 5-star deluxe hotels, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort at Navarino Dunes, W-Costa Navarino and Mandarin Oriental at Navarino Bay. In the coming years, more upscale branded hotels will be added to our portfolio, both in Messinia and Athens.Navarino Dunes Costa Navarino facilities include 766 bedroom units award winning Anazoe Spa, a 4,000m2 spa & thalassotherapy center, four multi-awarded, signature golf courses, over 20 fine dining venues, 5,000 m2 House of Events and a wide range of sports, such as the “Mouratoglou Tennis Center”, Bayern Munich football academy, Navarino Outdoor and many more.W Costa Navarino, exclusively for adults and young adults over 12 years old, offers 226 stylish rooms, 2 bedroom suites and 3 bedroom villas with infinity private pools, staged in the Bay of Navarino with stunning Ionian Sea views, The Watersports Center, The Away Spa and gym with a heated 25m-long lap pool, including the new Navarino Agora, an open marketplace with retail, street food, open-air cinema and exciting programming throughout the day and night.The award-winning The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort Costa Navarino are seeking for Bar Team Leaders to support the Bar Manager in all aspects of the Food and Beverage and each Outlet’s operation. A Bar Team Leader must be able to organize and proactively prepare the outlet. Must have excellent knowledge of all products offered and of the SOPs to ensure seamless operation, check and monitor par stock levels and be able to assist when needed in all aspects of administration responsibilities. Functioning as the main link on passing on the vision to all team members and must ensure that the team efforts are aligned to offer impeccable services throughout the outlet operation.Responsibilities Organize daily outlet operations in a timely manner and according to brand standards. Ensure all equipment is operable and in working condition. Excellent knowledge of menu, beverage, and snack items as well as all beverage recipes and classic / signature cocktails. Greet and welcome guests in a courteous manner, take orders and serve with accuracy, demonstrate upselling knowledge. Excellent knowledge of brand standards, and SOP procedures, ensuring that they are constantly followed. Assist at all times and locations, to ensure a flawless operation. Responsible for the overall supervision of all associates, as per brand standards, maintaining a positive attitude, mentoring and ensuring their development. Organize, monitor and check unit stock and ensure effective ordering through MC. Handle and solve efficiently guest complaints, ensuring a memorable experience for all guests. Assist and manage when needed in all administrational organization (weekly schedules / HR needs / Financial Management) and operational needs throughout the department. Follow all H&S rules, hotel policies, SOPs and Brand Standards at all times. Guide and encourage team to do the same. Attend all trainings and seminars provided by the company and continuously remain updated for all trends and market news. Requirements Minimum of 2 years’ experience in a similar position (ideally in an international hotel chain) Bachelor’s degree in Hospitality / Tourism management / Relevant Certification is highly desired Fluent in English and Greek Technical bar knowledge (recipes, equipment) Good knowledge of MICROS, POS and PC systems H&S, Brand Standards and Company procedures knowledge is highly desirable Excellent Communication skills, Customer service skills, as well as selling and upselling skills Good people management skills Planning, organizing and time management skills Ability to lead by example BenefitsWhat We Offer: Competitive Compensation Package Private Medical Plan Accommodation in the vicinity of Costa Navarino (for non-Messinian associates) Meals Provided On-site Personal & Professional Growth: Ongoing Training & Development Opportunities Potential for Task Force Assignments Abroad in Marriott Hotels Exposure to an International Work Environment Wellbeing & Perks: Use of Costa Navarino Facilities (subject to internal policies) Access to the Support Room – Online Wellness Platform Discounts at Marriott Hotels Worldwide', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653011, 'Bakery Chef de Partie, Costa Navarino (2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/305881', 'Πύλος', 'πριν μερικά δευτερόλεπτα', '2026-04-16 15:02:32', 'Costa Navarino', 'Costa Navarino is a sustainably driven destination in the Mediterranean, located in Messinia in the southwest Peloponnese. Graced with a breath-taking seaside landscape, this is a region shaped by 4,500 years of history. The Costa Navarino philosophy is driven by a genuine desire to preserve the natural beauty and heritage of Messinia. It is currently home to four 5-star hotels, The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort and The Westin Resort Costa Navarino at Navarino Dunes, W Costa Navarino and Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino at Navarino Bay.The destination comprises several distinct sites featuring five-star hotels, luxury private residences, a world-class golf experience, and many year-round activities. Navarino Dunes is home to The Romanos, a Luxury Collection Resort, The Westin Resort Costa Navarino and Costa Navarino Residences. Navarino Bay is the setting for Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino, W Costa Navarino and Navarino Agora, a curated marketplace. Both sites have signature golf courses, while at Navarino Hills there are two further signature golf courses.Costa Navarino is looking for a Bakery Chef de Partie. The selected candidate will demonstrate proper and safe usage of all bakery equipment, have knowledge of all standard procedures and policies pertaining to food preparation with HAACP. They will respond appropriately to quests needs while preparing and baking different bread types with brand standards. They will help the Head Baker to develop new products for the outlets while supporting food cost and food waste. They will check all the outlets orders and BEO and assist and oversee subordinates while maintaining adequate supply and ensures proper storage and refrigeration. They will decorate themed buffets set up and assist with the material orders and check the deliveries.ResponsibilitiesAssessment and communication of daily production needs in collaboration with the Junior Sous chefPreparation and creation of the Baked products and themed buffetsDemonstrate proper and safe usage of all pastry equipment.Have knowledge of all standard procedures and policies pertaining to food preparation, receiving, storage and sanitationRespond appropriately to guests’ needs during the hours of operationSupport the control of food costsBe able to clearly define productivity standards with quality requirements and methods required to obtain themCheck that all food and beverage outlets’ orders are at the correct level and do not surpass the stocks which are requiredAssist the Sous Chef with material orders and check the deliveriesMake sure all the HAACP documents are filled dailyCheck the BEO for upcoming events and help with the necessary preparationHelp and oversee the subordinates with the tasks that are assignedRequirements Minimum 5 years’ experience in the sector, or at least 1 year at the same position Pastry Degree Ability to speak, write and converse freely in both Greek and English Basic computer skills Good hygiene knowledge and HACCP Standards High energy, ability to work under pressure, good organizational skills and interpersonal skills Lead by example Compliance with the cleaning schedule BenefitsWhat We Offer: Competitive Compensation Package Private Medical Plan Accommodation in the vicinity of Costa Navarino (for non-Messinian associates) Meals Provided On-site Personal & Professional Growth: Ongoing Training & Development Opportunities Potential for Task Force Assignments Abroad in Marriott Hotels Exposure to an International Work Environment Wellbeing & Perks: Use of Costa Navarino Facilities (subject to internal policies) Access to the Support Room – Online Wellness Platform Discounts at Marriott Hotels Worldwide', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση');
