(653651, 'Paperpack Μονοπρόσωπη ΑΒΕΕ - Χειριστής Αμφίπλευρης Εκτυπωτικής Μηχανής', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/technicians-or-service-jobs/306387?origin=pjp', 'Μεταμόρφωση', 'πριν 16 λεπτά', '2026-04-17 15:02:15', 'Recruitment Services | Kariera.Group', 'Η ομάδα των Recruitment Services του kariera.gr απαρτίζεται από εξειδικευμένους επαγγελματίες που αναλαμβάνουν τη στελέχωση θέσεων πολλών ειδικοτήτων και επιπέδων. Με εξατομικευμένη προσέγγιση και βαθιά γνώση του σύγχρονου εργασιακού τοπίου, συνδέουμε τα ταλέντα με τις επαγγελματικές ευκαιρίες που τους ταιριάζουν πραγματικά. Για λογαριασμό της Paperpack, μιας σύγχρονης βιομηχανίας χάρτινης συσκευασίας με πολυετή δυναμική παρουσία στον κλάδο , εξειδικευμένη στη δευτερογενή φαρμακευτική συσκευασία και σε προϊόντα υψηλών ποιοτικών προδιαγραφών, αναζητούμε Χειριστή Αμφίπλευρης Εκτυπωτικής Μηχανής. Με σύγχρονες εγκαταστάσεις και εξειδικευμένο προσωπικό, παράγουμε πτυσσόμενα κουτιά και φαρμακευτικά φύλλα οδηγιών, αξιοποιώντας τεχνολογίες εκτύπωσης υψηλής ακρίβειας και καινοτόμες παραγωγικές διαδικασίες. Επενδύουμε συνεχώς σε ανάπτυξη, αυτοματοποίηση και βιώσιμες πρακτικές, διασφαλίζοντας υψηλή ποιότητα, αξιοπιστία και ένα σύγχρονο εργασιακό περιβάλλον.   Κύριες Αρμοδιότητες: Χειρισμός και ρύθμιση εκτυπωτικών μηχανών Roland Hi Print Εκτύπωση αμφίπλευρων εργασιών σε λεπτά χαρτιά (40–100 gsm) Διασφάλιση υψηλής ποιότητας εκτύπωσης και σωστής ευθυγράμμισης (register) Ρύθμιση μελανιών, πιέσεων και τροφοδοσίας χαρτιού Βασική συντήρηση και αντιμετώπιση τεχνικών ζητημάτων Προαπαιτούμενα Προσόντα: Αποδεδειγμένη εμπειρία σε μηχανές Roland Hi Print Εξειδίκευση στην εκτύπωση λεπτού χαρτιού (40–60 gsm) Γνώση διαδικασιών offset εκτύπωσης Προσοχή στη λεπτομέρεια και υπευθυνότητα Δυνατότητα εργασίας σε κυλιόμενες βάρδιες Ικανότητα εργασίας υπό πίεση και τήρησης χρονοδιαγραμμάτων Επιθυμητά Προσόντα: Σπουδές ή τεχνική κατάρτιση στις γραφικές τέχνες Εμπειρία σε παραγωγικό περιβάλλον εκτυπωτικής μονάδας Η Εταιρεία Προσφέρει: Ανταγωνιστικό πακέτο αποδοχών Σταθερή εργασία σε σύγχρονο περιβάλλον Δυνατότητες επαγγελματικής εξέλιξης Ιδιωτική ασφάλιση υγείας Κυλιόμενο ωράριο εργασίας / Full time  Σύμβαση εργασίας αορίστου χρόνου', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653652, 'Digital Marketing Assistant - Heraklion, Crete', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/marketing-or-advertising-jobs/306384', 'Ηράκλειο', 'πριν 19 λεπτά', '2026-04-17 15:02:17', 'Metaxa Hospitality Group', 'Metaxa Hospitality Group, awarded as the \"Best Hospitality Group in Greece\" by the World Travel Awards 2021 - 2025, has been creating unique experiences of authentic hospitality for more than five decades and invites you to become a member of a group of multi-awarded in Crete and Santorini.Metaxa Hospitality Group is looking for its Sales & Marketing Department based in Heraklion:Digital Marketing AssistantWe are seeking a Digital Marketing Assistant to support the execution and day-to-day management of our digital marketing activities across the Group’s portfolio. The role will focus on campaign support, reporting, and operational coordination, contributing to the effectiveness and consistency of our digital presence.Key Responsibilities: Campaign Execution SupportAssist in the setup and implementation of digital campaigns across platforms (Google Ads, Meta Ads) Upload and manage campaign assets, ensuring accuracy and alignment with campaign requirements Perform quality checks before and during campaign launches Performance Monitoring & ReportingMonitor campaign performance on a daily basis and highlight any irregularities or optimization opportunities Prepare recurring reports and support the analysis of campaign performance Ensure accuracy and consistency of reported data Collaboration & Content CoordinationWork closely with the Copywriter and Art Director to support the development of cohesive and effective marketing campaigns Ensure alignment between campaign requirements and delivered creative assets across channelsOperational & Coordination SupportMaintain internal documentation and campaign structures Support coordination between Digital Marketing, other internal teams, and external collaboratorsRequirementsNecessary qualifications:Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Business Administration, or a related fieldBasic understanding of paid media platforms (Google Ads and/or Meta Ads)Knowledge of Social Media Marketing and social media management Proficiency in Microsoft Excel and familiarity with Microsoft 365 toolsVery good knowledge of the English language (both written and spoken)Strong attention to detail and organizational skillsAbility to manage multiple tasks in a structured and timely manner Desired qualifications:1–2 years of experience in digital marketing or a related field, ideally within the hospitality or tourism sectorFamiliarity with Google Ads and Meta Ads platforms Basic knowledge of Google Analytics  Soft SkillsProactive with a willingness to learn and develop Detail-oriented with a structured approach to execution Strong team collaboration and communication skills Ability to follow processes and ensure consistencyBenefitsCompetitive salary remunerationCareer development in a fast-paced, growing work environment.Training opportunities.Full year job Friendly work environment', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653653, 'Assistant Waiter/ress', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/306366', 'Γλυφάδα', 'πριν μερικά δευτερόλεπτα', '2026-04-17 15:02:17', 'ACE HOTEL&SWIM CLUB ATHENS', 'What We Look For Our ideal candidate reflects the energy and philosophy of SORA and brings: A genuine passion for hospitality, global flavors, and contemporary Pan-Asian cuisine Proven experience as a waiter/waitress in a luxury restaurant or rooftop venue Confidence working in a fast-paced, service-driven environment with strong attention to detail A collaborative mindset and the ability to perform seamlessly within a professional team Naturally warm, guest-focused personality with a talent for creating memorable dining experiences Professional presence, excellent communication skills, and a strong sense of responsibility', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(653654, 'HR Specialist', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/human-resources-jobs/306351?origin=pjp', 'Ελληνικό', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-17 15:02:19', 'INTER CARS GREECE ΜΟΝ. ΕΠΕ', 'Inter Cars Greece Single Member Liability Company is a subsidiary of Inter Cars S.A., the biggest importer and distributor of automotive spare parts and garage equipment in the Middle and Eastern Europe, with over 200 branches in Poland and more than 190 branches in Europe. Inter Cars Greece values passion and involvement, partnership, reliability, loyalty and leadership by example. Inter Cars Greece is seeking to strengthen its team with a new colleague for the position of Human Resources Specialist, based in Elliniko. The successful candidate will support daily HR operations and actively contribute to the continuous improvement and development of Human Resources processes. Responsibilities: Supporting and managing the employee lifecycle (onboarding – offboarding). Managing the recruitment process and actively supporting hiring decisions. Monitoring and updating the company’s organizational structure and charts. Supporting the performance evaluation process. Assisting managers and supervisors on HR policies and procedures. Participating in employer branding initiatives to strengthen the company’s image and attract top talent. Contributing to HR projects (process improvement, engagement initiatives, training programs). Supporting employees’ continuous development, by identifying training needs and coordinating training programs.  Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, or a related field 2–4 years of experience in a similar HR role Good knowledge of labor legislation Familiarity with HRIS / ERP systems (experience with SoftOne will be considered an asset) Good knowledge of MS Office Good command of the English language Strong organizational skills and attention to detail Excellent communication skills, professionalism, and a collaborative mindset Ability to effectively collaborate with different levels of hierarchy Hands‑on approach with a practical mindset Benefits: Opportunity to work in a dynamic, multinational environment Job stability within a growing and continuously evolving organization. Competitive remuneration package and private health insurance. Continuous training and professional development opportunities. Career development prospects.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653655, 'Υπάλληλος Καθαριότητας Γραφείων -BENNETT', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/306365?origin=pjp', 'Κηφισιά', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-17 15:02:19', 'Recruitment Services | Kariera.Group', ' H ομάδα των Recruitment Services του kariera.gr απαρτίζεται από εξειδικευμένους επαγγελματίες που αναλαμβάνουν τη στελέχωση θέσεων πολλών ειδικοτήτων και επιπέδων. Με εξατομικευμένη προσέγγιση και βαθιά γνώση του σύγχρονου εργασιακού τοπίου, συνδέουμε τα ταλέντα με τις επαγγελματικές ευκαιρίες που τους ταιριάζουν πραγματικά. Εκ μέρους της φαρμακευτικής εταιρεία Bennet αναζητούμε Υπάλληλο Καθαριότητας για τη φροντίδα και διατήρηση των χώρων γραφείων της, στην Κηφισία Αρμοδιότητες Καθημερινός καθαρισμός γραφειακών χώρων, meeting rooms και κοινόχρηστων χώρων Καθαρισμός κουζίνας και χώρων υγιεινής Διαχείριση απορριμμάτων Αναπλήρωση αναλώσιμων (χαρτικά, σαπούνια κ.λπ.) Διατήρηση υψηλών προτύπων καθαριότητας και υγιεινής Απαραίτητα Προσόντα Προϋπηρεσία σε αντίστοιχη θέση θα θεωρηθεί επιπλέον προσόν Υπευθυνότητα και συνέπεια Προσοχή στη λεπτομέρεια Επαγγελματική συμπεριφορά Παροχές Σταθερό και ευχάριστο εργασιακό περιβάλλον Συνεργασία με οργανωμένη εταιρεία στον χώρο της φαρμακευτικής αγοράς Ανταγωνιστικές αποδοχές 📍 Σημαντική Διευκρίνιση Η θέση αφορά καθαριότητα γραφείων και όχι εργοστασιακών εγκαταστάσεων. Εάν ενδιαφέρεστε να γίνετε μέλος μιας οργανωμένης και αξιόπιστης ομάδας, θα χαρούμε να λάβουμε την αίτησή σας.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653656, 'ΚΑΘΑΡΙΣΤΡΙΑ / ΚΑΘΑΡΙΣΤΗΣ', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/306362', 'Αχαρνές', 'πριν 14 λεπτά', '2026-04-17 15:02:21', 'TOI TOI HELLAS AE', 'Η Toi Toi Hellas ΑΕ, με έδρα τις Αχαρνές, που δραστηριοποιείται πανελλαδικά στον τομέα της παροχής υπηρεσιών υγιεινής και ιδιαίτερα στην ενοικίαση ποικίλων τύπων φορητών τουαλετών και αντίστοιχων ρυμουλκούμενων μονάδων, αναζητά υπάλληλο καθαρίστρια / καθαριστή με άδεια διπλώματος οδήγησης Β’ κατηγορίας. Ο κατάλληλος υποψήφιος/α θα πρέπει να έχει την δυνατότητα να εργάζεται με ευέλικτο ωράριο ώστε να παρέχει τακτικές και έκτακτες υπηρεσίες καθαρισμού σε χώρους εκδηλώσεων (συναυλίες, κινηματογραφικές παραγωγές κτλ) που έχει αναλάβει η εταιρεία μας. Προσφέρονται: Έξοδα μετακίνησης  Εταιρικό τηλέφωνο Ικανοποιητικές αποδοχές αναλόγως προσόντων Παρακαλούνται οι ενδιαφερόμενοι όπως καλέσουν στο 210 2449770 ή αποστείλουν σύντομο βιογραφικό σημείωμα στην ακόλουθη διεύθυνση : [email protected]  ', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653657, 'Head Waiter', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/306350', 'Γλυφάδα', 'πριν 2 λεπτά', '2026-04-17 15:02:21', 'ACE HOTEL&SWIM CLUB ATHENS', 'Our ideal candidate reflects the energy and philosophy of SORA and brings: A genuine passion for hospitality, global flavors, and contemporary Pan-Asian cuisine Proven experience as a waiter/waitress in a luxury restaurant or rooftop venue Confidence working in a fast-paced, service-driven environment with strong attention to detail A collaborative mindset and the ability to perform seamlessly within a professional team Naturally warm, guest-focused personality with a talent for creating memorable dining experiences Professional presence, excellent communication skills, and a strong sense of responsibility', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(653659, 'IT Product Manager', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/306364?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-17 15:02:23', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doΙn this role you will act as the bridge between Business and IT, owning and shaping demand by co-creating solutions that deliver business value. The Product Manager is responsible for translating business needs into clear product requirements and driving delivery within an Agile environment. More specifically you will: Act as the primary liaison between Business stakeholders and IT teams Capture, shape, and co-create demand with the business, ensuring alignment with strategic priorities Analyse business needs and translate them into clear product requirements and features Collaborate closely with Solution Architects to define optimal solutions Own and manage the product backlog, ensuring prioritization based on business value Participate in agile ceremonies (e.g., PI Planning, backlog refinement, sprint planning) Support the definition of features and user stories, ensuring clarity and readiness for development Ensure alignment between business expectations and delivered solutions Monitor delivery progress and support issue resolution and decision-making Contribute to continuous improvement of ways of working and Agile maturityWho you areMSc or BSc in Computer Science, Information Systems or any other related field At least 2-3 years of experience as a Product Manager, Product Owner, or similar role Strong ability to bridge business and technical teams Experience in requirements analysis and solution definition Good understanding of Agile frameworks Experience working with Solution Architects and development teams Strong stakeholder management and communication skills Analytical mindset with a focus on delivering business value Ability to work in a fast-paced, cross-functional environment Exposure to AI and automation tools for enhancing product processes, insights, or decision-making is considered a plus Not a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youAward-winning work environment -certified #1 Top Employer in GreeceCompetitive pay, bonus & remuneration packagePrivate Health & Medical InsuranceHybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroadUnlimited access to learning resources and trainingsVodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of serviceSpirit of Vodafone Day: one day each quarter dedicated to your personal developmentExtra days off: Vodafone Day, Family Day, Volunteering DayOffice amenities (subject to the office location): such as restaurant, beauty corner, gym and parkingSpecial employee offers and discountsWho we areWe are a leading international Telco, serving millions of customers. At Vodafone, we believe that connectivity is a force for good. If we use it for the things that really matter, it can improve people\'s lives and the world around us. Through our technology we empower people, connecting everyone regardless of who they are or where they live and we protect the planet, whilst helping our customers do the same.Belonging at Vodafone isn\'t a concept; it\'s lived, breathed, and cultivated through everything we do. You\'ll be part of a global and diverse community, with many different minds, abilities, backgrounds and cultures. ;We\'re committed to increase diversity, ensure equal representation, and make Vodafone a place everyone feels safe, valued and included.If you require any reasonable adjustments or have an accessibility request as part of your recruitment journey, for example, extended time or breaks in between online assessments, please refer to https://careers.vodafone.com/application-adjustments/ for guidance.Together we can.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653660, 'Junior Software Engineer/Consultant', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/306360', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 33 λεπτά', '2026-04-17 15:02:25', 'Netcompany', 'Company DescriptionAre you ready to shape the future technological landscape in Europe?We are dedicated to responsible digitalisation, building innovative, inclusive solutions that drive meaningful impact. With over 8,900 professionals across Europe, we help EU institutions, public and private organisations thrive in a rapidly evolving digital world. Are you ready to shape the future through technology? Your journey starts here. Take a look at some of our impactful projects here: https://netcompany.com/cases/Job DescriptionEver wondered what it feels like to be a Junior Software Engineer/Consultant at Netcompany?At Netcompany, you won\'t just write code — you\'ll help shape digital solutions that transform how organizations operate across Europe. From day one, you\'ll work at the intersection of technology and business, combining hands-on development with client-facing advisory work.Based in Athens, you\'ll join high-performing, agile teams delivering large-scale IT transformation projects for major public and private sector clients — projects that impact millions of users.As a Junior Software Engineer/Consultant you will:Participate in all phases of IT projects — from requirements analysis and solution design to development, testing (UAT), and user trainingWork closely with clients to understand business needs and translate them into effective technical solutionsDesign, build, and maintain enterprise applications using modern technologies such as Java, C#, JavaScript, and TypeScript, along with frameworks like Spring Boot, .NET, React.js, and AngularContribute across the full stack, including backend, frontend, and system integrations within complex environmentsSupport the implementation and integration of CRM/CX platformsAct as a trusted advisor by identifying opportunities for improvement and proposing innovative solutionsTake ownership of specific workstreams, contribute to agile ceremonies, and communicate progress to stakeholdersBuild strong, long-term client relationships through reliability and technical excellenceContribute to business growth by identifying opportunities within existing client engagementsCreate clear and concise technical and functional documentationShare knowledge within your team and grow into mentoring responsibilities over timeQualificationsWhat would make you a fit for the role:A degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related fieldStrong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to connect business needs to technical solutionsA client-focused mindset and genuine curiosity about how businesses operateExcellent communication skills in English, with confidence in client-facing situationsStrong collaboration skills and the ability to work effectively in international, cross-functional teamsAttention to detail and a commitment to high-quality deliveryA proactive mindset, sense of ownership, and willingness to take initiativeFlexibility to travel when neededAdditional InformationBeing a part of the Netcompany team, you will be provided with: The opportunity to work in a modern environment & in a hybrid working modelA seamless onboarding experience and a buddy to support you on your first stepsA competitive compensation & benefits packageHealth and life insurance program Meal and commuting allowanceWell-being activities (on premises)Continuous learning opportunities using the most modern methods (unlimited access to Udemy for Business, ad-hoc trainings)A personalized development plan for targeted career growthIf you are looking forward to be part of a diverse environment, and have the opportunity to work alongside well-experienced professionals, on challenging, large-scale projects that directly impact millions of citizens around the globe, then this is the place to be!By joining Netcompany in Athens, you will be part of a vivid team of 2,300+ tech professionals. When at the office, you\'ll have the flexibility to work from our three modern, sustainable, and state-of-the-art offices!Please upload your CV in English via the Apply button. All applications will be treated as strictly confidential.We ensure equal opportunities, treatment, and consideration to all candidates. Discrimination based on sex, racial or ethnic origin, religion or belief, disability, age, sexual orientation or marital status, physical or mental disability, or any other factor protected by applicable laws and regulations is prohibited. As part of the Netcompany culture, we respect human rights and focus on creating a positive workplace, where all employees are valued, and where diversity and inclusion are a vital part of our everyday working experience.In the following link you may find our CV Submission privacy notice: https://netcompany.com/cv-submission-privacy-notice/', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(653661, '.NET Developer (Junior-Mid)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/306359', 'Θεσσαλονίκη', 'πριν 8 λεπτά', '2026-04-17 15:02:25', 'Netcompany', 'Company DescriptionAre you ready to shape the future technological landscape in Europe?We are dedicated to responsible digitalisation, building innovative, inclusive solutions that drive meaningful impact. With over 8,900 professionals across Europe, we help EU institutions, public and private organisations thrive in a rapidly evolving digital world. Are you ready to shape the future through technology? Your journey starts here. Take a look at some of our impactful projects here: https://netcompany.com/cases/Job DescriptionEver wondered what it feels like to be a .NET Developer (Junior-Mid) at Netcompany?As a .NET Developer (Junior-Mid), you will join a collaborative engineering team working on modern digital solutions. In this role, you will contribute to the development of backend services and applications, while learning from experienced engineers and growing your technical expertise.This position is ideal for developers with initial professional experience who are eager to build strong foundations in backend development and gradually take on more responsibility in real-world projects.You will work on production systems where code quality, maintainability, and teamwork matter. You\'ll be encouraged to develop your skills, ask questions, and actively contribute to team success.As a .NET Developer (Junior-Mid) you will:Develop and maintain backend applications using .NET / C#Assist in building and improving RESTful APIsTranslate business requirements into clean and maintainable code with guidance from senior team membersFollow coding standards and best practices to write reliable and testable codeParticipate in code reviews and learn from feedbackCollaborate with developers, QA engineers, and product ownersSupport debugging, troubleshooting, and performance improvementsContribute to Agile/Scrum ceremonies such as sprint planning and daily stand-upsGradually take ownership of smaller features and technical tasksLearn and contribute to CI/CD processes and testing practicesQualificationsWhat would make you a fit for the role:1-3 years of experience in .NET / C# developmentBasic understanding of RESTful APIs and web servicesFamiliarity with core software engineering principles (e.g., OOP, basic design patterns)Some experience working with databases (e.g., SQL Server)Exposure to frontend technologies (e.g., Angular or React) is a plusBasic knowledge of tools like Git, and optionally Docker or cloud platforms (e.g., Azure)Willingness to learn, grow, and receive constructive feedbackStrong problem-solving attitude and attention to detailGood communication skills in EnglishAdditional InformationBeing a part of the Netcompany team, you will be provided with: The opportunity to work in a modern environment & in a hybrid working modelA seamless onboarding experience and a buddy to support you on your first stepsA competitive compensation & benefits packageHealth and life insurance programMeal and commuting allowanceWell-being activities (on premises)Continuous learning opportunities using the most modern methods (unlimited access to Udemy for Business, ad-hoc trainings)A personalized development plan for targeted career growthIf you are looking forward to be part of a diverse environment, and have the opportunity to work alongside well-experienced professionals, on challenging, large-scale projects that directly impact millions of citizens around the globe, then this is the place to be!Our branch in Thessaloniki employs 300+ talented professionals, working on a variety of EU mission-critical projects!Please upload your CV in English via the Apply button. All applications will be treated as strictly confidential.We ensure equal opportunities, treatment, and consideration to all candidates. Discrimination based on sex, racial or ethnic origin, religion or belief, disability, age, sexual