(656219, 'Electrical/Mechanical Engineer QA/QC (MEP Engineer)-Microsoft Data Center', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/engineering-jobs/307479?origin=pjp', 'Σπάτα Λούτσας', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-21 15:01:08', 'GEK TERNA GROUP', 'TERNA S.A., member of GEK TERNA Group, is currently looking for a:Electrical/Mechanical Engineer QA/QC (MEP Engineer)-Microsoft Data CenterRole Responsibilities:Ensures the implementation of the Company’s Quality Management SystemCollaborates with the Project construction personnel for the preparation and updating of the Inspection & Test PlansPerforms inspection and testing activities regularlyMonitors testing performed by third parties in cooperation with the competent construction personnelCollaborates with the Engineering Department for the issuance of the Work Method StatementsInforms the Project Director in case of Nonconformity and ensures that all the corrective actions defined by the Project Director are put in operationEnsures that the Materials Control System in general, such as submission for approval, receipt, storage, preservation, traceability and recording, is performed in accordance with the Project Quality Plan / SystemParticipates in training of the project personnel regarding quality issuesPerforms quality audits at regular time intervals assessing the implementation of the Project Quality Plan / SystemPrepares monthly reports for the performance status of Project Quality activities and relevant issuesContributes to continuous improvement of the Company\'s Quality Management System and the Project Quality Program through the review of performance and performance indicatorsRequirements:BSc in Civil or Electromechanical Engineering3 years of working experience as a Quality Engineer in the construction sectorExperience working on sophisticated construction projects is highly desirableExcellent command of the English language (both oral and written)Excellent knowledge of MS Office suiteCompetencies:Excellent written and verbal communication skillsAttention to detail and good analytical skillsAbility to multi-task and manage various projectsProblem-solving and critical-thinking skills', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(656220, 'Shift Leader (Βοηθός Καταστήματος) - Stavroupoli, Thessaloniki', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/sales-or-business-development-or-account-management-jobs/307473?origin=pjp', 'Σταυρούπολη', 'πριν 2 λεπτά', '2026-04-21 15:01:08', 'LPP Greece', 'Στην SINSAY μέλος της LPP, αναζητάμε SHIFT LEADER (ΒΟΗΘΟ ΚΑΤΑΣΤΗΜΑΤΟΣ) για το νέο μας κατάστημα που πρόκειται να ανοίξει σύντομα στην Θεσσαλονίκη, στην περιοχή Σταυρούπολη, επί της οδού Λαγκαδά 339!ΣΧΕΤΙΚΑ ΜΕ ΕΜΑΣΗ LPP S.A. είναι μία από τις μεγαλύτερες εταιρείες μόδας στην Κεντρική και Ανατολική Ευρώπη. Η εταιρεία δραστηριοποιείται σταθερά στην Πολωνία και στο εξωτερικό για περισσότερα από 26 χρόνια, και με επιτυχία ανταποκρίνεται στις απαιτήσεις της αγοράς στον τομέα των ενδυμάτων.Η LPP S.A. διαχειρίζεται 5 Brands μόδας: Reserved, Cropp, House, Mohito και Sinsay, που το κάθε ένα απευθύνεται σε διαφορετικό κοινό.Η εταιρεία έχει παρουσία σε 41 χώρες, απαριθμεί πάνω από 2.800 καταστήματα στο δίκτυό της και επιπλέον διαθέτει και καταστήματα on-line για το κάθε της Brand.Είμαστε φιλόδοξοι, πράγμα που σημαίνει ότι αναζητούμε συνεχώς νέες προκλήσεις και προσπαθούμε πάντα να γινόμαστε καλύτεροι.Η μεγαλύτερη δύναμή μας είναι η ομάδα μας, η οποία σήμερα αποτελείται από περισσότερα από 50.000 ταλαντούχα άτομα στα γραφεία και στα καταστήματά μας. Το πάθος τους μας παρακινεί να έχουμε την ενέργεια και την δύναμη να αναζητούμε περισσότερα.ΚΑΘΗΚΟΝΤΑ·         Διασφάλιση της εύρυθμης λειτουργίας του καταστήματος και τήρηση όλων των απαραίτητων διαδικασιών.·         Επίτευξη των στόχων των πωλήσεων και των KPIS του καταστήματος.·         Διασφάλιση της ποιοτικής εξυπηρέτησης του πελάτη με στόχο την αύξηση των πωλήσεων  και την δημιουργία σχέσης εμπιστοσύνης.·         Οργάνωση και συντονισμός της ομάδας για την αποτελεσματική διεξαγωγή των καθημερινών εργασιών του καταστήματος. ·         Ευθύνη για την εμπορική διαχείριση του καταστήματος. Παραλαβή, διακινήσεις μεταξύ καταστημάτων και επιστροφές εμπορευμάτων, έλεγχος των αποθεμάτων (stock), και  έγκαιρη αναπλήρωση του εμπορεύματος.·         Διασφάλιση της εμπορικής εικόνας του καταστήματος σύμφωνα με τους κανόνες  του Visual Merchandising  της εταιρείας. ·         Οργάνωση και παρουσίαση των προωθητικών ενεργειών στο κατάστημα.·         Γνώση της εμπορικότητας των προϊόντων και αξιοποίηση των εμπορικών σημείων του καταστήματος.·         Ανάλυση των πωλήσεων βάσει των εμπορικών reports, παραθέτοντας  προτάσεις για βελτίωση των αποτελεσμάτων.·         Διοίκηση της ομάδας, βασισμένη στην παρακίνηση, την οργάνωση την ανοιχτή επικοινωνία και τον σεβασμό.·         Εκπαίδευση, αξιολόγηση, επιμόρφωση και ανάπτυξη της ομάδας των εργαζομένων χρησιμοποιώντας όλα τα διαθέσιμα εργαλεία της εταιρείας.·         Τήρηση των κανόνων Loss & Prevention και κινητοποίηση της ομάδας για την ελαχιστοποίηση των απωλειών.·         Ευθύνη για την τήρηση των κανόνων για την Υγεία & Ασφάλεια των υπαλλήλων στον χώρο του καταστήματος και της αποθήκης (Health & Safety). Requirements·         Επιθυμητή η εργασιακή εμπειρία  σε αντίστοιχη θέση σε εταιρεία ένδυσης και υπόδησης.·         Γνώση των τάσεων της μόδας και του ανταγωνισμού. ·         Εμπειρία στη διαχείρηση ομάδας.·         Πολύ καλές οργανωτικές και επικοινωνιακές δεξιότητες.·         Πολύ καλή διαχείριση του χρόνου εργασίας.·         Ομαδικό πνεύμα.·         Ανεπτυγμένο αίσθημα επαγγελματικής ευθύνης. ·         Προσανατολισμός στο αποτέλεσμα.·         Πολύ καλή γνώση χειρισμού Η/Υ ( MS Office).·         Πολύ καλή γνώση Αγγλικών.BenefitsΗ Εταιρεία Προσφέρει:·         Ανταγωνιστικό πακέτο αποδοχών.·         Παροχή διατακτικών (meal vouchers) σε όλους τους υπαλλήλους του καταστήματος.·         Μπόνους με βάση την επίτευξη των στόχων των πωλήσεων.·         Ομαδικό πρόγραμμα ιδιωτικής ασφάλισης υγείας.·         Γραμμή Υποστήριξης των Εργαζομένων (HELPP).·         Εκπτώσεις για αγορές στα καταστήματα της LPP στην Ελλάδα.·         Συνεχής κατάρτιση και εκπαίδευση.·         Προοπτικές για ανάπτυξη και εξέλιξη μέσα στην εταιρεία.·         Ευχάριστο εργασιακό περιβάλλον.Η LPP GREECE που εδρεύει στην Αθήνα, στην οδό Άγγελου Πυρρή 5 & Ευήνου, ως Υπεύθυνος Επεξεργασίας επεξεργάζεται τα προσωπικά σας δεδομένα αποκλειστικά στο μέτρο που απαιτείται κατά την διαδικασία συνέντευξης και ενδεχόμενης πρόσληψης και έχει λάβει όλα τα κατάλληλα τεχνικά και οργανωτικά μέτρα για την προστασία των προσωπικών δεδομένων σας σύμφωνα με την ισχύουσα ελληνική νομοθεσία και τις διατάξεις του Γενικού Κανονισμού Προστασίας Προσωπικών Δεδομένων (ΕΕ) 2016/679. Τα δεδομένα που γνωστοποιείτε στην LPP GREECE  μέσω της αίτησης σας θα διατηρούνται για τυχόν μελλοντική χρήση για χρονικό διάστημα ενός έτους από τη λήψη τους προς αξιοποίηση μελλοντικής πρόσληψης. Για την εκπλήρωση των ανωτέρω αναφερομένων σκοπών επεξεργασίας των προσωπικών σας δεδομένων η LPP GREECE  δύναται να γνωστοποιεί ή να διαβιβάζει προσωπικά δεδομένα που μας έχετε δώσει σε θυγατρικές ή συνδεδεμένες με την LPP GREECE εταιρείες. Μπορείτε ανά πάσα στιγμή με αίτημα σας στην  LPP GREECE να ασκήσετε τα δικαιώματα που προβλέπει ο Κανονισμός, συμπεριλαμβανομένου του δικαιώματος ενημέρωσης και πρόσβασης, διόρθωσης, διαγραφής, περιορισμού της επεξεργασίας,  φορητότητας και του δικαιώματος αντίρρησης ως προς την επεξεργασία μέσω email στη διεύθυνση [email protected] , αλλά και να απευθυνθείτε στην Αρχή Προστασίας Προσωπικών Δεδομένων (www.dpa.gr).', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(656222, 'Spa Therapist', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/beauty-services-or-fitness-jobs/307471', 'Βουλιαγμένη', 'πριν 6 λεπτά', '2026-04-21 15:01:10', 'THE MARGI', 'Το ξενοδοχείο The Margi, στη Βουλιαγμένη, μέλος της Small Luxury Hotels of the Word, αναζητά: Spa Therapist Απαραίτητα προσόντα: Προϋπηρεσία σε αντίστοιχη θέση σε ξενοδοχείο 4* ή 5* (city ή resort) Απαραίτητο το πτυχίο Φυσικοθεραπείας ή Αισθητικής, Ελλάδας ή εξωτερικού Εμπειρία σε εύρος θεραπειών προσώπου, σώματος και μασάζ Πολύ καλή γνώση της αγγλικής γλώσσας Ευχάριστος και φιλικός χαρακτήρας Παρέχουμε: Ευχάριστο περιβάλλον εργασίας Δυνατότητες εξέλιξης σε ένα διαρκώς αναπτυσσόμενο περιβάλλον', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση / Μερική απασχόληση'),
(656223, 'ΜΗΧΑΝΟΛΟΓΟΣ ΜΗΧΑΝΙΚΟΣ / ΠΟΛΙΤΙΚΟΣ ΜΗΧΑΝΙΚΟΣ', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/engineering-jobs/307330', 'Ταύρος', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-21 15:01:12', 'AA DEVELOPMENT', 'Η εταιρεία, με πολυετή παρουσία στον χώρο των κατασκευών, αναζητά Μηχανικούς οι οποίοι θα επιβλέπουν και θα συντονίζουν τις κατασκευές, με παρουσία στο εργοτάξιο και στο γραφείο, εξασφαλίζοντας την ομαλή ολοκλήρωση των έργων.   Αρμοδιότητες Επίβλεψη οικοδομών και εργοταξίων Συντονισμός εργασιών και προμηθευτών. Εντοπισμός τεχνικών θεμάτων στο πεδίο και παροχή πρακτικών λύσεων σε συνεργασία με την ομάδα. Τεχνική υποστήριξη στο στάδιο του αρχιτεκτονικού σχεδιασμού. Έλεγχος έργου πριν την παράδοση. Συγκέντρωση εγγράφων για την διεκπεραίωση των διαδιακσιών του εργοταξίου.   Απαραίτητα Προσόντα Πτυχίο Μηχανικού σχετικής ειδικότητας. Προϋπηρεσία σε επίβλεψη εργοταξίου Ικανότητα συντονισμού εργασιών και ανθρώπινου δυναμικού Δυνατότητα έκδοσης και υπογραφής αδειών μικρής κλίμακας και ενεργειακών πιστοποιητικών Άριστη Γνώση AutoCAD  Συνέπεια, ικανότητα οργάνωσης χρόνου Ικανότητα επίλυσης τεχνικών θεμάτων στο εργοτάξιο Επαγγελματική επικοινωνία και ικανότητα τεχνικής τεκμηρίωσης (reports, emails, πρακτικά) Άνεση σε περιβάλλον που απαιτεί τόσο πεδίο όσο και γραφείο Δίπλωμα οδήγησης και δυνατότητα μετακίνησης σε έργα   Παροχές Σταθερή απασχόληση με σύμβαση αορίστου χρόνου Πλήρης ασφάλιση  Άκρως υποστηρικτικό και οργανωμένο περιβάλλον Ανταγωνιστικό πακέτο αποδοχών  Προοπτικές εξέλιξης ', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(656224, 'AI Team Lead', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/307458', 'Θεσσαλονίκη', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-21 15:01:12', 'Netcompany', 'Company DescriptionAre you ready to shape the future technological landscape in Europe?We are dedicated to responsible digitalisation, building innovative, inclusive solutions that drive meaningful impact. With over 8,900 professionals across Europe, we help EU institutions, public and private organisations thrive in a rapidly evolving digital world. Are you ready to shape the future through technology? Your journey starts here. Take a look at some of our impactful projects here: https://netcompany.com/cases/Job DescriptionSo, what are the main responsibilities of the AI Team Lead in Netcompany\'s Enterprise Solutions? Joining us as the AI Team Lead, you will own the end-to-end delivery of GenAI, LLM and Machine Learning (ML) solutions for enterprise clients across the public and private sectors. You will act as a trusted advisor to senior client stakeholders, translating complex AI and ML capabilities into tangible business outcomes, while building and leading a high-performing team of AI and ML engineers. This is a client-facing leadership role. Your ability to navigate complex stakeholder environments, manage expectations, and drive alignment across business and technology teams will be as important as your technical expertise. You will be the primary AI and ML point of contact for key accounts, presenting to C-level executives, leading workshops, and shaping AI and ML adoption roadmaps. Focus (but not limited to) the design and implementation of advanced GenAI and ML pipelines leading a technical AI project team to deliver end-to-end creative applications that go beyond current tools and ensuring your team delivers scalable, reusable, extensible and flexible solutions. As the AI Team Lead, you will:Serve as the primary AI and ML advisor to key enterprise clients, understanding their business challenges and translating them into AI- and ML-powered solutions that deliver measurable value. Lead and grow a team of AI/ML Engineers, and collaborate with MLOps and DevOps specialists, to design, develop, and optimize ML and GenAI architectures tailored to client-specific use cases and business requirements. Manage stakeholder relationships across multiple concurrent projects, including steering committees, progress reporting, and escalation management. Architect and oversee end-to-end ML and GenAI pipelines, delivering AI applications for key client transformation projects across the region and international business. Mentor and develop team members, identifying skill gaps, and creating individual development plans. Lead client workshops, discovery sessions, and technical presentations to shape AI strategy and drive adoption. Execute the GenAI, LLM and ML strategy including people, technology, methodologies, platforms, and processes, while fostering a culture of technical excellence, innovation and continuous improvement.QualificationsWhat would make you a fit for the role:Bachelor\'s or Master\'s degree in AI, Data Science, Machine Learning, Computer Science, Engineering, Operational Research or a related field. PhD in Operational Research preferred. 6+ years of experience in AI/ML engineering, with a proven track record of delivering AI projects in enterprise/consulting environments from conception to production, with at least 2 years in a people management or practice leadership role. Demonstrated experience managing client relationships, leading workshops, and presenting technical solutions to non-technical senior stakeholders (C-level, board members, steering committees). Experience leading and developing teams, including hiring, performance management, and career development. Strong expertise in Machine Learning and GenAI solutions including open source frameworks, RAG architectures, prompt engineering, LLM models (Claude, GPT, Gemini), and production deployment patterns. Solid understanding of MLOps, AI model lifecycle management, Model Context Protocol (MCP), and experience with cloud platforms (AWS, Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud Platform). Hands-on experience with open source ML/AI frameworks, agentic AI technologies, prompt engineering, and leading LLM models (Claude, GPT, Gemini, Nvidia AI stack). It would also be a plus if you match some of the following:Experience in consulting, systems integration, or professional services environments. Experience with AIOps practices, LLM monitoring frameworks, and AI governance. Strong knowledge of ML and GenAI frameworks (e.g. LlamaIndex, LangGraph) and AI evaluation tools. Pre-sales or business development experience in AI/data services.Additional InformationBeing a part of the Netcompany team, you will be provided with: The opportunity to work in a modern environment & in a hybrid working modelA seamless onboarding experience and a buddy to support you on your first stepsA competitive compensation & benefits packageHealth and life insurance programMeal and commuting allowanceWell-being activities (on premises)Continuous learning opportunities using the most modern methods (unlimited access to Udemy for Business, ad-hoc trainings)A personalized development plan for targeted career growthIf you are looking forward to be part of a diverse environment, and have the opportunity to work alongside well-experienced professionals, on challenging, large-scale projects that directly impact millions of citizens around the globe, then this is the place to be!Our branch in Thessaloniki employs 300+ talented professionals, working on a variety of EU mission-critical projects!Please upload your CV in English via the Apply button. All applications will be treated as strictly confidential.We ensure equal opportunities, treatment, and consideration to all candidates. Discrimination based on sex, racial or ethnic origin, religion or belief, disability, age, sexual orientation or marital status, physical or mental disability, or any other factor protected by applicable laws and regulations is prohibited. As part of the Netcompany culture, we respect human rights and focus on creating a positive workplace, where all employees are valued, and where diversity and inclusion are a vital part of our everyday working experience.In the following link you may find our CV Submission privacy notice: https://netcompany.com/cv-submission-privacy-notice/', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(656225, 'Business Development Consultant', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/sales-or-business-development-or-account-management-jobs/307456', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 32 λεπτά', '2026-04-21 15:01:14', 'Netcompany', 'Company DescriptionAre you ready to shape the future technological landscape in Europe?We are dedicated to responsible digitalisation, building innovative, inclusive solutions that drive meaningful impact. With over 8,900 professionals across Europe, we help EU institutions, public and private organisations thrive in a rapidly evolving digital world. Are you ready to shape the future through technology? Your journey starts here. Take a look at some of our impactful projects here: https://netcompany.com/cases/Job DescriptionEver wondered what it feels like to be a Business Development Consultant in Netcompany?Joining us as a Business Development Consultant, you will drive growth by identifying customer needs, shaping solutions and strengthening customer relationships.As a Business Development Consultant you will:Consult Public Sector customers to shape their vision and identify domain and customer needsConceptualize compelling solutions and business propositionsAnalyze competition and provide relevant insights Identify and formulate the solution and value proposition to be offered to the clientBuild and nurture strong relationships with key stakeholders, mostly with the end-customer(s), while mapping the domain and customer stakeholder landscape to position the offering effectivelyCreate high-quality business development materials (concept papers, proposals, vision statements, executive presentations)Work closely with the sales team to convert opportunities into tangible business outcomesDrive business growth with a results-oriented approach, ensuring alignment with key performance indicators (KPIs) and strategic objectives.QualificationsWhat would make you a fit for the role:Extensive and proven experience (minimum 8 years) in Business Development and/or IT consulting in Digital Government and the broader Public Sector domain in Greece./ Defense / Civil protection / Immigration / Foreign affairsBachelor\'s degree in Computer Science or a related field; Master\'s degree would be an assetDeep understanding of the Public Sector domain in GreeceStrong business and technology knowledge relevant to Digital Government and Public Sector transformationExcellent communication and relationship-building skillsAbility to create impactful business development content for different audiences and purposesStrategic mindset, proactiveness, and a solution-oriented approachDemonstrated success in achieving business development targets and driving business growthStrong analytical skills with the ability to interpret complex data and market trendsExcellent Greek and English communication skills.Additional InformationBeing a part of the Netcompany team, you will be provided with: The opportunity to work in a modern environment & in a hybrid working modelA seamless onboarding experience and a buddy to support you on your first stepsA competitive compensation & benefits packageHealth and life insurance programMeal and commuting allowanceWell-being activities (on premises)Continuous learning opportunities using the most modern methods (unlimited access to Udemy for Business, ad-hoc trainings)A personalized development plan for targeted career growthIf you are looking forward to be part of a diverse environment, and have the opportunity to work alongside well-experienced professionals, on challenging, large-scale projects that directly impact millions of citizens around the globe, then this is the place to be!By joining Netcompany in Athens, you will be part of a vivid team of 2,300+ tech professionals. When at the office, you\'ll have the flexibility to work from our three modern, sustainable, and state-of-the-art offices!Please upload your CV in English via the Apply button. All applications will be treated as strictly confidential.We ensure equal opportunities, treatment, and consideration to all candidates. Discrimination based on sex, racial or ethnic origin, religion or belief, disability, age, sexual orientation or marital status, physical or mental disability, or any other factor protected by applicable laws and regulations is prohibited. As part of the Netcompany culture, we respect human rights and focus on creating a positive workplace, where all employees are valued, and where diversity and inclusion are a vital part of our everyday working experience.In the following link you may find our CV Submission privacy notice: https://netcompany.com/cv-submission-privacy-notice/', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(656226, 'AI Team Lead', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/307457', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 7 λεπτά', '2026-04-21 15:01:14', 'Netcompany', 'Company DescriptionAre you ready to shape the future technological landscape in Europe?We are dedicated to responsible digitalisation, building innovative, inclusive solutions that drive meaningful impact. With over 8,900 professionals across Europe, we help EU institutions, public and private organisations thrive in a rapidly evolving digital world. Are you ready to shape the future through technology? Your journey starts here. Take a look at some of our impactful projects here: https://netcompany.com/cases/Job DescriptionSo, what are the main responsibilities of the AI Team Lead in Netcompany\'s Enterprise Solutions? Joining us as the AI Team Lead, you will own the end-to-end delivery of GenAI, LLM and Machine Learning (ML) solutions for enterprise clients across the public and private sectors. You will act as a trusted advisor to senior client stakeholders, translating complex AI and ML capabilities into tangible business outcomes, while building and leading a high-performing team of AI and ML engineers. This is a client-facing leadership role. Your ability to navigate complex stakeholder environments, manage expectations, and drive alignment across business and technology teams will be as important as your technical expertise. You will be the primary AI and ML point of contact for key accounts, presenting to C-level executives, leading workshops, and shaping AI and ML adoption roadmaps. Focus (but not limited to) the design and implementation of advanced GenAI and ML pipelines leading a technical AI project team to deliver end-to-end creative applications that go beyond current tools and ensuring your team delivers scalable, reusable, extensible and flexible solutions. As the AI Team Lead, you will:Serve as the primary AI and ML advisor to key enterprise clients, understanding their business challenges and translating them into AI- and ML-powered solutions that deliver measurable value. Lead and grow a team of AI/ML Engineers, and collaborate with MLOps and DevOps specialists, to design, develop, and optimize ML and GenAI architectures tailored to client-specific use cases and business requirements. Manage stakeholder relationships across multiple concurrent projects, including steering committees, progress reporting, and escalation management. Architect and oversee end-to-end ML and GenAI pipelines, delivering AI applications for key client transformation projects across the region and international business. Mentor and develop team members, identifying skill gaps, and creating individual development plans. Lead client workshops, discovery sessions, and technical presentations to shape AI strategy and drive adoption. Execute the GenAI, LLM and ML strategy including people, technology, methodologies, platforms, and processes, while fostering a culture of technical excellence, innovation and continuous improvement.QualificationsWhat would make you a fit for the role:Bachelor\'s or Master\'s degree in AI, Data Science, Machine Learning, Computer Science, Engineering, Operational Research or a related field. PhD in Operational Research preferred. 6+ years of experience in AI/ML engineering, with a proven track record of delivering AI projects in enterprise/consulting environments from conception to production, with at least 2 years in a people management or practice leadership role. Demonstrated experience managing client relationships, leading workshops, and presenting technical solutions to non-technical senior stakeholders (C-level, board members, steering committees). Experience leading and developing teams, including hiring, performance management, and career development. Strong expertise in Machine Learning and GenAI solutions including open source frameworks, RAG architectures, prompt engineering, LLM models (Claude, GPT, Gemini), and production deployment patterns. Solid understanding of MLOps, AI model lifecycle management, Model Context Protocol (MCP), and experience with cloud platforms (AWS, Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud Platform). Hands-on experience with open source ML/AI frameworks, agentic AI technologies, prompt engineering, and leading LLM models (Claude, GPT, Gemini, Nvidia AI stack). It would also be a plus if you match some of the following:Experience in consulting, systems integration, or professional services environments. Experience with AIOps practices, LLM monitoring frameworks, and AI governance. Strong knowledge of ML and GenAI frameworks (e.g. LlamaIndex, LangGraph) and AI evaluation tools. Pre-sales or business development experience in AI/data services.Additional InformationBeing a part of the Netcompany team, you will be provided with: The opportunity to work in a modern environment & in a hybrid working modelA seamless onboarding experience and a buddy to support you on your first stepsA competitive compensation & benefits packageHealth and life insurance programMeal and commuting allowanceWell-being activities (on premises)Continuous learning opportunities using the most modern methods (unlimited access to Udemy for Business, ad-hoc trainings)A personalized development plan for targeted career growthIf you are looking forward to be part of a diverse environment, and have the opportunity to work alongside well-experienced professionals, on challenging, large-scale projects that directly impact millions of citizens around the globe, then this is the place to be!By joining Netcompany in Athens, you will be part of a vivid team of 2,300+ tech professionals. When at the office, you\'ll have the flexibility to work from our three modern, sustainable, and state-of-the-art offices!Please upload your CV in English via the Apply button. All applications will be treated as strictly confidential.We ensure equal opportunities, treatment, and consideration to all candidates. Discrimination based on sex, racial or ethnic origin, religion or belief, disability, age, sexual orientation or marital status, physical or mental disability, or any other factor protected by applicable laws and regulations is prohibited. As part of the Netcompany culture, we respect human rights and focus on creating a positive workplace, where all employees are valued, and where diversity and inclusion are a vital part of our everyday working experience.In the following link you may find our CV Submission privacy notice: https://netcompany.com/cv-submission-privacy-notice/', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(656227, 'Senior Network Deployment & Systems Project Manager', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/operations-jobs/307469?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 3 λεπτά', '2026-04-21 15:01:16', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doDrive the successful delivery of fiber and core network projects, manage the systems that support implementation and design new tools / automation solutions to improve delivery efficiency.More specifically you will:• Lead end-to-end fiber and core network projects• Manage project\'s coordination & delivery (feasibility, planning, implementation, subcontractor management, SLA/H&S, risk management)• Manage subcontractor relationships, monitor performance, and ensure SLA and safety compliance.• Collaborate with internal stakeholders (ND Field & FO design, VBTS, VBU, Legal, Regulatory)• Handle systems management & development (existing tools + new automation)• Apply strong stakeholder management, problem-solving, and adaptability to simplify complex processes and deliver actionable results.• Prepare reports, dashboards, and presentations to provide clear visibility of project status, risks, and performance to internal stakeholders.Who you are• Bachelor\'s degree in Telecoms, Engineering or related field• MSc Degree in Telecoms related field or equivalent experience (preferred)• 3+ years\' experience in similar position within a service provider/operator or vendor• Experience in Fiber Optics technologies & project management• Experience with project management tools, systems, and reporting dashboards• Experience of managing the relations with Vendors, Subcontractors and cross-functional teams• Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills• Excellent written and verbal communications skills in Greek & EnglishNot a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youAward-winning work environment -certified #1 Top Employer in GreeceCompetitive pay, bonus & remuneration packagePrivate Health & Medical InsuranceHybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroadUnlimited access to learning resources and trainingsVodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of serviceSpirit of Vodafone Day: one day each quarter dedicated to your personal developmentExtra days off: Vodafone Day, Family Day, Volunteering DayOffice amenities (subject to the office location): such as restaurant, beauty corner, gym and parkingSpecial employee offers and discountsWho we areWe are a leading international Telco, serving millions of customers. At Vodafone, we believe that connectivity is a force for good. If we use it for the things that really matter, it can improve people\'s lives and the world around us. Through our technology we empower people, connecting everyone regardless of who they are or where they live and we protect the planet, whilst helping our customers do the same.Belonging at Vodafone isn\'t a concept; it\'s lived, breathed, and cultivated through everything we do. You\'ll be part of a global and diverse community, with many different minds, abilities, backgrounds and cultures. ;We\'re committed to increase diversity, ensure equal representation, and make Vodafone a place everyone feels safe, valued and included.If you require any reasonable adjustments or have an accessibility request as part of your recruitment journey, for example, extended time or breaks in between online assessments, please refer to https://careers.vodafone.com/application-adjustments/ for guidance.Together we can.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση');
INSERT INTO `kariera` (`id`, `title`, `url`, `location`, `posted`, `scraped`, `company`, `description`, `type`) VALUES
(656228, 'Head of Asset Rotation', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/307474?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 5 λεπτά', '2026-04-21 15:01:16', 'Metlen Energy & Metals', 'At METLEN Energy & Metals, we are catalysts for a sustainable future, positioned at the forefront of the energy transition while being a reference point for competitive green metallurgy at both the European and global levels. We are a global industrial and energy company operating across two highly interconnected and complementary sectors: Energy and Metals. With a consolidated turnover of €5,683 million and an EBITDA of €1,080 million, along with a workforce of over 7,627 dedicated individuals, we drive success through cutting-edge technology and diverse talent.We are committed to embracing new state-of-the-art technologies and advancements, propelling us towards a cleaner, brighter tomorrow. Our positive footprint extends across five continents, creating a lasting impact. At METLEN, we foster a culture of resilience, challenge, respect, excellence, and change, empowering our diverse workforce to achieve remarkable outcomes.Job Description Head of Asset Rotation 20/04/2026 Job Description: We are looking for a Global Head of Asset Rotation to lead the execution of METLEN\'s renewable energy divestment strategy, combining senior deal-making responsibility with the build-out of a global Sell-Side M&A function.By joining this role, you\'ll play a pivotal role in delivering asset rotation and capital recycling objectives, acting both as a senior transaction leader and as the architect of a scalable, international operating model.Your role will encompass:Lead and execute the global asset rotation strategy in line with corporate objectives and capital recycling targets.Design and implement the global target operating model (hub-and-spoke), including governance, processes, and reporting lines.Directly lead and execute priority sell-side transactions during the build-out phase, acting as deal lead and managing external advisors and internal stakeholders.Drive investor engagement, due diligence, negotiations, and transaction structuring to maximize valuation and competitive tension.Oversee and guide regional asset rotation teams, ensuring consistent execution quality, governance, and knowledge sharing across geographies.Ensure close cross-functional alignment with EPC, Development, Finance, Legal, Strategy, and Investment Committees throughout the transaction lifecycle.What you bring to the role:10+ years of experience in senior M&A, asset rotation, or project finance roles within renewable energy or infrastructure.Proven track record of executing sell-side transactions for large-scale energy or infrastructure assets.Strong understanding of and relationships with global infrastructure investors, utilities, sovereign wealth funds, and financial institutions.Experience operating in both leadership and hands-on execution roles, including building or scaling international teams and functions.Bachelor\'s degree in Finance, Economics, Business Administration, Engineering, or a related field; an MBA or Master\'s degree is preferred.Strong financial modelling, valuation expertise, and experience negotiating transaction documentationKey skills & competencies:Strong leadership with a hands-on, execution-oriented mindset.Excellent negotiation and senior stakeholder management skills.Ability to operate effectively in a global, matrixed organization.Deep commercial and financial acumen.High degree of autonomy, pragmatism, and problem-solving capability.Strong communication skills and executive presence.Share the same Value-Based Behaviors:People & Personal GrowthResults Orientation & Safety ExcellenceCollaboration & TrustEmpathy & Effective CommunicationFlexibility & AdaptabilityWhat we offer:Competitive compensation packageSTIP: Performance-based bonusCompany carFuel allowancePension planMedical planFollow us on LinkedIn and stay updated on our latest newsWe respect your personal data. All personal information in your application and CV will remain strictly confidential. At Metlen Energy & Metals we are proud to have Diversity and Inclusion at the centre of everything we do. We are committed to Equal Employment Opportunity regardless of race, colour, national origin, ethnicity, gender, age, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or religion.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(656229, 'Corporate Technical Support (CTS)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/technicians-or-service-jobs/307470?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 13 λεπτά', '2026-04-21 15:01:18', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doWe are looking for a Corporate Technical Support Engineer to be hired with the responsibility to perform Converged Telephony and Legacy Services support in direct contact with Business Customers, field technicians and 2nd level support teamsKey accountabilities • Troubleshoot and resolve customer technical issues which arise after service activation. • Perform all required actions to support Converged Telephony and Legacy Services to customer, also doing all Vodafone internal coordination activities that follow the troubleshooting process.• Organize field technician visits to customer premises to perform all appropriate actions.• Perform Services proactive Monitoring and run health checks. • Send technical incident reports to Business customers.Who you areWho you are:• Good general and technical education with qualifications in telecommunications and computing. TEI or University degree.• At least 3 years\' experience in administration of technology services (Fixed telephony - PBX administration- Internet solutions) • Technical knowledge of Transmission/Transport, IP Networks and Cisco configuration• Logical approach to problem solving and self-motivation.• Broad experience of supporting major corporate customers through virtual teams, suppliers, contractors, and integrators.• Thorough knowledge, end to end, of fixed voice/ Internet telecommunication network operation• Knowledge of Microsoft Office programs (Word, Excel, PowerPoint)• Knowledge of Microsoft Teams, including collaboration and calling/telephony features, along with basic administration in Microsoft 365.• Very good level of Greek and English language (oral and written)Not a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youAward-winning work environment -certified #1 Top Employer in GreeceCompetitive pay, bonus & remuneration packagePrivate Health & Medical InsuranceHybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroadUnlimited access to learning resources and trainingsVodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of serviceSpirit of Vodafone Day: one day each quarter dedicated to your personal developmentExtra days off: Vodafone Day, Family Day, Volunteering DayOffice amenities (subject to the office location): such as restaurant, beauty corner, gym and parkingSpecial employee offers and discountsWho we areWe are a leading international Telco, serving millions of customers. At Vodafone, we believe that connectivity is a force for good. If we use it for the things that really matter, it can improve people\'s lives and the world around us. Through our technology we empower people, connecting everyone regardless of who they are or where they live and we protect the planet, whilst helping our customers do the same.Belonging at Vodafone isn\'t a concept; it\'s lived, breathed, and cultivated through everything we do. You\'ll be part of a global and diverse community, with many different minds, abilities, backgrounds and cultures. ;We\'re committed to increase diversity, ensure equal representation, and make Vodafone a place everyone feels safe, valued and included.If you require any reasonable adjustments or have an accessibility request as part of your recruitment journey, for example, extended time or breaks in between online assessments, please refer to https://careers.vodafone.com/application-adjustments/ for guidance.Together we can.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(656230, 'Billing Support Engineer', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/engineering-jobs/307468?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 10 λεπτά', '2026-04-21 15:01:18', 'Vodafone', 'Join UsAt Vodafone, we\'re not just shaping the future of connectivity for our customers - we\'re shaping the future for everyone who joins our team. When you work with us, you\'re part of a global mission to connect people, solve complex challenges, and create a sustainable and more inclusive world. If you want to grow your career whilst finding the perfect balance between work and life, Vodafone offers the opportunities to help you belong and make a real impact.What you\'ll doManage and initiate continuous operation improvements to verify and improve operational effectiveness of Billing services.Key Accountabilities: • Administrate, configure and monitor Billing applications, ensuring system\'s integrity• Act as second level support, processing incoming incidents, problems and requests through Service Desk ensuring alignment with business users• Perform health and quality checks to verify operational excellence• Collaborate with vendors and Billing delivery teams in the development and deployment of new functionalities• Ensure operations related activities are performed in compliance with company processes and regulationsWho you are• At least 3 years of professional experience in a relevant role• Bachelor\'s Degree in Computer Science or Engineering. Master\'s Degree will be considered an asset.• Strong experience with Billing IT services and Oracle SQL (relevant certifications will be considered a plus)• Capable to understand the technical aspect of complex systems with strong analytical and problem-solving skills• Experience with cloud platforms (e.g. Azure, AWS)• Good understanding of live monitoring tools (eg Splunk, Dynatrace)• ITIL Certification is preferred• Ability to influence, mentor, and collaborate with agile development teams• Self - motivated with strong time-management skills and the ability to juggle multiple balls• Excellent written and verbal communications skills in Greek & English, with both technical and business audiences Not a perfect fit?Worried that you don\'t meet all the desired criteria exactly? At Vodafone we are passionate about empowering people and creating a workplace where everyone can thrive, whatever their personal or professional background. If you\'re excited about this role but your experience doesn\'t align exactly with every part of the job description, we encourage you to still apply as you may be the right candidate for this role or another opportunity.What\'s in it for youAward-winning work environment -certified #1 Top Employer in GreeceCompetitive pay, bonus & remuneration packagePrivate Health & Medical InsuranceHybrid way of working: a blend of remote and office-based working, including the option to work from abroadUnlimited access to learning resources and trainingsVodafone Parental Leave: 16 weeks of fully paid parental leave to all employees regardless of gender, sexual orientation or length of serviceSpirit of Vodafone Day: one day each quarter dedicated to your personal developmentExtra days off: Vodafone Day, Family Day, Volunteering DayOffice amenities (subject to the office location): such as restaurant, beauty corner, gym and parkingSpecial employee offers and discountsWho we areWe are a leading international Telco, serving millions of customers. At Vodafone, we believe that connectivity is a force for good. If we use it for the things that really matter, it can improve people\'s lives and the world around us. Through our technology we empower people, connecting everyone regardless of who they are or where they live and we protect the planet, whilst helping our customers do the same.Belonging at Vodafone isn\'t a concept; it\'s lived, breathed, and cultivated through everything we do. You\'ll be part of a global and diverse community, with many different minds, abilities, backgrounds and cultures. ;We\'re committed to increase diversity, ensure equal representation, and make Vodafone a place everyone feels safe, valued and included.If you require any reasonable adjustments or have an accessibility request as part of your recruitment journey, for example, extended time or breaks in between online assessments, please refer to https://careers.vodafone.com/application-adjustments/ for guidance.Together we can.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(656231, 'Korean Speaking Consultant for Online Security Software', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/307472', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 13 λεπτά', '2026-04-21 15:01:20', 'TP Greece', 'Job Overview: Are you a fluent Korean speaker with good computer skills? Be part of our Helpdesk team that helps customers stay safe online!TP Greece collaborates with the leading IT Security Software companies dedicated to protecting your personal data. We invite you to be part of a team that assists customers of antivirus software find the solutions they are looking for. If cybersecurity and online safety is your thing, grab this opportunity to join our team and work with the leaders of the industry, while enhancing your resume. This is your chance to work as a consultant for the world\'s top multinational cybersecurity and antivirus providers.What you will do: Communicate with customers via phone, chat & e-mail Ensure full functionality of the antivirus protection Troubleshoot technical issues using your problem-solving skills Track and follow cases to ensure they closed in an efficient and timely manner Maintain high customer satisfaction, representing a major brand Provide and maintain strong, professional relationships with all partners and show empathy at all times Log the cases on internal systems, while getting up to date with client\'s products & services. What you will bring: Fluency in Korean Very good communication skills in English Exceptional written and spoken communication skills, soft skills, as well as problem-solving skills Empathy and a passion for customer service Familiarity with current Anti-Malware and Firewall products Ability to install an operating system and install additional necessary software Ability to troubleshoot common PC, Mac and mobile issues Knowledge of MAC, iOS and Android Operating Systems Knowledge of Firewall, Antivirus products and Security domain Knowledgeable in Windows X OS (Windows XP to 10) & Mac OS fundamentals Base knowledge of networking technologies (TCP/IP, DNS, WLAN) What we offer: Complete support to help you ease your relocation to Greece (we cover your flight tickets expenses, hotel accommodation, support with the house searching process (-all at no cost to you-) Competitive monthly salary + 2 extra salaries per year Refer-A-Friend : Bring your friends and receive great bonuses! Health care benefits and numerous other discounts Full training by certified instructors Professional growth & development opportunities Special events as well as community & social responsibility initiatives Free online Greek language courses State of the art premises, providing a great working environment with relaxing break areas Work for a Great Place to Work-Certified Company that fosters diversity Moreover, this is a great opportunity to advance your career and work for a multinational company, by developing strong experience and skills, while representing one of the biggest brands worldwide. In addition, you will be a member of a company that fosters diversity, offering equal opportunities to all, regardless of gender, ethnicity, religion, culture or age. For these reasons, we invite you to join our big family of more than 12.000 people from 110+ nationalities.Thinking about relocating and wondering about cost of living in Greece? Get an idea here:Greece has enviable history and culture, climate and cuisine - and yet, the cost of living is among the lowest in Europe, according to Greek authorities and the EURES network . No wonder Greece is a popular destination for tourists and expats alike. Find out more!Would you like to see more Korean speaking jobs options? Do you need even more available jobs ?', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(656232, 'Υπάλληλος Καταστήματος (8ωρη πλήρη / 6ωρη μερική απασχόληση) στην Πάρο', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/retail-jobs/307452?origin=pjp', 'Πάρος', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-21 15:01:20', 'Lidl Ελλάς', 'Ποιοι είμαστεΠάνω από 6.700 άνθρωποι, 5 logistics centers και περισσότερα από 230 καταστήματα σε όλη την Ελλάδα. Και παρόλ\' αυτά, η αγαπημένη μας λέξη είναι το «μαζί». Μαζί πετυχαίνουμε τους στόχους μας. Μαζί μας εξελίσσεσαι. Μαθαίνουμε ασταμάτητα, ξεπερνάμε τον εαυτό μας, χτίζουμε το μέλλον μας. Γινόμαστε όλα όσα είμαστε, χάρη σε σένα!Θέλεις να γίνεις μέλος της ομάδας; Ψάχνουμε Υπάλληλο για το κατάστημά μας!Η θέσηΓνωρίζεις το κατάστημα μας απ\' έξω και ανακατωτά! Ξέρεις που πρέπει να βρίσκεσαι ανά πάσα στιγμή, στο ταμείο πετάς, τακτοποιείς τα προϊόντα με κλειστά τα μάτια, οι πελάτες μας θα σου έδιναν βραβείο εξυπηρέτησης. Πίστεψέ μας, δε βαριέσαι ποτέ, ακριβώς γιατί κάθε μέρα τα πόστα σου εναλλάσσονται.Μια μέρα στη δουλειάΕδώ ξεπερνάμε τον εαυτό μας κάθε μέρα. Και αυτό ξεκινάει από τα πιο μικρά και καθημερινά μας καθήκοντα. Φαντάσου μια μέρα σου στη δουλειά:Γνωρίζεις το κατάστημα σαν να ήταν το δεύτερο σπίτι σου! Τα ψυγεία, τα καλάθια και τα ράφια μας είναι πάντα γεμάτα. Ναι ξέρουμε, δεν είμαστε το σούπερ μάρκετ που έχεις συνηθίσει. Όλα θέλουμε να βρίσκονται στη σωστή θέση.Η αποθήκη μας είναι σε τάξη και στις απογραφές δε μας ξεφεύγει τίποτα. Ξέρουμε ότι μπορούμε να φτάσουμε εκεί χάρη σε σένα. Και μέσα σε όλα αυτά, να φροντίζεις για το ταμείο και τους βασικούς κανόνες υγιεινής.Κούτες, κιβώτια, παλέτες και εμπορεύματα: φροντίζεις και για τη μεταφορά και την τοποθέτησή τους στα ράφια μας με τα κατάλληλα εργαλεία. H μέρα σου έχει και αρκετή χειρωνακτική δουλειά!Το αγαπημένο σου κομμάτι; Ο φούρνος και η μαναβική μας. Κι αυτό γιατί είσαι το άτομο που φροντίζει να έχουμε έτοιμο, ζεστό, λαχταριστό ψωμί και φρέσκα φρούτα κάθε μέρα. Μπορεί να ξεκινήσει καλύτερα η μέρα;Οι πελάτες μας σε λατρεύουν! Τους εξυπηρετείς και τους καθοδηγείς σε κάθε τους βήμα στο κατάστημα.Θέλεις να \'δεις\' μια μέρα στη δουλειά; Κάνε κλικ στο βίντεο. Είσαι αυτό που αναζητάμε;Ας δούμε τα βασικά:Δεν χρειάζεται να έχεις κανένα πτυχίο ούτε προϋπηρεσία! Θέλουμε μόνο να αγαπάς το εμπόριο! Είσαι ταλέντο στην επικοινωνία και όλοι μιλάνε για την ευγένειά σου. Το πρόγραμμά σου είναι ευέλικτο και ανοιχτό σε διαφορετικές βάρδιες - πρόγραμμα που θα ξέρεις πολλές μέρες πριν. Σου αρέσει να δουλεύεις με ομάδες και πάνω από όλα: μπορείς να γίνεις το επόμενο αγαπημένο πρόσωπο των πελατών μας.Τι σου προσφέρουμε εμείςΞέρουμε πόσο σημαντικό είναι να φροντίζουμε την ομάδα. Είμαστε και φέτος Κορυφαίος Εργοδότης στην Ελλάδα (Top Employer). Γιατί δε σταματάμε ποτέ να προσπαθούμε. Μαζί μας, θα βρεις όλα τα παρακάτω:Μηναίο μισθό που ξεκινάει από τα 1.150€ μικτά και φτάνειέως και τα 1.560€ ανάλογα με προηγούμενη εμπειρία και σε περίπτωση που είσαι έγγαμος, για 8ωρη/5ήμερη απασχόληση. Μηναίο μισθό που ξεκινάει από τα 862€ μικτά και φτάνειέως και τα 1.170€ ανάλογα με προηγούμενη εμπειρία και σε περίπτωση που είσαι έγγαμος, για 6ωρη/5ήμερη απασχόληση. Μισθός που θα προσαυξάνεται ανάλογα,σε περίπτωση υπερωρίας, νυχτερινής εργασίας ή εργασίας την Κυριακή. Άλλωστε στη Lidl κάθε λεπτό εργασίας καταγράφεται και πληρώνεται. Kουπόνια τροφίμων για τις αγορές σου από τα καταστήματά μας 100€ κάθε μήνα. Bonus 300€ μικτά κάθε Οκτώβριο, εφόσον έχεις συμπληρώσει 6 μήνες στην εταιρία.Σταθερά 5ήμερη εργασία. Ναι, ακόμα και τον Ιούλιο και τον Αύγουστο.Ιδιωτική ιατρική ασφάλιση. Η υγεία σου είναι πάντα η πρώτη μας προτεραιότητα. Γι\' αυτό όλη η ομάδα μας αποκτά ιδιωτική ιατρική ασφάλιση.Πρόγραμμα εκπαίδευσης περίπου 2 μηνών: πριν μπεις στα βαθιά, φροντίζουμε να μάθεις όσα χρειάζεσαι για να ξεκινήσεις δουλειά την επόμενη μέρα! Φυσικά και πληρώνεσαι παράλληλα.Μια δεμένη ομάδα: αυτό που μας ξεχωρίζει είναι η κουλτούρα της ομάδας μας, οι ευκαιρίες που βρίσκουμε για να κάνουμε πράγματα μαζί. Μαθαίνουμε online, μοιραζόμαστε δώρα, γιορτάζουμε, βραβεύουμε τα αγαπημένα μας καταστήματα, φροντίζουμε ο ένας τον άλλονΈλα στο #teamlidl Είσαι το επόμενο κεφάλαιο του success story μας; Κάνε την αίτησή σου τώρα και γίνε μέρος του #teamlidl , της πιο δυναμικής ομάδας στο #retail.', 'Μερική απασχόληση'),
(656233, 'Υπεύθυνος Βάρδιας Καταστήματος (8ωρη πλήρη / 6ωρη μερική απασχόληση) στην Πάρο', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/retail-jobs/307451?origin=pjp', 'Πάρος', 'πριν 21 λεπτά', '2026-04-21 15:01:22', 'Lidl Ελλάς', 'Ποιοι είμαστεΠάνω από 6.700 άνθρωποι, 5 logistics centers και περισσότερα από 230 καταστήματα σε όλη την Ελλάδα. Και παρόλ\' αυτά, η αγαπημένη μας λέξη είναι το «μαζί». Μαζί πετυχαίνουμε τους στόχους μας. Μαζί μας εξελίσσεσαι. Μαθαίνουμε ασταμάτητα, ξεπερνάμε τον εαυτό μας, χτίζουμε το μέλλον μας. Γινόμαστε όλα όσα είμαστε, χάρη σε σένα!Θέλεις να γίνεις μέλος της ομάδας; Ψάχνουμε υπεύθυνο/η βάρδιας για το κατάστημά μας στην ΧΧΧΧ.Η θέσηΩς Υπεύθυνος/η Βάρδιας, συνεργάζεσαι με την ομάδα για την ομαλή λειτουργία του καταστήματος. Και δεν είσαι μόνος/η καθώς σε κάθε κατάστημα μπορεί να υπάρχουν μέχρι και 2-3 υπεύθυνοι/ες βάρδιας. Μέσα στην ημέρα, μπορεί να αναλάβεις τον συντονισμό μιας μικρής ομάδας ή να εργαστείς αυτόνομα ολοκληρώνοντας σημαντικές εργασίες όπως τον έλεγχο φρεσκάδας. Μια μέρα στη δουλειάΕδώ ξεπερνάμε τον εαυτό μας κάθε μέρα. Και αυτό ξεκινάει από τα πιο μικρά και καθημερινά μας καθήκοντα. Φαντάσου μια μέρα σου στη δουλειά:Το κατάστημα λειτουργεί άψογα, γιατί συμβάλλεις ουσιαστικά στη διαχείρισή του. Οι τιμές μας είναι οι σωστές, τα προϊόντα μας είναι πάντα φρέσκα και το κατάστημα αστράφτει. Ετοιμάζεις τις παραγγελίες, τακτοποιείς τα προϊόντα μας και έτσι τα ράφια είναι πάντα γεμάτα.Αναλαμβάνεις τον συντονισμό μέρους της ομάδας, και εξασφαλίζεις την ολοκλήρωση εργασιών. Μάλιστα, όταν λείπει ο Διευθυντής/ τρια ή ο Υποδιευθυντής/τρια βασιζόμαστε πάνω σου ότι όλα κυλούν ρολόι!Δε φοβάσαι καθόλου τη χειρωνακτική εργασία! Ξέρεις ότι σε ένα κατάστημα πολλές φορές θα χρειαστεί να κουβαλήσεις, να μετακινήσεις και να τακτοποιήσεις εμπορεύματα, παλέτες και κιβώτια στα ράφια τους. Το \'χεις!Ξέρουμε ότι η εμπειρία και η εξυπηρέτηση των πελατών μας είναι μοναδική χάρη σε σένα και την ομάδα. Όχι μόνο οργανώνεις μέρος της ομάδας στις καθημερινές της εργασίες αλλά φροντίζεις να λειτουργεί πάντα ενωμένη.Χρηματοοικονομική διαχείριση και παραγγελίες εμπορευμάτων; Είναι λέξεις που δεν σε τρομάζουν!Δε σταματάς όμως εκεί. Ξέρεις ότι όλα αυτά μπορούν να γίνουν ακόμα καλύτερα και πάντα έρχεσαι με νέες προτάσεις!Είσαι αυτό που αναζητάμε;Ας δούμε τα βασικά:Έχεις πάρει το απολυτήριό σου. ΕΠΑΛ, Γενικό ή Τεχνικό Λύκειο, δεν έχει καμία σημασία. Αν έχεις και ανώτερες σπουδές, ακόμα καλύτερα!Προηγούμενη εμπειρία στον χώρο του εμπορίου είναι έξτρα πόντοι!Η τεχνολογία δε σε τρομάζει, αντίθετα σε βοηθάει να κάνεις τη δουλειά ευκολότερα.Ξέρεις να καθοδηγείς και να συντονίζεις μικρές ομάδες — και το κάνεις με τρόπο που εμπνέει. Η χειρωνακτική εργασία είναι σημαντικό μέρος της καθημερινότητας και δεν σε τρομάζει. Οι άνθρωποι γύρω σου μιλούν για την ευγένεια, τη συνέπεια και την υπευθυνότητά σου. Είσαι ευέλικτος/η με το ωράριό σου και μπορείς να εργαστείς σε εναλλασσόμενες βάρδιες.Τι σου προσφέρουμε εμείςΞέρουμε πόσο σημαντικό είναι να φροντίζουμε την ομάδα. Είμαστε και φέτος Κορυφαίος Εργοδότης στην Ελλάδα (Top Employer). Γιατί δε σταματάμε ποτέ να προσπαθούμε. Μαζί μας, θα βρεις όλα τα παρακάτω:Μηναίο μισθό που ξεκινάει από τα 1.355€ μικτά και φτάνειέως και τα 1.765€ ανάλογα με προηγούμενη εμπειρία και σε περίπτωση που είσαι έγγαμος, για 8ωρη/5ήμερη απασχόληση. Μηναίο μισθό που ξεκινάει από τα 1.035€ μικτά και φτάνειέως και τα 1.340€ ανάλογα με προηγούμενη εμπειρία και σε περίπτωση που είσαι έγγαμος, για 6ωρη/5ήμερη απασχόληση. Μισθός που θα προσαυξάνεται ανάλογα,σε περίπτωση υπερωρίας, νυχτερινής εργασίας ή εργασίας την Κυριακή. Άλλωστε στη Lidl κάθε λεπτό εργασίας καταγράφεται και πληρώνεται. Kουπόνια τροφίμων για τις αγορές σου από τα καταστήματά μας 100€ κάθε μήνα. Bonus 300€ μικτά κάθε Οκτώβριο, εφόσον έχεις συμπληρώσει 6 μήνες στην εταιρία.Σταθερά 5ήμερη εργασία. Ναι, ακόμα και τον Ιούλιο και τον Αύγουστο.Ιδιωτική ιατρική ασφάλιση. Η υγεία σου είναι πάντα η πρώτη μας προτεραιότητα. Γι\' αυτό όλη η ομάδα μας αποκτά ιδιωτική ιατρική ασφά