(657288, 'Cyber Security SOC Manager', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/307963', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 9 λεπτά', '2026-04-23 07:00:37', 'Deloitte', 'Cyber Security SOC Manager What Impact will you make?   #YourOpportunity If you understand the very real dangers cyber threats pose and embrace the challenge of helping keep people and networks safe, then Deloitte Cyber is the right place to develop your career. We offer a wide range of opportunities to work with industry-leading clients and projects — and the technological resources to help them tackle their biggest challenges. A role with Deloitte Cyber, isn’t just a career. It’s a calling. To help make the world more trustworthy, resilient, and secure. If you’re interested in joining a group of people who don’t just want to fix what’s broken but want to build something better, apply for a role with Deloitte Cyber. We are currently seeking Senior professionals with good analytical skills and a well-rounded personality to become part of our dynamic Cyber team. You will build your knowledge and experience working in a team of diverse and talented professionals who enjoy designing and implementing innovative cybersecurity and data protection strategies, for market leading clients in diverse industries. You want to be involved in the definition of new and cutting-edge solutions to address cybersecurity challenges for the most relevant and prestigious clients across industry verticals. You want to work with inspiring, ambitious, and supportive people with diverse geographical and academic backgrounds and extensive skills. You are a cyber enthusiast and visionary and you think that it will shape our future. You get excitement in managing clients shifting priorities and accomplish tasks in a challenging, fast-paced environment. You like to nurture people and share your knowledge with others. Deloitte’s Cyber professionals help organizations focus on enterprise-level cyber risks through a strategic approach. Our services help clients reimagine cyber risk to uncover strategic opportunities aligned with their business priorities — to gain competitive advantage and become more trustworthy, resilient, and secure. We help clients conduct cyber assessments and benchmarking that set a foundation for training and reporting across the organization. And we help them identify potential insider threats and design programs to thwart it. Then we turn the lens toward helping clients modernize their core and traditional/ cloud infrastructures with next-generation security controls that help manage cyber risks and exposure.   #YourRole Manage cybersecurity activities within wider projects, identifying, evaluating, and designing best-in-class security services from security operational, architectural, and engineering perspectives, demonstrating operational excellence, vision, and strategic thinking. Responsible for service management of the team including overall use of resources and initiation of corrective action where required for the SOC team. Responsible for the SOC team’s success in security incident monitoring, identification, assessment, quantification, reporting, communication, and mitigation efforts. Participate in incident response (IR) efforts; detect, identify, respond, contain, and remediate information security incidents. Provide tactical support as needed for major incidents impacting clients. Ensure compliance to Service Level Agreements (SLAs), process adherence and process improvement to achieve operational objectives. Coordination and collaboration with Deloitte’s EMEA Cyber Security Centre to support service delivery. Execute complex project activities, coach and support less experienced team members, and coordinate part of the team while supporting your more senior colleagues in managing client relations and expectations to achieve common goals aligned with business objectives. Manage own work against the project plan to ensure a superior client experience. Engage with internal and external stakeholders to strengthen business relations and create business opportunities. Receive training and attain certifications in the use of cutting-edge cybersecurity products and various cybersecurity topics.   #WinningRequirements Bachelor and/or Master’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Cyber Security or equivalent. 5 - 7 years of experience in a SOC (leading) position (e.g., SOC Manager, SOC team leader, Incident Respond leader, Security Architect, etc.), preferably in an MSSP or consulting company. Working experience in security technologies such as: Security information and event management (SIEM), IDS/IPS, Data Loss Prevention (DLP), Proxy, Web Application Firewall (WAF), Endpoint detection and response (EDR), Anti-Virus, Sandboxing, network- and host- based firewalls, Threat Intelligence, Penetration Testing, etc. Extensive knowledge of Advanced Persistent Threats (APT) tactics, techniques, and procedures. Understanding of possible attack activities such as network probing/ scanning, DDOS, malicious code activity, etc. Technical expertise in incident response planning, handling and management. Relevant professional certifications, such as CISSP, CISM, GIAC certification, and MS Certification, will be considered a plus. Demonstrate leadership and communication skills. Proven ability to translate complex information sets into specific recommendations that can be actioned by customers to enhance their security posture. Be an independent and collaborative person who cooperates in one or more project teams to deliver high-quality results. Possess interpersonal skills and the ability to develop effective and lasting relationships with clients and colleagues. Fluent knowledge of the English language. Military obligations fulfilled where applicable.   #ChooseDeloitteif: You want to work with inspiring, ambitious, and supportive people with diverse geographical and academic backgrounds and extensive skills. You get excitement in managing clients shifting priorities and accomplish tasks in a challenging, fast-paced environment. You like to nurture people and share your knowledge with others.   #AboutDeloitte Our services Deloitte offers Global professional services that include Audit, Risk Advisory, Tax, Consulting and Financial Advisory. Our approach combines insight and innovation from multiple disciplines with global business and industry expertise to help our clients excel anywhere in the world. We deliver outstanding impact on the reputation and success of our clients, in Greece and globally. In pursuing this we contribute to a sustainable and prosperous society, and are firm believers in the positive impact business can and should have on the world it operates within.   Our Purpose Our purpose, “To make an impact that matters for our clients, our people and society “- defines who we are and what we stand for. This is not about size, it\'s about being the first choice. The first choice for the largest and most influential clients, and the first choice for the best talent.   Our values At Deloitte we foster a collaborative culture where talented individuals can produce their best work. We value innovative thinking, diverse insights and a genuinely distinctive level of customer service. We value difference, with respect at the heart of our inclusive culture, and we support agile working arrangements.   Our talent experience From day one at our firm, practitioners are part of a community. Our development and career progression framework will help them develop the skills and capabilities to succeed. The wellness of our people and the ability to offer agile working arrangements is at the centre of our unique talent experience. We create a workplace that encourages collaboration, creativity, inclusiveness to ensure our staff are supported, encouraged, and feel a sense of purpose and meaning in what they do each day.   Sounds like the sort of role for you? Apply now.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(657289, 'Senior Cyber Security Engineer', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/307962', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 3 λεπτά', '2026-04-23 07:00:37', 'Deloitte', 'Senior Cyber Security Engineer What Impact will you make?   #YourOpportunity Do you thrive at solving complex challenges? Want to work on next-generation, cutting-edge products and services that deliver outstanding value? Work with other experts in your field? Work for a world-class organization that provides exceptional career experience and an inclusive and collaborative culture? Want to make an impact that matters? Consider joining Deloitte. We are currently seeking for an enthusiastic team player with exceptional security engineering skills and a well-rounded personality to become part of our dynamic Cyber team in our offices in Athens. The team is part of a European network, where brilliant colleagues collaborate across Deloitte locations to deliver services to our clients both in Greece and abroad. As a Senior Cyber Security Engineer, you will design, develop and support leading security solutions to our clients. Typical engagements include security solutions management such as network, infrastructure, SIEM, XDR, XSOAR, etc.   #YourRole Your role as a Senior Cyber Security Engineer will enable you to work alongside fellow Cyber Security engineers, who are incredibly passionate about what they do and are characterized by their commitment to working as a team and their ever-present customer focus. In this role, you will actively participate and contribute to technical advisory, planning, delivery and support of best-in-class cybersecurity solution technologies for our clients, and you will find yourself in a personal learning, challenging, and development fast-track and will be given many opportunities to get exposure and make an impact that matters. During your tenure as a Senior Cyber Security Engineer, you will be able to: Be part of a global community of Deloitte experts in Cyber Security Engineering. Work on projects focused on development and continuous improvement of security infrastructure. Support clients in identifying weaknesses in their infrastructure by deploying, configuring and supporting Cyber Security tools. Support your wider team in the delivery of cyber security work, including threat modelling, security architecture assessments, cloud security vulnerability assessments, Infrastructure security management, etc. Work closely with the team towards the continuous improvement of services offered. Receive training and attain certifications in the use of cutting-edge cybersecurity products but also on various cybersecurity engineering topics. Work closely with the best experts from many different disciplines and geographies.   #WinningRequirements To qualify for the role, you must have: Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Computer and Network Engineering, IT,  or equivalent work experience. At least 2 years of experience in SOC environment with hands-on knowledge of security-related products and technologies (e.g. Network/Endpoint Security, IDS/IPS, Firewall, SIEM, XDR, SOAR etc.) Experience in troubleshooting security and related network issues. Professional certifications such as Checkpoint Certification (CCSA), Fortinet NSE4, Cisco CCNA, Microsoft SC-200, Microsoft AZ-500 would be considered a strong plus. Commitment to teamwork and ability to build strong client relationships. Strong communication skills (in Greek and in English). Ability to maintain professionalism and always strive for high ethical standards. Military obligations fulfilled where applicable.   #ChooseDeloitteif: You want to work with inspiring, ambitious, and supportive people with diverse geographical and academic backgrounds and extensive skills. You get excitement in managing clients shifting priorities and accomplish tasks in a challenging, fast-paced environment. You like to nurture people and share your knowledge with others.   #AboutDeloitte Our services Deloitte offers Global professional services that include Audit, Risk Advisory, Tax, Consulting and Financial Advisory. Our approach combines insight and innovation from multiple disciplines with global business and industry expertise to help our clients excel anywhere in the world. We deliver outstanding impact on the reputation and success of our clients, in Greece and globally. In pursuing this we contribute to a sustainable and prosperous society, and are firm believers in the positive impact business can and should have on the world it operates within.   Our Purpose Our purpose, “To make an impact that matters for our clients, our people and society “- defines who we are and what we stand for. This is not about size, it\'s about being the first choice. The first choice for the largest and most influential clients, and the first choice for the best talent.   Our values At Deloitte we foster a collaborative culture where talented individuals can produce their best work. We value innovative thinking, diverse insights and a genuinely distinctive level of customer service. We value difference, with respect at the heart of our inclusive culture, and we support agile working arrangements.   Our talent experience From day one at our firm, practitioners are part of a community. Our development and career progression framework will help them develop the skills and capabilities to succeed. The wellness of our people and the ability to offer agile working arrangements is at the centre of our unique talent experience. We create a workplace that encourages collaboration, creativity, inclusiveness to ensure our staff are supported, encouraged, and feel a sense of purpose and meaning in what they do each day.   Sounds like the sort of role for you? Apply now.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(657290, 'Junior Penetration Tester', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/307959', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 5 λεπτά', '2026-04-23 07:00:39', 'Deloitte', 'Junior Penetration Tester   What Impact will you make?   #YourOpportunity Do you thrive at solving complex challenges? Want to work on next-generation, cutting-edge products and services that deliver outstanding value? Work with other experts in your field? Work for a world-class organization that provides exceptional career experience and an inclusive and collaborative culture? Want to make an impact that matters? Consider joining Deloitte. We are currently seeking for enthusiastic team players with exceptional penetration testing skills and a well-rounded personality to become part of our dynamic Cyber - Offensive Security team. The team is part of a global network, where brilliant colleagues collaborate across Deloitte locations, to deliver services to our clients both in Greece and abroad. As a Junior Penetration Tester, you will work in a highly skilled team to perform various Penetration Testing and Red Teaming engagements for our domestic and international clients. Using your offensive skills, you will covertly breach our clients’ networks and provide recommendations to strengthen the client’s security posture. To sharpen your skills, you will be trained with the Offensive Security trainings; you will join the periodic Deloitte Global Ethical Hacking and Red Team knowledge exchange sessions, and perform research on the latest techniques and tools. Moreover, you will serve as a “Subject Matter Expert”, adding interpretive value to findings presented and be responsible for creating and executing custom penetration testing engagements to identify if client systems are vulnerable to security issues.   #YourRole Your role as a Junior Penetration Tester will enable you to work alongside fellow Ethical Hackers, who are incredibly passionate about what they do and are characterized by their commitment to working as a team, and their ever-present customer focus. In this role, you will actively participate in technical planning and the delivery of best-in-class service to our clients. In this role, you will find yourself in a personal learning and development fast track and will be given many opportunities to get exposure and make an impact that matters.   During your tenure as a Junior Penetration Tester, you will be able to: Receive training and attain certifications in the use of cutting-edge cybersecurity products but also on various cybersecurity engineering topics. Be part of a truly global community of Deloitte experts in Ethical Hacking and Cyber Security. Work on projects focused on identifying security vulnerabilities on client’s infrastructure, Web and Mobile Apps etc. Find creative ways to obtain a foothold in a client\'s network. Apply an adversary mindset to simulate sophisticated actors and achieve project-specific objectives. Perform research and develop your own tools and sharpen your tradecraft. Share your research within the Deloitte Global Hacking and Red Team community. Turning security weaknesses into tailored and concrete recommendations. Share knowledge and experiences to support the development of peers. Monitor your own results against objectives and seek feedback to identify ways to improve personal and team performance.   #WinningRequirements To qualify for the role, you must have: Bachelor’s Degree in Information Technology, Information Systems Security, Cybersecurity or any related discipline Familiar with penetration testing like Web Application, Mobile, Infrastructure and Vulnerability Assessments both on *nix and Windows environments. Expertise using Kali Linux and tools like Burp, Metasploit, Covenant, Cobalt Strike, and Nessus. Willingness to research new security testing techniques and tradecraft. Experience effectively prioritizing workload to meet deadlines and work objectives. Demonstrated ability to write clearly, succinctly, and in a manner that appeals to a wide audience. Consultant mindset, commitment to teamwork, and ability to build strong client relationships. Strong communication skills in Greek and English. Ability to maintain professionalism and always strive for high ethical standards. Military obligations fulfilled where applicable Ideally: Burp Suite Certified Practitioner (BSCP) - PortSwigger Hack the Box level: Pro Hacker and above   #ChooseDeloitteif: You want to work with inspiring, ambitious, and supportive people with diverse geographical and academic backgrounds and extensive skills. You get excitement in managing clients shifting priorities and accomplish tasks in a challenging, fast-paced environment. You like to nurture people and share your knowledge with others.   #AboutDeloitte   Our services Deloitte offers Global professional services that include Audit, Risk Advisory, Tax, Consulting and Financial Advisory. Our approach combines insight and innovation from multiple disciplines with global business and industry expertise to help our clients excel anywhere in the world. We deliver outstanding impact on the reputation and success of our clients, in Greece and globally. In pursuing this we contribute to a sustainable and prosperous society, and are firm believers in the positive impact business can and should have on the world it operates within.   Our Purpose Our purpose, “To make an impact that matters for our clients, our people and society “- defines who we are and what we stand for. This is not about size, it\'s about being the first choice. The first choice for the largest and most influential clients, and the first choice for the best talent.   Our values At Deloitte we foster a collaborative culture where talented individuals can produce their best work. We value innovative thinking, diverse insights and a genuinely distinctive level of customer service. We value difference, with respect at the heart of our inclusive culture, and we support agile working arrangements.   Our talent experience From day one at our firm, practitioners are part of a community. Our development and career progression framework will help them develop the skills and capabilities to succeed. The wellness of our people and the ability to offer agile working arrangements is at the centre of our unique talent experience. We create a workplace that encourages collaboration, creativity, inclusiveness to ensure our staff are supported, encouraged, and feel a sense of purpose and meaning in what they do each day.   Sounds like the sort of role for you? Apply now.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(657291, 'Cyber Intelligence Center Security Analyst (Athens, Thessaloniki, Patras)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/307960', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 6 λεπτά', '2026-04-23 07:00:39', 'Deloitte', 'Cyber Intelligence Center Security Analyst (Athens, Thessaloniki, Patras) What Impact will you make?     #YourOpportunity       At Deloitte, the spirit of the excellence is part of our DNA. We strive to hire the brightest minds from all around the globe, allowing us to excel in both long-term strategic thinking and business improvement implementation as the undisputed global leader in professional services. We are committed to delivering impacting results for diverse private and public organization clients, linking our peerless talent in cyber risk with unrivalled opportunities for impact – committing ourselves to sustainable growth and investment in our employees’ development and inclusion along the way. Our culture is rooted in profound shared values. Our values guide us as we live our purpose to serve our clients with quality and distinction, inspire our people to work collaboratively to deliver value, actively contribute to society, and lead the profession by challenging ourselves to do what matters most. Deloitte’s values are what unite us across cultures and geographies, and ultimately help us earn the trust and respect of our people, clients, and society. We believe that our differences enable us to #makeanimpactthatmatters.   #ChooseDeloitteif You want to be involved in the definition and implementation of new and cutting-edge solutions to address cybersecurity detection and response challenges for the most relevant and prestigious clients across industry verticals You want to work with inspiring, ambitious, and supportive people with diverse geographical and academic backgrounds and extensive skills You are a cyber security enthusiast and visionary and are eager to explore how it can be embedded in our future You get excitement in managing clients shifting priorities and accomplish tasks in a challenging, fast-paced environment You like to nurture people and share your knowledge with others   With the scale and complexity of cyber-attacks increasing every year and the world becoming increasingly more interconnected and technology-enabled, being prepared for the inevitable and able to confidently detect and respond to even the most sophisticated incidents, is no longer an option it’s a necessity. Our team, supports clients across industry verticals enhance their preparedness to deal with the inevitable by expanding their visibility over networks and systems through cutting-edge technology, building and maturing their attack detection capability through tried and tested detection analytics, proactively identifying potential indicators of compromise through threat hunting, and supporting them respond to cyber incidents should the need arise.    #YourRole Be part of Deloitte’s Cyber Intelligence Center and conduct advanced cyber security analysis to detect adversaries that may have bypassed conventional controls remaining undetected in our clients’ networks and systems. Analyze network and system activity on client systems (during standard business hours only) leveraging technologies such as EDR, XDR and SIEM, to support detection capability development and incident response efforts. Face and solve client cyber threat prevention, detection, and response challenges in an innovative and effective way. Enable clients to respond to cyber incidents swiftly and effectively supporting containment, eradication, remediation and recovery efforts. Receive training and attain certifications in the use of cutting-edge cybersecurity products but also on various cybersecurity topics. Closely collaborate with experts from many different disciplines and geographies. Be part of a global community of Deloitte experts in Cyber Incident Response and Threat Intelligence that provide clients with actionable intelligence to detect and respond against APTs.   #WinningRequirements University degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Cyber Security or equivalent. 1-2 years of experience, preferably in a Cyber Security Analyst or Cyber Security Engineer role will be considered an advantage. Experience with Windows and Unix/ Linux systems. Solid understanding of core networking and operating systems concepts. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Scripting skills (Python, Powershell, Bash etc.) would be considered advantageous. Passion and curiosity for the cybersecurity industry and technology trends, innovations and frameworks, as well as current IT security technologies. Possess interpersonal skills and the ability to develop effective and lasting relationships with clients and colleagues. Ability to conduct complex analyses and communicate outcomes clearly and concisely. Fluent in both English and Greek language. Military obligations fulfilled where applicable. #ChooseDeloitteif:   You want to work with inspiring, ambitious, and supportive people with diverse geographical and academic backgrounds and extensive skills. You get excitement in managing clients shifting priorities and accomplish tasks in a challenging, fast-paced environment. You like to nurture people and share your knowledge with others.   #AboutDeloitte   Our services Deloitte offers Global professional services that include Audit, Risk Advisory, Tax, Consulting and Financial Advisory. Our approach combines insight and innovation from multiple disciplines with global business and industry expertise to help our clients excel anywhere in the world. We deliver outstanding impact on the reputation and success of our clients, in Greece and globally. In pursuing this we contribute to a sustainable and prosperous society and are firm believers in the positive impact business can and should have on the world it operates within.   Our Purpose Our purpose, “To make an impact that matters for our clients, our people and society “- defines who we are and what we stand for. This is not about size, it\'s about being the first choice. The first choice for the largest and most influential clients, and the first choice for the best talent.   Our values At Deloitte we foster a collaborative culture where talented individuals can produce their best work. We value innovative thinking, diverse insights, and a genuinely distinctive level of customer service. We value difference, with respect at the heart of our inclusive culture, and we support agile working arrangements.   Our talent experience From day one at our firm, practitioners are part of a community. Our development and career progression framework will help them develop the skills and capabilities to succeed. The wellness of our people and the ability to offer agile working arrangements is at the centre of our unique talent experience. We create a workplace that encourages collaboration, creativity, inclusiveness to ensure our staff are supported, encouraged, and feel a sense of purpose and meaning in what they do each day.   Sounds like the sort of role for you? Apply now.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(657292, 'Senior Cyber Intelligence Center Security Analyst', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/307957', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 5 λεπτά', '2026-04-23 07:00:41', 'Deloitte', 'Senior Cyber Intelligence Center Security Analyst What Impact will you make?   #YourOpportunity   If you understand the very real dangers cyber threats pose and embrace the challenge of helping keep people and networks safe, then Deloitte Cyber is the right place to develop your career. We offer a wide range of opportunities to work with industry-leading clients and projects - and the technological resources to help them tackle their biggest challenges. A role with Deloitte Cyber, isn’t just a career. It’s a calling. To help make the world more trustworthy, resilient, and secure. If you’re interested in joining a group of people who don’t just want to fix what’s broken but want to build something better, apply for a role with Deloitte Cyber.   As a Senior Cyber Intelligence Center Security Analyst, you will share your knowledge and experience working in a team of diverse and talented professionals that enjoy supporting clients in building and maturing their cyber-attack detection and response capability.   #YourRole   Be part of Deloitte’s Cyber Intelligence Center and conduct advanced cyber security analysis/ threat hunting activities using known adversary tactics, techniques, and procedures as well as indicators of attack, to detect adversaries that may have bypassed conventional controls remaining undetected in our clients’ networks and systems. Analyze network and system activity on client systems (during standard business hours only) leveraging technologies such as EDR, XDR and SIEM, to support detection capability development and incident response efforts. Face and solve client cyber threat prevention, detection, and response challenges in an innovative and effective way. Enable clients to respond to cyber incidents swiftly and effectively supporting containment, eradication, remediation and recovery efforts. Support your team in advising clients in both technical and tactical decisions when dealing with incidents, ranging from crypto-malware infections to advanced persistent threats (APTs). Support your team in delivering an excellent service to clients through technical reporting and presentations and actively contribute towards continuous service improvement. Receive training and attain certifications in the use of cutting-edge cybersecurity products but also on various cybersecurity topics. Closely collaborate with experts from many different disciplines and geographies. Be part of a global community of Deloitte experts in Cyber Incident Response and Threat Intelligence that supply clients with actionable intelligence to detect and respond against APTs. Leverage on said technology to provide operational excellence and improved detection and response capability to clients.   #WinningRequirements   2-5 years of experience, preferably in a Cyber Security Analyst or Cyber Incident Response role. University degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Cyber Security, and a postgraduate qualification in Information Security or equivalent. Experience with Windows and Unix/ Linux systems. Solid understanding of core networking and operating systems concepts. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Prior experience with log analysis, network traffic analysis and endpoint analysis. Understanding of common cyber threats and adversary tactics, techniques, and procedures (TTPs). Scripting skills (Python, PowerShell, Bash etc.) Passion and curiosity for the cybersecurity industry and technology trends, innovations, and frameworks, as well as current IT security technologies. Be an independent and collaborative person who cooperates in one or more project teams to deliver high quality results. Possess interpersonal skills and the ability to develop effective and lasting relationships with clients and colleagues. Ability to conduct complex analyses and communicate them clearly and concisely to target audiences of different cultures, technical backgrounds and levels of seniority. Fluent in both English and Greek language. Military obligations fulfilled where applicable.   #ChooseDeloitteif:   You want to work with inspiring, ambitious, and supportive people with diverse geographical and academic backgrounds and extensive skills. You get excitement in managing clients shifting priorities and accomplish tasks in a challenging, fast-paced environment. You like to nurture people and share your knowledge with others.   #AboutDeloitte   Our services Deloitte offers Global professional services that include Audit, Risk Advisory, Tax, Consulting and Financial Advisory. Our approach combines insight and innovation from multiple disciplines with global business and industry expertise to help our clients excel anywhere in the world. We deliver outstanding impact on the reputation and success of our clients, in Greece and globally. In pursuing this we contribute to a sustainable and prosperous society and are firm believers in the positive impact business can and should have on the world it operates within.   Our Purpose Our purpose, “To make an impact that matters for our clients, our people and society “- defines who we are and what we stand for. This is not about size, it\'s about being the first choice. The first choice for the largest and most influential clients, and the first choice for the best talent.   Our values At Deloitte we foster a collaborative culture where talented individuals can produce their best work. We value innovative thinking, diverse insights, and a genuinely distinctive level of customer service. We value difference, with respect at the heart of our inclusive culture, and we support agile working arrangements.   Our talent experience From day one at our firm, practitioners are part of a community. Our development and career progression framework will help them develop the skills and capabilities to succeed. The wellness of our people and the ability to offer agile working arrangements is at the centre of our unique talent experience. We create a workplace that encourages collaboration, creativity, inclusiveness to ensure our staff are supported, encouraged, and feel a sense of purpose and meaning in what they do each day.   Sounds like the sort of role for you? Apply now.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(657293, 'Cyber Security GRC Principal/Senior Manager', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/it-jobs/307958', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 16 λεπτά', '2026-04-23 07:00:41', 'Deloitte', 'Cyber Security GRC Principal/Senior Manager What Impact will you make?   #YourOpportunity If you understand the very real dangers cyber threats pose and embrace the challenge of helping keep people and networks safe, then Deloitte Cyber is the right place to develop your career. We offer a wide range of opportunities to work with industry-leading clients and projects — and the technological resources to help them tackle their biggest challenges. A role with Deloitte Cyber, isn’t just a career. It’s a calling. To help make the world more trustworthy, resilient, and secure. If you’re interested in joining a group of people who don’t just want to fix what’s broken but want to build something better, apply for a role with Deloitte Cyber. We are currently seeking experienced professionals with good analytical skills and a well-rounded personality to become part of our dynamic Cyber team. You will build your knowledge and experience working in a team of diverse and talented professionals who enjoy designing and implementing innovative cybersecurity and data protection strategies, for market leading clients in diverse industries (e.g., Financial Services, Energy, Telecommunications Media & Technology, Life Sciences & Healthcare etc.). You want to be involved in the definition of new and cutting-edge solutions to address cybersecurity challenges for the most relevant and prestigious clients across industry verticals. You want to work with inspiring, ambitious, and supportive people with diverse geographical and academic backgrounds and extensive skills. You are a cyber enthusiast and visionary and you think that it will shape our future. You get excitement in managing clients shifting priorities and accomplish tasks in a challenging, fast-paced environment. You like to nurture people and share your knowledge with others. Deloitte’s Cyber professionals help organizations focus on enterprise-level cyber risks through a strategic approach. Our services help clients reimagine cyber risk to uncover strategic opportunities aligned with their business priorities — to gain competitive advantage and become more trustworthy, resilient, and secure. We help clients conduct cyber assessments and benchmarking that set a foundation for training and reporting across the organization. And we help them identify potential insider threats and design programs to thwart it. Then we turn the lens toward helping clients modernize their core and traditional/ cloud infrastructures with next-generation security controls that help manage cyber risks and exposure. You will thrive in a global environment, developing and managing innovative strategic initiatives for customers and collaborating with colleagues belonging to different geographies and backgrounds.   #YourRole Direct and manage cybersecurity projects, identifying, evaluating, and designing best in class cybersecurity and data protection solutions, demonstrating operational excellence, vision and strategic thinking. Lead complex project activities, mentor, and support less experienced team members, coordinate part of the team while supporting your more senior colleagues in managing client relations and expectations. Contribute to the development of the cyber practice. Face and solve customer cybersecurity and data protection technology-driven challenges in an innovative and effective way. Engage with internal and external stakeholders to strengthen business relations and create business opportunities.     #WinningRequirements   Bachelor degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, or a related field. Master’s degree in Cyber/ Information Security, or a related field. Previous relevant managerial experience, preferably in a Consulting company, is required. Previous experience in managing teams, complex problems and budgets is required. Solid expertise in Cyber Security Strategies, Cyber Security Assessments, Cyber Security Frameworks, Data Privacy & Protection concepts. Experience in DORA, NIS2, ISO27001, NIST, AI security. Relevant professional certifications, such as: CISM, CISSP, CISA, CDPSE, CRISC, CIPM, ISO 27001 Lead Auditor etc. Fluent knowledge of English language. Passion and curiosity for the cybersecurity industry and technology trends, innovations and frameworks, as well as current IT security technologies. Be an independent and collaborative person who cooperates in one or more project teams to deliver high quality results. Possess interpersonal skills and the ability to develop effective and lasting relationships with clients and colleagues. Ability to conduct complex analyses and communicate them clearly and concisely to target audiences of different cultures, technical backgrounds and levels of seniority. Military obligations fulfilled where applicable.   #AboutDeloitte Our services Deloitte operates in Greece since 1975, as a member of one of the world’s largest professional services networks, Deloitte Touche Tohmatsu. With offices in Athens, Thessaloniki, Heraklion, Patras and Ioannina, Deloitte Greece employs more than 2,900 professionals. After 50 years of successful and dynamic presence in the Greek market, we bring an unmatched breadth and depth of expertise across audit and assurance, technology & transformation, tax & legal and strategy, risk & transactions advisory services. Operating in a multidisciplinary model enables us to draw from a pool of world-class talent, identifying the ideal skillset for each project, and to collaborate across businesses, to solve the toughest, most challenging issues of our clients. It is with them that we have built a trusted relationship, by delivering innovative solutions and utilizing state-of-the-art tools and technologies across all industries- Consumer Products, Energy Resources & Industrials, Financial Services, Life Sciences & Health Care, Government & Public Services, Technology, Media & Telecommunications.   Our Purpose Our purpose, “To make an impact that matters for our clients, our people and society “- defines who we are and what we stand for. This is not about size, it\'s about being the first choice. The first choice for the largest and most influential clients, and the first choice for the best talent.   Our values At Deloitte we foster a collaborative culture where talented individuals can produce their best work. We value innovative thinking, diverse insights, and a genuinely distinctive level of customer service. We value difference, with respect at the heart of our inclusive culture, and we support agile working arrangements.   Our talent experience From day one at our firm, practitioners are part of a community. Our development and career progression framework will help them develop the skills and capabilities to succeed. The wellness of our people and the ability to offer agile working arrangements is at the centre of our unique talent experience. We create a workplace that encourages collaboration, creativity, inclusiveness to ensure our staff are supported, encouraged, and feel a sense of purpose and meaning in what they do each day.   Sounds like the sort of role for you? Apply now.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
