(660126, 'Assistant Bar Manager', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309157?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν 9 λεπτά', '2026-04-27 15:00:25', 'Mandarin Oriental Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for an Assistant Bar Manager to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Assistant Bar Manager assists the Bar Manager in developing and implementing beverage menus and bar philosophy in line with Mandarin Oriental standards. The Assistant Bar Manager reports to the Bar Manager. As Assistant Bar Manager, you will be responsible for the following duties: Provide knowledgeable, friendly, and professional bar service, ensuring high guest satisfaction. Prepare and serve beverages, while maintaining full knowledge of menus, promotions, recipes, and garnishes. Oversee wine and beverage inventory, stock control and billing accuracy, while ensuring adherence to Mandarin Oriental standards. Ensure cleanliness, safety, sanitation, and proper presentation of Front and Back of House bar areas at all times. Promote respectful, generous service and effective communication within the F&B team through regular briefings and meetings. Maintain close collaboration with the Culinary team to ensure smooth operations and a harmonious working environment. As Assistant Bar Manager, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Experience in a similar role. Fluency in English. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(660127, 'Εξωτερικός Πωλητής Β2Β - Ενέργεια - Μισθός από 1200 - αυτοκίνητο', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/sales-or-business-development-or-account-management-jobs/309160?origin=pjp', 'Ναύπλιο', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-27 15:00:25', 'CQS SA', 'Η CQS διακρίθηκε ξανά! Στη φετινή κατάταξη Top Employers 2025 του WhereWeWork.com — βάσει των αξιολογήσεων των ανθρώπων μας — πετύχαμε:🏆 1η θέση στον κλάδο BPO & Services 🌟 2η θέση στη συνολική κατάταξη Top 50 στην ΕλλάδαΓίνε κι εσύ μέλος μιας ομάδας που διακρίνεται για το εργασιακό της περιβάλλον!Στη CQS, Leading Employer in Greece, είμαστε μια ομάδα περισσότερων από 2000 ανθρώπων που πετυχαίνει κάτι καταπληκτικό καθημερινά, αντιμετωπίζουμε προκλήσεις και κατακτάμε τους στόχους μας!Εάν και εσύ έχεις πάθος για την επίτευξη των στόχων σου και θέλεις να είσαι μέλος μιας ομάδας που κερδίζει, γίνε ο επόμενος Εξωτερικός Πωλητής Β2Β για κορυφαία εταιρεία ενέργειας! Τι θα κάνεις;Ο ρόλος σου θα εστιάζει στην direct προώθηση υπηρεσιών της κορυφαίας εταιρείας ενέργειας σε εταιρικούς πελάτες, με σκοπό την ανάπτυξη του πελατολογίου στην περιοχή ευθύνης σου και την παροχή υπηρεσιών υψηλού επιπέδου.Έλα στην ομάδα μας αν:  Έχεις άριστες επικοινωνιακές και διαπραγματευτικές δεξιότητες  Γνωρίζεις πως να κερδίζεις την εμπιστοσύνη του πελάτη  Είσαι προσανατολισμένος στο αποτέλεσμα  Σε διακρίνει ομαδικό πνεύμα Θέλεις να εργάζεσαι για τον Κορυφαίο Εργοδότη της Ελλάδας για το 2025!Διαθέτεις επιπλέον:  Απολυτήριο Λυκείου   Δίπλωμα αυτοκινήτου (με ισχύ άνω του 6μήνου)  Καλή γνώση Η/Υ  Εκπληρωμένες στρατιωτικές υποχρεώσεις  Η προϋπηρεσία στον κλάδο των πωλήσεων θα θεωρηθεί επιπρόσθετο προσόν Τι σου προσφέρουμε: Ανταγωνιστικό μηνιαίο πακέτο αποδοχών ανάλογο της προϋπηρεσίας και ασφάλιση Αναγνώριση και επιβράβευση με υψηλό bonus βάσει ατομικής επίτευξης στόχωνΣύμβαση εργασίας αορίστου χρόνου Αυτοκίνητο & καύσιμα κίνησης Κινητό & laptop Ongoing μάθηση και υποστήριξη από την έμπειρη ομάδα πωλητών μαςΔομημένο πρόγραμμα onboarding από την πρώτη μέρα και προσωπικός buddy που θα σε καθοδηγεί στα πρώτα σου βήματα Refer a Friend πρόγραμμα με bonus! Ομαδικές εθελοντικές δράσεις, προνόμια και εκδηλώσεις όλο το χρόνο Φιλικό και υποστηρικτικό εργασιακό περιβάλλονΓια εμάς η διαφορετικότητα δεν είναι απλώς μια λέξη, αλλά ο ίδιος ο παλμός της προόδου και της καινοτομίας. Τα χρώματα της διαφορετικότητας μας εμπνέουν και μας ωθούν να δημιουργούμε ένα περιβάλλον εργασίας που είναι ανοιχτό, συμπεριληπτικό και χωρίς διακρίσεις. Είμαστε υπερήφανο μέλος της Χάρτας Διαφορετικότητας για Ελληνικές επιχειρήσεις. Στην ομάδα μας πιστεύουμε ότι η αξία κάθε ατόμου δεν σχετίζεται με τα χαρακτηριστικά του φύλου, της ηλικίας, της εθνικότητας, του σεξουαλικού προσανατολισμού, της αναπηρίας, των χρόνιων παθήσεων ή της θρησκείας.Στην CQS δεν αναζητούμε τέλειους ανθρώπους. Χτίζουμε την ομάδα που ταιριάζει τέλεια σ’ εσένα.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660128, 'Sales Associate / Πωλητής / Πωλήτρια Καταστήματος - Γλυφάδα - Full Time', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/sales-or-business-development-or-account-management-jobs/309148', 'Γλυφάδα', 'πριν 4 λεπτά', '2026-04-27 15:00:27', 'Αφοι Βοτση - Cozykids', 'Η Flexa/Cozykids ξεχωρίζει για τα παιδικά έπιπλα κορυφαίας ποιότητας και υψηλής αισθητικής, προσφέροντας μοναδικά προϊόντα για το παιδί, με έμφαση στην ασφάλεια και την οικολογική συνείδηση. Στόχος μας είναι να παρέχουμε την καλύτερη εμπειρία σε γονείς που αναζητούν την εξαιρετική ποιότητα. Ενισχύουμε την ομάδα μας με Πωλητές/Πωλήτριες για το κατάστημά μας στη Γλυφάδα.   Απαραίτητα προσόντα: - Προϋπηρεσία στη λιανική πώληση (προϋπηρεσία στην πώληση επίπλων θα εκτιμηθεί) - Πολύ καλή γνώση Αγγλικών - Άνεση στη χρήση Η/Υ   - Άριστη εξυπηρέτηση και επικοινωνιακές δεξιότητες   - Θετική διάθεση, επαγγελματισμός και ομαδικό πνεύμα   - Ευελιξία ωραρίου (8ωρη εργασία – κυλιόμενες βάρδιες)    Παροχές:   - Σταθερή θέση πλήρους απασχόλησης - Μηνιαία κάρτα σίτισης - Bonus πωλήσεων - Πρόγραμμα ομαδικής ασφάλισης   - Έκπτωση στα προϊόντα των καταστημάτων μας - Συνεχής εκπαίδευση και υποστήριξη στην εργασία - Ευχάριστο και αξιοκρατικό εργασιακό περιβάλλον Θέλεις να γίνεις μέλος της οικογένειας της Flexa/Cozykids και να εργαστείς σε έναν χώρο όπου πρωταγωνιστούν η ποιότητα και η φροντίδα; Στείλε μας το βιογραφικό σου σήμερα!', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660129, 'Assistant Restaurant Manager', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309155?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν 9 λεπτά', '2026-04-27 15:00:27', 'Mandarin Oriental Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for an Assistant Restaurant Manager to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars About the job Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Assistant Restaurant Manager assists the F&B management in the leadership of the service team, while driving service excellence and delivering the Mandarin Oriental objectives. As Assistant Restaurant Manager, you will be responsible for the following duties:  Support F&B management in operational and administrative tasks, stepping in during their absence. Manage daily operations and shifts to ensure smooth and efficient service, while maintaining strong communication with the culinary team. Assist in supervising duty schedules and ensure compliance with them. Lead the service team and foster effective teamwork. Ensure all operational and quality standards are met consistently. Oversee outlet maintenance, cleanliness, and collaborate with engineering and housekeeping for regular inspections. As Assistant Restaurant Manager, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. 2 years\' experience in a similar role, in a luxury hotel operation. Fluency in English. Local and international food and beverage awareness. Advanced knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite; Outlook, Word, Excel and PowerPoint. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(660130, 'Γραμματειακή Υποστήριξη', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/medicine-or-healthcare-jobs/309154', 'Νέα Ερυθραία', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-27 15:00:29', 'Affidea', 'Job description O Όμιλος Affidea, o μεγαλύτερος πάροχος πρωτοβάθμιων υπηρεσιών υγείας στην Ευρώπη, στα πλαίσια της συνεχούς ανάπτυξης των δραστηριοτήτων του, αναζητά Γραμματειακή Υποστήριξη για να ενταχθεί στην ομάδα του Affidea Ν. Ερυθραίας! Job description: Υποδοχή και Εξυπηρέτηση εξεταζομένων Kαταχώρηση εξετάσεων και παράδοση αποτελεσμάτων Τηλεφωνική εξυπηρέτηση πελατών και προγραμματισμός ραντεβού Συντονισμός και συνεργασία με επιμέρους τμήματα Job requirements Έως 2 έτη εμπειρίας σε αντίστοιχη θέση σε Διαγνωστικό Κέντρο Καλή γνώση Αγγλικών Επικοινωνιακές δεξιότητες και συνεργατικότητα Δυνατότητα απασχόλησης σε ευέλικτα ωράρια και βάρδιες What we Offer: Σύγχρονο εργασιακό περιβάλλον με υψηλές απαιτήσεις Ικανοποιητικό πακέτο αποδοχών Ιδιωτική Ασφάλεια Υγείας Ένταξη στην εκπτωτική πολιτική των υπηρεσιών του Ομίλου Affidea Συνεχής επιμόρφωση, ανάπτυξη και εξέλιξη Σχετικά με την Affidea: Είμαστε ένας εξαιρετικά επιτυχημένος πανευρωπαϊκός πάροχος υγειονομικής περίθαλψης που προσφέρει κορυφαίες υπηρεσίες εξωτερικών ιατρείων, απεικόνιση, εργαστηριακή διάγνωση, ορθοπεδική και ανίχνευση καρκίνου και θεραπεία. Η ομάδα της Affidea αποτελείται από αφοσιωμένους και έμπειρους επαγγελματίες υγείας και δουλεύουμε μόνο με τεχνολογία αιχμής. Διαθέτοντας ένα εξαιρετικά σεβαστό portfolio ιατρικών κέντρων σε ολόκληρη την ήπειρο, οι υπηρεσίες της Affidea βρίσκονται στην αιχμή της περίθαλψης των ασθενών - μια \"γραμμή ασφαλείας\" για τους ασθενείς που χρειάζονται την εμπειρογνωμοσύνη της, η οποία είναι διαθέσιμη σε 15 χώρες σε ολόκληρη την Ευρώπη.Στην Affidea, πιστεύουμε ότι δεν υπάρχει τίποτα πιο σημαντικό από την υγεία. Είμαστε παθιασμένοι με την υγεία και ευσυνείδητοι απέναντι στους ανθρώπους. *Μπορείτε να βρείτε και να ενημερωθείτε για την “Πολιτική Ιδιωτικότητας Προσωπικών Δεδομένων για Υποψήφιους Συνεργάτες” της Affidea, ακολουθώντας τo Link που σας οδηγεί σε αυτή.', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660131, 'Πωλητές – Πωλήτριες Αμπελόκηποι 3 (6ωρη μερική απασχόληση)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/retail-jobs/309152?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-27 15:00:29', 'PET CITY GROUP ΑΕΒΕ', 'Έχεις πάθος για τις πωλήσεις? Θέλεις να εργαστείς και να εξελίξεις την καριέρα σου σε ένα δυναμικό και συνεχώς αναπτυσσόμενο περιβάλλον? Αγαπάς τα κατοικίδια όσο εμείς? Μην περιμένεις άλλο! Κάνε τώρα την αίτησή σου και γίνε μέλος της πιο Pawsome ομάδας🐾   Ποιοι είμαστε; Ο Όμιλος Pet City είναι η μεγαλύτερη αλυσίδα καταστημάτων τροφών και αξεσουάρ κατοικίδιων ζώων στην Ελλάδα, με παρουσία άνω των 35 χρόνων στο χώρο του λιανικού εμπορίου. Η ομάδα μας αποτελείται από ένα δίκτυο 100+  καταστημάτων και 800 ανθρώπων που αγαπούν τα ζώα, τους αρέσει η εξέλιξη και η γνώση και δίνουμε καθημερινά τον καλύτερό μας εαυτό στην Pet εξυπηρέτηση. Στα πλαίσια της ανάπτυξης μας αναζητούμε ενθουσιώδεις υποψηφίους με πάθος για τις πωλήσεις και προσανατολισμένους στην καλύτερη δυνατή εξυπηρέτηση των πελατών μας για 6ωρη μερική απασχόληση για τις θέσεις Πωλητής/τρια στο κατάστημα μας Αμπελόκηποι 3.    Τι κάνει ένα Sales Associate να ξεχωρίζει; Ως Sales Associate είσαι η καρδιά των καταστημάτων μας. Με το χαμόγελο και την ευχάριστη διάθεση σου συμβουλεύεις και καθοδηγείς κάθε Pet Parent, ώστε να μας εμπιστεύονται καθημερινά τόσο για τις αγορές τους, όσο και για την φροντίδα των αγαπημένων τους pets. Κάποια από τα χαρακτηριστικά που θα πρέπει ένας πετυχημένος Sales Associate να έχει, είναι ο προσανατολισμός στον πελάτη, ευχέρεια στην επικοινωνία, ευγένεια, αξιοπιστία, να είναι στοργικός, φιλόζωος, συνεπής και προσαρμοστικός και πάνω από όλα να θέλει να μάθει και να εξελιχθεί εντός του Ομίλου μας!   Οι αρμοδιότητες σας: Υποδοχή, ενημέρωση και καθοδήγηση πελατών για την καλύτερη επιλογή αγοράς Πωλήσεις και εξυπηρέτηση μετά την πώληση εξασφαλίζοντας ένα θετικό customer experience Έλεγχος stock καταστήματος και αναπλήρωση όταν είναι απαραίτητο για την καλύτερη δυνατή εξυπηρέτηση των αναγκών Διεκπεραίωση των παραγγελιών, παραλαβή και οργάνωση αποθήκης και του κεντρικού χώρου του καταστήματος Παραλαβή και έλεγχος παραγγελίας Χρήση ταμειακής μηχανής Απαραίτητα προσόντα: Διάθεση για εκπαίδευση και εξέλιξη Προσανατολισμός στην εξυπηρέτηση του πελάτη  Βασική γνώση αγγλικών και Η/Υ Ευχέρεια στην επικοινωνία και ευχάριστη προσωπικότητα Υπευθυνότητα και συνέπεια Ομαδικό πνεύμα συνεργασίας Οι παροχές μας: 💶  Σταθερό πακέτο αποδοχών 🏆 Πρόγραμμα επιβράβευσης για την επίτευξη των εταιρικών στόχων 🎓 Συνεχής εκπαίδευση και ανάπτυξη  💼 Ευκαιρίες επαγγελματικής εξέλιξης σε Supervisor à Store Supervisor à Store Manager μέσα σε ένα δυναμικό και συνεχώς αναπτυσσόμενο περιβάλλον 💊 Προνομιακές τιμές και εκπτώσεις σε δίκτυο συνεργαζόμενων εταιρειών για παροχές υγείας, ευ ζην και ασφάλισης 🏷️ Εκπτώσεις για το προσωπικό στα προϊόντα και της υπηρεσίες μας.', 'Μερική απασχόληση'),
(660132, 'HR Operations Senior Manager', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/administrative-or-secretarial-jobs/309146', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 5 λεπτά', '2026-04-27 15:00:31', 'ManpowerGroup Greece', 'Manpowergroup, on behalf of its client, a leading company in the Hospitality Industry, is looking for an HR Operations Senior Manager.The company has established a strong reputation for delivering exceptional guest experiences through operational excellence. This role is a key strategic position within the HR department, ensuring smooth HR operations across the resort and delivering an outstanding employee experience throughout the full employee lifecycle.📌 Location: Crete, Greece📍 Working Model: On-site🖋️ You will be reporting to: HR Operations DirectorWhat you will do:As an HR Operations Senior Manager, you will act as the critical link between HR and Operations, overseeing the daily functions of the HR department within the resort and ensuring the smooth execution of all HR operational processes.More specifically, the candidate will:HR Operations & Strategy Alignment:● Ensure HR operational policies and procedures are continuously improved and aligned with the Group’s HR strategy.● Lead the HR Operations team and supervise the smooth operation of employee accommodation and employee services within the resort.Recruitment, Hiring & Employee Lifecycle:● Monitor recruitment progress and hiring timelines in collaboration with Hiring Managers and Talent Acquisition teams.● Ensure high-quality pre-boarding, onboarding, hiring, and offboarding experience for all seasonal employees.● Oversee job offers, repeaters, and new joiners while ensuring business standards and timelines are met.Employee Experience & Retention:● Implement employee retention strategies to improve engagement and increase repeater rates for future seasons.● Manage employee recognition programs, satisfaction assessments, and turnover analysis.● Ensure excellent working conditions, a healthy work environment, and equal and fair treatment for all employees.Employee Relations & Compliance:● Oversee employee behavior, disciplinary procedures, and compliance with internal HR policies.● Manage employee relations, including collaboration with unions and local labor authorities when required.● Ensure compliance with Greek labor law, employee contracts, payroll reconciliation, permits, sick leaves, absenteeism, and appraisal processes.HR Collaboration & Reporting:● Collaborate closely with Compensation & Benefits, Learning & Development, and Talent Acquisition teams to support business goals.● Manage HR operational budget and prepare detailed HR reports with insights, action plans, and KPI analysis to support strategic decision-making.What we are looking for:● Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Hospitality Management, or a related field● 2-3 years of experience in a similar HR Operations role, preferably within hospitality or large-scale organizations● Strong knowledge of Greek labor law and HR operational processes● Advanced user of MS Office, especially Excel and PowerPoint● Experience with HR systems and tools such as Pylon, ERGANI, or similar HRM platforms● Strong leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills● Strong analytical thinking with the ability to translate HR KPIs into actionable strategies● Ability to work under pressure, manage multiple priorities, and proactively solve problems● Hands-on management style with strong employee-centric approachCompensation package and Benefits:✔️ Competitive salary⚕️ Private Medical Insurance📖 Continuous training and development opportunities🏨 Dynamic hospitality environment with strong career growth potential👥 Recruitment Process:If you’re interested in this role, feel free to apply directly. Our consultants will contact the candidates who meet the profile’s requirements to arrange an interview.#Empoweringtalent #WebelieveinTalent #ManpowerGroupGreece', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660133, 'Pizza Chef De Partie', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309151?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-27 15:00:31', 'Mandarin Oriental Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Pizza Chef De Partie to join our Culinary team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Culinary Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Pizza Chef De Partie carries out kitchen duties whilst ensuring smooth, coordinated team effort in the kitchen, with a focus on pizza preparation and baking. The Chef De Partie reports to the Pizza Chef. As Pizza Chef De Partie, you will be responsible for the following duties:  Work closely with the Pizza Sapienza team on daily operations, ensuring consistent quality in pizza production, including dough preparation, fermentation, and baking. Prepare and cook pizzas following established recipes and standards, ensuring proper texture, flavor, and presentation. Ensure proper food handling, monitor raw food availability, and inspect incoming goods. Attend all training sessions and participate in special events, promotions, and demonstrations. Maintain a clean, presentable uniform and ensure personal hygiene. Inform the Executive Chef and Pizza Chef regarding operational issues. Complete additional tasks as assigned by management. As Pizza Chef De Partie, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Globally recognized Culinary Qualification. 3 years of culinary experience, with a focus on pizza or Italian cuisine. Good level in English or Greek.  Our commitment to you: Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(660134, 'Security Officer (Προσωπικό Ασφαλείας)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/security-jobs/309147?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν 21 λεπτά', '2026-04-27 15:00:33', 'Mandarin Oriental Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for Security Officers to join our Security team. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Security Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Security Officer is responsible for the safety and security of all guests, colleagues and visitors of Mandarin Oriental, and the protection of all hotel assets. The Security Officer reports to the Security Supervisor. As Security Officer, you will be responsible for the following duties: Conduct property patrols and periodic inspections as per hotel procedures. Maintain accurate key control and follow lost and found procedures. Monitor safety and security systems, including surveillance cameras. Control entry and exit at the main gate to ensure safety. Respond to emergencies as part of the Emergency Response Team. Complete incident reports and cooperate with authorities when necessary. As Security Officer, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Valid Greek security personnel work permit. Basic first aid knowledge will be considered a plus. Fluency in English and Greek. Computer literacy in MS Office. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660135, 'Stewarding Supervisor', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309149?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν μερικά δευτερόλεπτα', '2026-04-27 15:00:33', 'Mandarin Oriental Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Stewarding Supervisor to join our Stewarding team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Stewarding Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Stewarding Supervisor oversees the work of the Stewards, ensuring that all areas are kept clean and free of hazards. The Stewarding Supervisor reports to the Back of House Manager. As Stewarding Supervisor, you will be responsible for the following duties:  Maintain the cleanliness of all stewarding areas and kitchen equipment, while keeping accurate records of cleaning schedules and chemicals used.  Lead, train and supervise the Stewarding Team, while ensuring Mandarin Oriental standards are followed. Ensure all set-ups and supplies are in place for each function. Ensure all breakages and chipped items are removed from circulation and inventoried for warranty. Ensure all kitchen equipment is in working order, report any items in need of repair and create an engineering request. Maintain a clean and safe work environment for all colleagues. As Stewarding Supervisor, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Previous working experience as a Stewarding Supervisor or in a similar role in the hospitality industry. Good level in English & Greek. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(660136, 'Εργάτες / Εργάτριες Παραγωγής', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/production-jobs/309145', 'Θεσσαλονίκη', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-27 15:00:35', 'AGRINO - ΕΥ ΓΕ ΠΙΣΤΙΟΛΑΣ ΑΒΕΕ', 'Η Agrino, Βιομηχανία Παραγωγής και Εμπορίας Ρυζιών, Οσπρίων και Ρυζογκοφρετών, αναζητά στην ΒΙΠΕΘ Σίνδου Θεσσαλονίκης   Εργάτες/Εργάτριες Παραγωγής   -Τοποθεσία :                  Θεσσαλονίκη -Διεύθυνση εργασίας:   Σίνδος, ΒΙΠΕΘ -Απασχόληση :               Πλήρης απασχόληση, 3-βάρδιο, 5-θήμερο -Αποδοχές :                    Αναλόγως των προσόντων Καθήκοντα Συμμετοχή στη διαδικασία παραγωγής και συσκευασίας Έλεγχος προϊόντων (οπτικός και βασικός ποιοτικός έλεγχος) Τροφοδοσία και παρακολούθηση μηχανών Καθαριότητα και τακτοποίηση χώρου εργασίας Τήρηση κανόνων υγιεινής και ασφάλειας Απαραίτητα προσόντα Απόφοιτος Δευτεροβάθμιας Εκπαίδευσης ή Τεχνικής Σχολής Δυνατότητα εργασίας σε βάρδιες Υπευθυνότητα και συνέπεια Ομαδικό πνεύμα Προαιρετική γνώση του Microsoft Office/WMS (Προϋπηρεσία σε βιομηχανία θα εκτιμηθεί, αλλά δεν είναι απαραίτητη) Παροχές Σταθερή εργασία σε οργανωμένο περιβάλλον Ανταγωνιστικές αποδοχές Εκπαίδευση στη θέση εργασίας Δυνατότητα εξέλιξης Ιδιωτική ιατροφαρμακευτική περίθαλψη', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660137, 'Χειριστές Μηχανών Παραγωγής ή/και Συσκευασίας', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/production-jobs/309144', 'Θεσσαλονίκη', 'πριν 16 λεπτά', '2026-04-27 15:00:35', 'AGRINO - ΕΥ ΓΕ ΠΙΣΤΙΟΛΑΣ ΑΒΕΕ', 'Η Agrino, βιομηχανία Παραγωγής και Εμπορίας Ρυζιών, Οσπρίων και Ρυζογκοφρετών, αναζητά στην ΒΙΠΕΘ Σίνδου Θεσσαλονίκης   Χειριστές Μηχανών Παραγωγής ή/και Συσκευασίας   -Τοποθεσία :                  Θεσσαλονίκη -Διεύθυνση εργασίας:   Σίνδος, ΒΙΠΕΘ -Απασχόληση :               Πλήρης απασχόληση, 3-βάρδιο, 5-θήμερο -Αποδοχές :                     Αναλόγως των προσόντων   Αρμοδιότητες Χειρισμός και επίβλεψη μηχανών παραγωγής ή/και συσκευασίας Παρακολούθηση της παραγωγικής διαδικασίας και εξασφάλιση ομαλής λειτουργίας Έλεγχος ποιότητας προϊόντων κατά τη διάρκεια της παραγωγής Τήρηση οδηγιών παραγωγής και διαδικασιών ασφάλειας & υγιεινής Συμμετοχή σε βασικές εργασίες συντήρησης και καθαρισμού εξοπλισμού   Απαραίτητα / Επιθυμητά Προσόντα Απόφοιτος ΑΤΕΙ ή Τεχνικής Σχολής (Μηχανολογία, Ηλεκτρολογία, Αυτοματισμός, Τεχνολογίας Τροφίμων, Γεωπονίας ή συναφές αντικείμενο – επιθυμητό) Προϋπηρεσία σε βιομηχανικό περιβάλλον ή παραγωγή (επιθυμητή) και ειδικά σε βιομηχανία τροφίμων. Βασικές γνώσεις Η/Υ και Αγγλικών (επιθυμητές) Επιθυμητή γνώση Microsoft Office και WMS Δυνατότητα εργασίας σε βάρδιες Συνέπεια, υπευθυνότητα και ομαδικό πνεύμα   Τι προσφέρουμε Σταθερή εργασία σε οργανωμένο περιβάλλον Ανταγωνιστικές αποδοχές Εκπαίδευση στη θέση εργασίας Δυνατότητα εξέλιξης Ιδιωτική ιατροφαρμακευτική περίθαλψη', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660138, 'Room Attendant (Καμαριέρα)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309143?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-27 15:00:37', 'Mandarin Oriental Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for Room Attendants to join our Housekeeping team, for season 2026.  Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Housekeeping Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Room Attendant ensures occupied and vacant guestrooms are cleaned and maintained up to the Mandarin Oriental standards. The Room Attendant reports to the Housekeeping Supervisor. As Room Attendant, you will be responsible for the following duties:  Clean guestrooms and bathrooms, including all inside windows and mirrors. After cleaning, dry all areas, fixtures, and surfaces. Replenish amenities. Efficiently make beds to meet Mandarin Oriental appearance standards. Remove soiled linens and towels from guestrooms, and hand them over to Housemen or dispose in linen chute. Arrange clothing items in occupied guestrooms and fold them neatly. Remove guestroom service trays from guestroom hallways. Ensure to sign in and out for keys and hand-held device on a daily basis. Hand over any special requests to the incoming shift leader or respective manager. Report any suspicious person or item in the guest rooms and corridors. Report missing, damaged or substandard furniture, fixtures, and equipment. Ensure that electronic devices (television, remote controls, stereo, lamps, and telephones) are working properly. Ensure guestrooms assigned are completed, with correct status marked at the end of the day, including any information for input into guest history file. As Room Attendant, we expect from you: Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. 1 year of housekeeping experience will be considered as a plus. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(660139, 'F&B Host / Hostess', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309142?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν 15 λεπτά', '2026-04-27 15:00:37', 'Mandarin Oriental Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for an F&B Host/Hostess to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the F&B Host/Hostess is responsible to provide the highest level of service and professional excellence, being ever present in the operation, ensuring the highest standards and satisfying completely our guests during their meal experience. The F&B Host/Hostess reports to the F&B Supervisor. As F&B Host/Hostess, you will be responsible for the following duties: Support restaurant operations, including greeting, seating, and resetting tables. Provide kind and professional service to both guests and colleagues. Manage reservations using the SevenRooms system, ensuring accuracy and efficiency. Assist with guest inquiries, special requests, and communicate key information to the team. Maintain cleanliness, organisation, and stock of menus, newspapers, and surroundings. Respond proactively to guest feedback, ensuring satisfaction and effective communication. As F&B Host/Hostess, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Working experience in a similar role. Fluency in English. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(660140, 'Mini Bar Attendant', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309141?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν 5 λεπτά', '2026-04-27 15:00:39', 'Mandarin Oriental Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Mini Bar Attendant to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece the Mini Bar Attendant maintains and replenishes mini-bars in guest rooms, ensuring accuracy in inventory, billing, and presentation while delivering the legendary Mandarin Oriental guest experience. The Mini Bar Attendant reports to the Assistant In Room Dining Manager. As Mini Bar Attendant, you will be responsible for the following duties: Restock mini-bars according to Mandarin Oriental standards. Conduct daily inventory checks and update consumption records in the system. Ensure accurate posting of charges to guests\' account records and resolve discrepancies promptly. Maintain cleanliness and presentation of mini-bar areas; report maintenance issues. Uphold safety and hygiene standards, including proper handling of alcoholic beverages. Respond to guest inquiries with courtesy and efficiency. As Mini Bar Attendant, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Valid driving license. 1 year of experience in a similar role, in a luxury hotel/restaurant/bar operation. Good level of English. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(660141, 'BSB Spanish-Speaking e-Shop Administrator', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/general-management-jobs/309123', 'Νέα Φιλαδέλφεια', 'πριν 5 λεπτά', '2026-04-27 15:00:39', 'B and F', 'Job Overview We are seeking a detail-oriented and proactive Spanish-Speaking E-Shop Administrator to manage and maintain our online store. The ideal candidate will ensure smooth daily operations of the e-commerce platform, provide excellent customer support in Spanish, and optimize product listings to drive sales and customer satisfaction. Key Responsibilities Manage and update product listings (descriptions, images, stock levels) Translate and localize product content into Spanish Monitor and process online orders, returns, and refunds Provide customer support via email, chat, and phone in Spanish Coordinate with logistics and warehouse teams to ensure timely deliveries Assist in promotional campaigns, discounts, and seasonal sales Optimize product pages for SEO and conversion Create, schedule, and send newsletters to Spanish-speaking customers Plan and publish social media posts (Facebook, Instagram, etc.) Requirements Native or fluent Spanish (written and spoken) Good command of English (preferred) Strong organizational and multitasking skills Attention to detail and accuracy Basic knowledge of SEO principles Customer-service oriented mindset Preferred Qualifications Previous experience in e-commerce administration Familiarity with digital marketing tools Basic understanding of analytics tools (Google Analytics, etc.)', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση');
