(660142, 'Bartender/Mixologist', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309139?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν 11 λεπτά', '2026-04-27 15:00:41', 'Mandarin Oriental Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Bartender/Mixologist to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Bartender/Mixologist drives the development and maintenance of an innovative and unique beverage menu. The Bartender/Mixologist reports to the Head Bartender. As Bartender/Mixologist, you will be responsible for the following duties: Provide respectful and generous service to both guests and colleagues. Greet guests, explain menu items, and provide recommendations. Prepare and serve drinks while ensuring accuracy and guest satisfaction. Maintain cleanliness, organisation, and proper stock levels in the bar area. Follow liquor regulations and ensure all served items are accounted for on the bill. Attend training sessions and department meetings. As Bartender/Mixologist, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. 1-2 years of bartending experience. Fluency in English. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(660143, 'Senior Sommelier', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309140?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν μερικά δευτερόλεπτα', '2026-04-27 15:00:41', 'Mandarin Oriental Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Senior Sommelier to join our Food & Beverage team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Food & Beverage Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Senior Sommelier supports the Head of Wines in delivering an exceptional wine experience, leading by example on the floor, mentoring Sommeliers, and ensuring operational excellence, cost control, and guest satisfaction. The Senior Sommelier reports to the Head of Wines. As Senior Sommelier, you will be responsible for the following duties: Support the Head of Wines in leading the sommelier function during service, ensuring consistent service excellence, strong team performance, and exceptional guest satisfaction. Assist the Head of Wines with administrative duties. Drive kind and generous service by role-modelling respectful, professional behavior towards both guests and colleagues, while maintaining daily communication with F&B and Culinary colleagues. Demonstrate outstanding food and wine knowledge, confidently recommending and pairing wines, supporting wine list execution, and enhancing the overall dining experience. Mentor Sommeliers, assist with the wine training and development of the F&B Service and Bar colleagues and support ongoing learning initiatives. Support operational controls including beverage charging accuracy, stock management, cellar organization, and preparation for monthly stock takes, while ensuring compliance with Mandarin Oriental standards and budgets. Attend required meetings and report maintenance issues. As Senior Sommelier, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Sommelier certification is mandatory. Experience in a similar role. Fluency in English. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(660144, 'ΥΠΑΛΛΗΛΟΣ ΓΡΑΦΕΙΟΥ ΕΜΠΟΡΙΚΟΥ ΤΜΗΜΑΤΟΣ', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/retail-jobs/309120', 'Καλλιθέα', 'πριν μία ώρα', '2026-04-27 15:00:43', 'ΟΙΚΙΑΚΟΣ ΕΞΟΠΛΙΣΜΟΣ ΑΕΒΕ', 'Η «Παρουσίαση», η μεγαλύτερη αλυσίδα καταστημάτων ειδών σπιτιού και επαγγελματικού εξοπλισμού στην Ελλάδα, με πολυετή παρουσία στον χώρο αναζητά Υπάλληλο Γραφείου για το Εμπορικό Τμήμα, στα κεντρικά γραφεία μας στην Καλλιθέα. Η εταιρεία συνεργάζεται με κορυφαίους διεθνείς οίκους έχοντας την αποκλειστική εκπροσώπησή τους στην ελληνική αγορά.   Το εμπορικό μας τμήμα αναζητά νέους συνεργάτες με οργανωτικές δεξιότητες, διάθεση για μάθηση και ενδιαφέρον για τον κλάδο του οικιακού εξοπλισμού, που θα υποστηρίξουν αποτελεσματικά τις καθημερινές λειτουργίες του τμήματος. Καθήκοντα Θέσης Διαχείριση δελτίων αποστολών Καταχώριση δελτίων επιστροφών - πιστωτικά Τηλεφωνική εξυπηρέτηση πελατών Δημιουργία και συντονισμός παραγγελιών προς εκτέλεση Έλεγχος αρχείων παραγγελιών Καταχώριση παραγγελιών Καταχώριση και παρακολούθηση στοιχείων στο εμπορικό σύστημα Οργάνωση αρχείων και διοικητική υποστήριξη   Απαραίτητα Προσόντα Επικοινωνιακές και οργανωτικές δεξιότητες• Συνεργατικότητα και ομαδικό πνεύμα• Ευχάριστη και επαγγελματική προσωπικότητα• Επιθυμητή γνώση Αγγλικής γλώσσας (γραπτός & προφορικός λόγος)• Καλή γνώση MS Office• Εμπειρία σε ERP σύστημα (ειδικότερα EnterSoft) θα θεωρηθεί επιπλέον προσόν• Επιθυμητή εμπειρία 2 – 4 ετών σε αντίστοιχη θέση   Παροχές Σύμβαση αορίστου χρόνου• Σύγχρονο και υποστηρικτικό εργασιακό περιβάλλον• Προοπτικές επαγγελματικής εξέλιξης εντός του Ομίλου• Εταιρική έκπτωση στα προϊόντα της αλυσίδας', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660145, 'Senior Waiter - Kookoonari Beach Bar Restaurant', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309133', 'Νέστωρ', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-27 15:00:43', 'ΟΜΙΛΟΣ ΕΣΤΙΑΣΗΣ', '  Responsibilities: Welcoming and serving guests with professionalism and courtesy Presenting the menu with knowledge and confidence Supervising assistants and collaborating with the front-of-house team Ensuring high standards of hospitality and guest experience Required Qualifications: Previous experience in the food & beverage sector Strong communication skills and team spirit Excellent command of Greek and English Benefits: Competitive salary package Work in a high-aesthetic beachfront environment Accommodation and meals provided Opportunity for year-round employment and collaboration within the group’s restaurants in Athens CV Submission: [email protected]', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660146, 'Junior Sous Chef', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309137?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν 25 λεπτά', '2026-04-27 15:00:47', 'Mandarin Oriental Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Junior Sous Chef to join our Culinary team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Culinary Department in Pylos, Messenia, Greece, the Junior Sous Chef ensures the smooth running of culinary operations and the good working environment between colleagues. The Junior Sous Chef reports to the Sous Chef.  As Junior Sous Chef, you will be responsible for the following duties:  Check the quality of all food production in the kitchen, ensure all live products received are in top condition and are of top quality, oversee stock rotation (F.I.F.O.) and carry out the kitchen requisitioning and ordering. Check standard recipes ensuring proper portion control and uniformity of taste and quality. Oversee the overall food cost, as well as kitchen supplies, kitchen energy costs and kitchen utensils. Propose, and initiate when approved, new services and products for our guests. Motivate and lead by example. Ensure that all designated action points from daily briefings or other operational meetings are being followed by the individuals concerned. Complete additional tasks as assigned by management. As Junior Sous Chef, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. Globally recognized Culinary Qualification. 1-2 years of experience in a similar role. Good level in English.  Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(660147, 'Spa Therapist', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309138?origin=pjp', 'Πύλος', 'πριν 12 λεπτά', '2026-04-27 15:00:47', 'Mandarin Oriental Costa Navarino', 'Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is looking for a Spa Therapist to join our Spa & Wellness team, for season 2026. Are you a master of craft? Do you thrive in a team that succeeds together, demonstrating integrity and respect while acting responsibly? Do you embrace a growth mindset? We invite you to become a fan of the exceptional.  Mandarin Oriental is the award-winning owner and operator of some of the most luxurious hotels, resorts and residences located in prime destinations around the world, with a strong development pipeline. Increasingly recognised for creating some of the world’s most sought-after properties, the Group provides legendary service inspired by Asian heritage whilst representing the very cutting-edge of luxury experiences. Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino is located on the southwest coast of the Peloponnese, one of the most unspoiled and breath-taking landscapes in the Mediterranean, and 45 minutes’ drive from Kalamata International Airport. The beachfront resort comprises of 99 suites and villas, all with outdoor terraces and sea views, along with seven restaurants and bars. About the job Based at the Mandarin Oriental, Costa Navarino within the Spa & Wellness Department in Pylos, the Spa Therapist is responsible for enlightening the guests on various body treatments, massage techniques, and spa services and for customising the massage treatments as per the guest’s requirements. The Spa Therapist reports to the Head Therapist. As Spa Therapist, you will be responsible for the following duties: Deliver spa treatments while ensuring guest comfort and satisfaction. Maintain cleanliness, organisation, and high service standards in the spa in line with Mandarin Oriental procedures. Attend meetings and trainings to maintain professional standards. Recommend and upsell spa products and services to enhance guest experience. Report equipment issues and ensure inventory is well-stocked. Assist in various spa operations, including front desk, retail, and relaxation areas. As Spa Therapist, we expect from you:  Valid EU Passport or Hellenic Residence Permit. License in Physiotherapy or related field is mandatory. Good level in English. Working experience as a licensed spa therapist. Working knowledge of skin care therapies, beauty products and trends will be considered as a plus. Our commitment to you Learning & Development. Your success is our success. We craft unique learning and development programmes for various stages in your career so that you grow, continuously. MOstay. When you work as hard as our colleagues do, it’s important to take time off. As a member of the #MOfamily, you can stay with us wherever you go in the world. The MOstay programme offers complimentary nights and additionally attractive rates on rooms for you and your loved ones. Heath & Colleague Wellness. Finding the right work-life balance is important. Your wellbeing matters to us. A variety of health benefits and wellness programmes are offered to all our colleagues, globally. Task force opportunities across the Group of Mandarin Oriental. Depending on your role, you may have the opportunities to be selected as a Cultural Exchange Ambassador. CEAs help to spread our unique Oriental heritage and act as role models, demonstrating how Colleagues will work together to deliver on our vision, mission and philosophies. Accommodation and laundry of linen. Three complimentary meals per day at our Colleague restaurant. Uniform and laundry of uniform. Private Medical Insurance. We’re Fans. Are you?', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
