(660902, 'Credit Controller', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/accounting-or-auditing-jobs/309491', 'Γλυφάδα', 'πριν 2 λεπτά', '2026-04-28 15:02:33', 'Antaeus Travel Group', 'Areas of Responsibility 1.Collections & Debt Monitoring Active Debt Recovery: Perform both reactive and proactive debt chasing, ensuring that customers\' debts are collected in line with contracted payment terms. Balance Oversight: Monitor customer account receivable balances and ageing reports to identify overdue invoices and potential payment issues. Persistent Communication: Follow up with customers via phone, email, and written correspondence; maintain professional and courteous communication while remaining firm in pursuing collections until final settlement. Account Reconciliation: Regularly reconcile customer accounts and handle any discrepancies or disputed invoices in collaboration with the accounting team. Record Keeping: Maintain accurate and detailed records of all collection activities and customer interactions.   2.Credit Assessment & Risk Management Risk Evaluation: Conduct credit assessments of new and existing customers to determine appropriate credit limits based on financial data and history. Policy Enforcement: Build and maintain positive relationships with customers and partners while ensuring strict adherence to company credit terms and policies. Inquiry Management: Address customer/partner inquiries and concerns regarding credit and payments promptly and professionally.   3.Reporting & Budgeting Financial Analysis: Provide weekly/monthly reports of expected collections and analyze data and KPIs relevant to the role. Cash Flow Forecasting: Forecast inbound cash receipts and update cash flow forecasts to ensure alignment with approved budgets.   Required Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Experience: 2-3+ years in a similar Credit Control or Collections role (Travel sector experience will be considered a plus). Education: Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, or Business Administration, or a related field. Languages: Fluency in English (written and verbal) is mandatory. Software: Proficiency in MS Excel (Advanced); experience with Power BI is a benefit. ERP: Mandatory experience with ERP systems (Microsoft Dynamics, S1 ERP or similar). Negotiation: Strong communication and negotiation skills with a firm but professional approach. Analysis: Excellent analytical skills and high level of accuracy/attention to detail. Methodology: Methodical approach to problem-solving and ability to manage multiple priorities.   Benefits 💼 A competitive compensation package and bonus scheme 🌱 Personal development opportunities 🌟 Excellent working environment 🚌 Private transportation from/to Elliniko metro station 🍽️ Monthly allowance for lunch expenses 🏥 Private Health Insurance plan', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660903, 'Waiter/tress | Mystique, a Luxury Collection Hotel (Season 2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309527?origin=pjp', 'Θήρα', 'πριν 7 λεπτά', '2026-04-28 15:02:33', 'Empiria Group', 'Waiter/ Waitress About usEmpiria Group owns, manages, and operates a distinctive collection of luxury hotels and villas, members of The Luxury Collection and Design Hotels™ by Marriott International, located in some of Greece’s most iconic destinations: Santorini, Paros, and the Peloponnese.With more than 30 years of expertise and a team of over 400 associates, Empiria Group is driven by a shared purpose: to create space for joy through elevated hospitality experiences. Our culture is shaped by four core values — finding joy, always elevating, exuding passion, and leading with purpose — guiding everything we do.At Empiria Group, hospitality is more than a profession. It is a craft, a mindset, and a journey of continuous growth. Role OverviewThe Waiter delivers exceptional, personalized service to guests, ensuring a warm, professional, and memorable dining experience. The role requires attentive service, detailed product knowledge, and seamless collaboration with the F&B team. The Waiter anticipates guest needs and contributes to a refined dining atmosphere, upholding the highest standards of service excellence. Key AccountabilitiesPresent and describe food and beverage menu items to guests in an engaging and knowledgeable manner.Greet guests warmly, seat them promptly, and ensure consistent, attentive service throughout the dining experience.Oversee table setup, maintain cleanliness and organization of dining areas, and uphold high service standards.Take and serve food and beverage orders accurately and in a timely manner.Coordinate with kitchen and bar teams to ensure accurate and prompt delivery of all orders.Handle guest inquiries, special requests, and complaints efficiently and professionally, ensuring swift resolution.Monitor inventory of dining supplies and beverages, maintain stock levels, and contribute to minimizing waste.Promote and upsell food, beverages, and specialty drinks to enhance guest satisfaction and increase revenue.Ensure compliance with all health, safety, and hygiene procedures, maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment.Assist with service across other hotel outlets, events, and in-room dining operations as required.RequirementsMinimum of 2 years of experience in a similar role within five-star hotels or high-volume fine dining venues.Degree or diploma in Tourism, Hospitality, or a related field.Knowledge of wines; experience in wine tasting is considered an advantage.Experience using MICROS or other POS systems is an advantage.Excellent command of English; additional languages are considered an asset. Candidate’s ProfileFlexibility and adaptability to respond effectively to a variety of work situations.Genuine passion for delivering consistently high levels of guest service.Strong negotiation, communication and interpersonal skills.Pleasant, professional, and guest-oriented personality with a positive attitude.BenefitsAt Empiria Group, our hotels are more than workplaces — they are environments where people grow, evolve, and find purpose.Staff accommodation with Wi-Fi and air conditioning.Half-board meal plan (Breakfast & Lunch).Continuous training and development opportunities.Career growth opportunities within Empiria Group and across Marriott International properties worldwide. At Empiria Group we are proud to foster Equal Employment Opportunities regardless of race, color, ethnicity, religion, gender, age, disability, or sexual orientation. All applications are considered strictly confidential. After careful consideration of all the resumes received, we will only contact the candidates who meet the requirements of the job to arrange an interview. ​You provide the Talent!We provide the Space for Opportunity and Growth!', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660904, 'Waiter/Waitress_Sifnos', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309524', 'Σίφνος', 'πριν ένα λεπτό', '2026-04-28 15:02:37', 'HotelBrain', 'Qualifications: 2-3 years’ minimum experience as a Captain or Waiter in a Luxury Boutique Hotel or a Restaurant Excellent command of both English and Greek language is essential Very good knowledge of a second foreign language will be considered as an asset Previous experience on POS & Micros systems is more than welcomed Self-motivated, enthusiastic, with natural ability and confidence to sell / promote Excellent Customer Service Skills Problem solving skills Well-groomed with strong interpersonal skills Responsibilities: Implementation on a daily basis of the operation procedures of the department Great attention to detail Offering upscaled customer service An attractive package of benefits is offered according to qualifications,  including staff accommodation and meals. Should you wish to be a member of HotelBrain team, please send us your CV with a photo. All applications will be treated in the strictest confidence.', 'Εποχιακός/ή'),
(660905, 'Sales Manager / Interior Designer - Luxury Furniture Showroom Chalandri', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/retail-jobs/309458', 'Χαλάνδρι', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-28 15:02:37', 'Μ & Π ΑΛΕΞΟΠΟΥΛΟΣ ΕΠΕ', 'O ρόλος αφορά ανάπτυξη πωλήσεων και συμβουλευτική διακόσμησης σε έργα κατοικιών και επιλεγμένων επαγγελματικών χώρων. Αναζητούμε άτομο με αισθητική αντίληψη, επαγγελματική παρουσία και ικανότητα διαχείρισης πελάτη υψηλών απαιτήσεων. Καθήκοντα Υποδοχή και εξυπηρέτηση πελατών στο showroom Κατανόηση αναγκών και πρόταση ολοκληρωμένων λύσεων επίπλωσης Δημιουργία layout προτάσεων, mood boards και παρουσιάσεων Παρουσίαση υλικών, υφασμάτων και φινιρισμάτων Συνεργασία με αρχιτέκτονες και interior designers Ανάπτυξη επαγγελματικών σχέσεων με μελετητικά γραφεία Απαραίτητα προσόντα Γνώση σχεδιαστικών προγραμμάτων (AutoCAD, SketchUp ή αντίστοιχο 3D) Πολύ καλή αισθητική και ενδιαφέρον για αρχιτεκτονική & design Πολύ καλή γνώση Αγγλικών (προφορικά & γραπτά) Άνεση στην επικοινωνία και επαγγελματική συμπεριφορά Οργάνωση και υπευθυνότητα στη διαχείριση project Θα εκτιμηθούν Εμπειρία σε showroom design, κουζίνας, επίπλου ή υλικών Επαφή με αρχιτεκτονικά γραφεία Παροχές Ανταγωνιστικός σταθερός μισθός Ποσοστά επί των πωλήσεων Εκπαίδευση στα προϊόντα και τα υλικά Επαφή με έργα κατοικιών υψηλών προδιαγραφών Προοπτική εξέλιξης ', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660906, 'Τεχνικοί Καταστημάτων - Βόρεια & Νότια Προάστια', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/sales-or-business-development-or-account-management-jobs/309525?origin=pjp', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-28 15:02:39', 'Plaisio Computers S.A.', 'Έχεις περιέργεια να μάθεις περισσότερα για το Life At Plaisio των συνεργατών μας στα καταστήματα?Κάνε join στη μεγάλη ομάδα του Πλαισίου 🔴, ως Τεχνικός τα καταστήματα των Νοτίων Προαστίων (Γλυφάδα, Άλιμος, Καλλιθέα, Δάφνη, Πειραιά) είτε στα καταστήματα των Βορείων Προαστίων (Αγία Παρασκευή, Μεταμόρφωση, Μαρούσι, Κηφισιά, Ψυχικό).🎉Τι θα κάνεις ως Stores Technician στο τμήμα συναρμολόγησης και service:✅Θα ανήκεις στην τεχνική μας ομάδα συναρμολόγησης, με βασικό task την ενασχόληση με το hardware τόσο σε επίπεδο build όσο και σε repair/service✅Θα έχεις τη δυνατότητα να κάνεις επισκευές και troubleshooting σε μεγάλο φάσμα της προϊοντικής μας γκάμας (desktops, laptops, κινητά, ψηφιακά μέσα κλπ.)Τι θα ήταν καλό να έχεις: 💻Οποιαδήποτε εμπειρία σε τεχνικό κομμάτι, την οποία μπορείς να φέρεις μαζί σου. Διαφορετικά, μην ανησυχείς, είμαστε ειδικοί στην εκπαίδευση⚡Πάθος για την επίλυση τεχνικών ζητημάτων🖥️Ενασχόληση με hardware είναι must (επιθυμητή είναι η εξοικείωση με repair PC & laptops)Τι Extra Προσφέρουμε:🔴 Ιδιωτική ασφάλεια Υγείας!🔴 Εκπτώσεις και προσφορές στα αγαπημένα σου tech gadgets, και όχι μόνο🔴 Bonus επίτευξης στόχου🔴Συνεχής εκπαίδευση σε νέες τεχνολογίες🔴Εκδηλώσεις και δράσεις εσωτερικά της εταιρείαςΕάν ταυτίστηκες ... ΤΟΤΕ:1. Στείλε μας το βιογραφικό σου2. Stay tuned για την επικοινωνία μαςΓιατί... #esenatheloume!', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660907, 'Barista / Bartender I Mystique, a Luxury Collection Hotel (Season 2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309526?origin=pjp', 'Θήρα', 'πριν 4 λεπτά', '2026-04-28 15:02:39', 'Empiria Group', 'Barista/ BartenderAbout usEmpiria Group owns, manages, and operates a distinctive collection of luxury hotels and villas, members of The Luxury Collection and Design Hotels™ by Marriott International, located in some of Greece’s most iconic destinations: Santorini, Paros, and the Peloponnese.With more than 30 years of expertise and a team of over 400 associates, Empiria Group is driven by a shared purpose: to create space for joy through elevated hospitality experiences. Our culture is shaped by four core values — finding joy, always elevating, exuding passion, and leading with purpose — guiding everything we do.At Empiria Group, hospitality is more than a profession. It is a craft, a mindset, and a journey of continuous growth. Role OverviewThe Barista / Bartender is responsible for preparing and serving high-quality coffee and beverage selections while delivering warm, professional, and personalized service. The role ensures that the bar and café areas are maintained to the highest standards of cleanliness and organization, manages POS transactions accurately, supports seamless service in collaboration with the wider hotel team, and actively promotes signature offerings, while fully complying with all health, safety, and hygiene standards. Key AccountabilitiesPrepare and serve a wide range of high-quality coffee, espresso beverages, cocktails, and other drink selections, ensuring consistency, accuracy, and exceptional presentation.Welcome guests warmly and engage with them professionally to understand preferences and provide personalized beverage recommendations.Present and describe beverage offerings and menu items in an engaging, knowledgeable, and confident manner.Maintain impeccable standards of cleanliness and organization in all bar and café areas, including equipment, glassware, tools, and workstations.Handle cash transactions and process payments accurately through the hotel’s point-of-sale (POS) system.Monitor, restock, and manage bar and café inventory, ensuring adequate supply levels and proper storage at all times.Collaborate closely with the wider hotel team to ensure smooth service flow and timely beverage delivery, particularly during peak service periods.Ensure full compliance with all health, safety, hygiene, and sanitation standards, maintaining a safe and professional working environment.Assist with the setup, preparation, and breakdown of bar and café areas at the beginning and end of each shift.Actively promote the hotel’s beverage offerings, including seasonal specials, signature drinks, and new menu items, enhancing the overall guest experience.Respond promptly and professionally to guest requests, including customized or special-order beverages, ensuring high levels of guest satisfaction.RequirementsMinimum of two years of experience as a Barista or Bartender in a 5-star hotel or luxury hospitality environment.Strong knowledge of coffee preparation and cocktail service; relevant certifications will be considered an advantage.Degree or diploma in Hospitality, Tourism, or a related field will be considered an asset.Excellent command of the English language; knowledge of additional languages will be considered an asset.Experience with MICROS or other POS systems is preferred. Candidate’s ProfileGenuine passion for delivering consistently exceptional guest service.Pleasant, professional, and customer-oriented personality with strong communication and interpersonal skills.Flexibility and adaptability to effectively respond to a variety of work situations. BenefitsAt Empiria Group, our hotels are more than workplaces — they are environments where people grow, evolve, and find purpose.Staff accommodation with Wi-Fi and air conditioning.Half-board meal plan (Breakfast & Lunch).Continuous training and development opportunities.Career growth opportunities within Empiria Group and across Marriott International properties worldwide. At Empiria Group we are proud to foster Equal Employment Opportunities regardless of race, color, ethnicity, religion, gender, age, disability, or sexual orientation. All applications are considered strictly confidential. After careful consideration of all the resumes received, we will only contact the candidates who meet the requirements of the job to arrange an interview. ​You provide the Talent!We provide the Space for Opportunity and Growth!', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660908, 'Assistant Waiter/tress | Mystique, a Luxury Collection Hotel (Season 2026)', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/tourism-jobs/309523?origin=pjp', 'Θήρα', 'πριν 8 λεπτά', '2026-04-28 15:02:41', 'Empiria Group', 'Assistant Waiter/ WaitressAbout usEmpiria Group owns, manages, and operates a distinctive collection of luxury hotels and villas, members of The Luxury Collection and Design Hotels™ by Marriott International, located in some of Greece’s most iconic destinations: Santorini, Paros, and the Peloponnese.With more than 30 years of expertise and a team of over 400 associates, Empiria Group is driven by a shared purpose: to create space for joy through elevated hospitality experiences. Our culture is shaped by four core values — finding joy, always elevating, exuding passion, and leading with purpose — guiding everything we do.At Empiria Group, hospitality is more than a profession. It is a craft, a mindset, and a journey of continuous growth. Role OverviewThe Assistant Waiter supports the service team in delivering a seamless, elegant, and personalized dining experience. The role involves ensuring impeccable table setup, maintaining well-prepared service areas, and responding promptly to guest needs, consistently contributing to the exceptional standards of service expected in a luxury hospitality environment. Key AccountabilitiesAssist in presenting and describing menu items, including food and beverages, in a professional and engaging manner.Τake and serve food and beverage orders accurately and in a timely manner.Deliver attentive, courteous, and personalized service throughout the guests’ dining experience.Set, clear, and reset tables in accordance with established restaurant and service standards.Monitor guest satisfaction and address requests or concerns promptly, professionally, and discreetly.Maintain high standards of cleanliness and organization in dining areas and service stations at all times.Assist with restocking service supplies, including napkins, cutlery, glassware, and condiments.Support the front-of-house team to ensure smooth, efficient, and well-coordinated service operations.Collaborate closely with kitchen and bar teams to ensure timely and accurate order delivery.Comply with all health, safety, hygiene, and sanitation regulations to ensure a safe and welcoming dining environment. RequirementsMinimum of one (1) year of experience in a similar role within a 5-star hotel or high-end restaurant environment.Degree or diploma in Hospitality, Tourism, or a related field will be considered an asset.Familiarity with MICROS or other POS systems is considered an advantage.Excellent command of the English language; knowledge of additional languages will be considered an asset. Candidate’s ProfileFlexibility and adaptability to respond effectively to a variety of work situations.Genuine passion for delivering consistently high levels of guest service.Strong communication and interpersonal skills.Pleasant, professional, and guest-oriented personality with a positive attitude. BenefitsAt Empiria Group, our hotels are more than workplaces — they are environments where people grow, evolve, and find purpose.Staff accommodation with Wi-Fi and air conditioning.Half-board meal plan (Breakfast & Lunch).Continuous training and development opportunities.Career growth opportunities within Empiria Group and across Marriott International properties worldwide. At Empiria Group we are proud to foster Equal Employment Opportunities regardless of race, color, ethnicity, religion, gender, age, disability, or sexual orientation. All applications are considered strictly confidential. After careful consideration of all the resumes received, we will only contact the candidates who meet the requirements of the job to arrange an interview. ​You provide the Talent!We provide the Space for Opportunity and Growth!', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση'),
(660909, 'Chair, Supervisory Board', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/other-jobs/309519', 'Αθήνα', 'πριν 3 ώρες', '2026-04-28 15:02:41', '', 'About EIT Water EIT Water is Europe\'s innovation community for water, marine and maritime systems. It connects industry, innovators, researchers, educators and policymakers to tackle the most urgent water challenges from scarcity, drought and flooding to pollution and ecosystem decline. EIT Water is part of the European Institute of Innovation and Technology (EIT), a body of the European Union. Founded in 2026, EIT Water has eight regional hubs across Europe and a mandate to deliver systemic innovation from source to sea. EIT Water is now establishing the governance structures that will guide its first Strategic Agenda and long-term impact. The Roles The Supervisory Board of EIT Water consists of nine members, five of whom, including the Chair will be appointed from non-member organisations. The Supervisory Board will oversee the strategic direction of EIT Water, approve Business Plans, and appoint the Chief Executive Officer alongside other leadership team members. As a founding board, its members will play an exceptional role in shaping EIT Water\'s direction from the outset. Chair (Independent) The Chair will lead the Supervisory Board and represent EIT Water at the highest levels of European stakeholder engagement. We are looking for an individual with demonstrated board leadership experience and a strong pan-European network, who is motivated to help build a new institution from its inception. Supervisory Board Members (8 seats; 4 member representatives & 4 independent) Board members contribute strategic oversight, sector expertise and governance experience. Together, the board must reflect the breadth of EIT Water\'s mission spanning water, marine and maritime innovation and meet EIT\'s requirements for gender balance, geographic diversity across Europe, and Knowledge Triangle representation across industry, research and society. Ideal candidates brings: A proven track record of seniority within their field, with prior experience as a non-executive or supervisory board member An active European network across industry, research, policy or finance relevant to water, marine or maritime systems A genuine commitment to EIT Water\'s mission and the ambition to help build a pan-European institution from the ground up The availability to meet the time commitment this role requires approximately 10–12 days per year, with a greater commitment expected during the founding year How to Apply Applications should be submitted via https://perrettlaver.com/eit-water-chair-supervisory-board-members-recruitment/ by 21st May 2026 and should include a current CV and a cover letter setting out your interest and relevant experience. Please indicate whether you are applying as an independent member or as a representative of a member organisation already aligned to EIT Water, or if your organisation intends to become a Strategic or a Cooperation Member of EIT Water. The appointment process is led by Perrett Laver on behalf of EIT Water. For questions about the process, please contact Feride Yetis [email protected]. EIT Water is part of the European Institute of Innovation and Technology (EIT), a body of the European Union. This activity is co-funded by the European Union. EIT Water is committed to equal opportunities and welcomes applications without discrimination on any grounds. EIT Water is an established Danish Association.', 'Εθελοντισμός'),
(660910, 'Μηχανικός Χρονικού Προγραμματισμού-Project Planner', 'https://www.kariera.gr/jobs/engineering-jobs/309521?origin=pjp', 'Ηράκλειο', 'πριν 2 ώρες', '2026-04-28 15:02:43', 'GEK TERNA GROUP', 'Η ΤΕΡΝΑ Α.Ε. εταιρεία του Ομίλου ΓΕΚ ΤΕΡΝΑ, αναζητά:Μηχανικό Χρονικού Προγραμματισμού-Project Planner για το έργο του Βόρειου Οδικού Άξονα ΚρήτηςΑρμοδιότητες:Καταρτίζει αναλυτικό πρόγραμμα εργασιών, σύμφωνα με τον σχεδιασμό κατασκευής του ΈργουΔιαμορφώνει, επεξεργάζεται και διαχειρίζεται το χρονοδιάγραμμα του έργου, διασφαλίζοντας την εμπρόθεσμη εκτέλεση των εργασιών σε όλες τις φάσεις υλοποίησής του Ελέγχει την πρόοδο του έργου και τη συνεχή συμμόρφωση της κατασκευής με τον σχεδιασμόΕνημερώνει το ημερολόγιο του έργου, διαχειρίζεται τις εκάστοτε αλλαγές και επικαιροποιεί το αντίστοιχο αρχείοΠροετοιμάζει και υποβάλει τις μηνιαίες αναφορές προόδου, καθώς και σχετικές εισηγήσεις για την αποφυγή αποκλίσεων από το χρονοδιάγραμμα του έργουΑναπτύσσει & διατηρεί πλαίσιο αποτελεσματικής συνεργασίας και επικοινωνίας μεταξύ όλων των ομάδων εργασίας και των εμπλεκόμενων μερών στο έργοΑπαιτούμενα Προσόντα:Πτυχίο ΑΕΙ  Πολιτικού/Ηλεκτρολόγου/Μηχανολόγου Μηχανικού10 με 15 έτη εμπειρίας σε διαχείριση χρονοδιαγράμματος κατασκευής έργων οδοποιίαςΠολύ καλή γνώση λογισμικού MS Project ή/και Primavera Πολύ καλή γνώση χειρισμού εφαρμογών MS Office Πολύ καλή γνώση της Αγγλικής γλώσσας (προφορικά & γραπτά)Δεξιότητες:Ικανότητα σχεδιασμού και τήρησης χρονοδιαγραμμάτωνΑνεπτυγμένες επικοινωνιακές δεξιότητεςΔεξιότητες άμεσης αντίδρασης και επίλυσης καθημερινών θεμάτωνΠαροχές Εταιρείας:Προοπτικές εξέλιξης και ανάπτυξης σε έναν ισχυρό Όμιλο εταιρειώνΣυμμετοχή σε Ομιλικό Πρόγραμμα Ιδιωτικής Ασφάλειας Υγείας & Ζωής', 'Πλήρης απασχόληση');
